l":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/c3fc1e4f9ffb928da2d1e69eb99f3f3ab610e31b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T08:30:30Z","email":"boostera385@gmail.com","name":"M.Kashif"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T08:30:30Z","email":"boostera385@gmail.com","name":"M.Kashif"},"message":"Count lead coverage by distance, not state substring\n\nThe first coverage implementation matched the lead''s state code as a\nsubstring of the technician Area text. Areas store full state names, so\n\"CA\" inside \"California\" matched every technician in the state: live\nleads read \"403 technicians near a house in Los Angeles\" while real\nmetros like Buford, GA and Oceanside, CA read zero and were labelled Bad\nCoverage.\n\nPlacement now goes through us_places (31,839 Census places already in the\ndatabase). The lead and each technician are placed on it and counted\nwithin 40 miles, the same rule the Map View coverage circles use. A lead\nthat cannot be placed shows no badge rather than a false zero, and a\ntechnician whose Area is blank, a whole state, or shorthand like \"DFW\"\ncounts for nobody.\n\nparse_lead_location gains a repaired city and state extraction. It\nrequired a comma before the state and rejected any candidate containing a\ndigit, so most real addresses produced NULL; and its state pattern had no\nword boundary, so \"California 94063\" matched \"ia\" and put a Redwood City\nlead in Iowa. Both now port the already-tested address-utils logic. Area\nrollups stop losing rows to a NULL city as a side effect.\n\nAdds 90_lead_coverage_us_places.sql, which executes the count and asserts\nthe state-substring regression specifically.","tree":{"sha":"51163557cc2c4ea88a46103b120bb4efedb55e08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/git/trees/51163557cc2c4ea88a46103b120bb4efedb55e08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/git/commits/c3fc1e4f9ffb928da2d1e69eb99f3f3ab610e31b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/291759050?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boostera385-afk","id":291759050,"login":"boostera385-afk","node_id":"U_kgDOEWPjyg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/c3fc1e4f9ffb928da2d1e69eb99f3f3ab610e31b","node_id":"C_kwDORlXpldoAKGMzZmMxZTRmOWZmYjkyOGRhMmQxZTY5ZWI5OWYzZjNhYjYxMGUzMWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/326c065bf6ce93ecf26d9001158906bd34ecc36c","sha":"326c065bf6ce93ecf26d9001158906bd34ecc36c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/326c065bf6ce93ecf26d9001158906bd34ecc36c"}],"sha":"c3fc1e4f9ffb928da2d1e69eb99f3f3