comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T11:39:06Z","email":"boostera385@gmail.com","name":"m.kashif"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T11:39:06Z","email":"boostera385@gmail.com","name":"m.kashif"},"message":"Fix mark-urgent doing nothing for admin and cs_admin, and stop queueing CS\n\nReported as: admin marks a lead urgent, past conversations exist in the chat, and\nnothing matches and no suggestions appear.\n\nTHE SILENT NO-OP\n\napprove_urgent_verification opened with\n\n  IF v_role <> ''customer_service'' THEN\n    -- Anyone who can already bypass the gate does not need a verification.\n    RETURN;\n  END IF;\n\nwhich was correct when the dialog was shown to customer_service only. Once the\ndialog was extended to admin and cs_admin, they called the same function, and it\nreturned immediately and wrote nothing.\n\nThe failure was silent and compound. The dialog reported success, onProceed() set\nthe status in local form state, and invalidateQueries refetched the lead. The\nrefetch returned the unchanged row, and\n\n  useEffect(() => { if (lead) setForm(lead) }, [lead]);\n\nwrote over the form. The status snapped back to what it had been. An admin saw a\nsuccess toast and no change, with nothing in the console. customer_service was\nunaffected because their path did write, which is why it survived being exercised\nonly on that role.\n\nAuthorises on access now, matching approve_urgent_acknowledgement, which was\nwritten later and already did this correctly. Two functions doing the same job\nshould not disagree about who they accept.\n\nTHE MATCHING WAS NEVER THE PROBLEM\n\nMeasured before touching anything: 132 of 133 urgent leads have a conversation\nwhose number matches their phone, and all 132 also match on the last seven\ndigits. One does not match. So the lookup was working and the message being shown\nwas not about the lookup at all.\n\nWhat it probably was: the OpenAI call failing. That was undiagnosable, because\nevery failure produced the same generic notice as a genuinely absent\nconversation. Two changes:\n\nThe function now maps the OpenAI status to a reason, ai_unauthorised,\nai_out_of_quota, ai_bad_request or ai_unavailable. Out of quota is the likely one\non a key created without billing attached.\n\nAnd the frontend now actually reads it. supabase-js does not put the function''s\nbody in error.message, it puts the Response in error.context and leaves the\nmessage as ''returned a non-2xx status code''. Reading only the message discarded\neverything the function said, which is why the two causes looked identical.\nCovered by two tests, one for a JSON body and one for a body that is not JSON.\n\nNOBODY IS QUEUED ANY MORE\n\ncustomer_service is no longer routed to a CS Admin. The check advises and the\nperson making the call decides, for every role that sees it. A queue carrying a\nlarge share of urgent work stops being read within a week, and a review step that\ngets rubber-stamped is worse than none because it still looks like a control.\n\nWhat still holds is the trigger. A raw write carrying no verification is refused,\nso the check cannot be skipped from the API or the extension. The dialog is how\nyou satisfy it; it is not what makes it true.\n\nPROCESSOR IS NOT ASKED\n\nshowsUrgentCheck is separate from bypassesUrgentGate on purpose. The database\nexempts processor, admin and cs_admin; the front end asks customer_service, admin\nand cs_admin. Those lists disagree for processor on purpose, and a test asserts\nthey stay that way. Collapsing them would either start showing processor the\ndialog or stop processor setting urgent directly.\n\nAlso removed the now-dead review path from the dialog and the three props that\nonly fed it, and annotated runUrgentVerification''s return type. It had none, so\nTypeScript inferred a union of the two return shapes instead of enforcing the\ndeclared one, which is how a missing field on the success path passed typecheck.\n\nHarness check 21 calls the function as each role it accepts and asserts the lead\nis actually urgent afterwards, rather than merely that nothing raised.\n\n315 tests, tsc clean, lint clean, build clean, extension parses.","tree":{"sha":"8ac3a84880681e7a5c66b788022d28161f4927be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/git/trees/8ac3a84880681e7a5c66b788022d28161f4927be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/git/commits/2636f280348a7d0120f0cde9566d88239e9c5ffe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/291759050?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boostera385-afk","id":291759050,"login":"boostera385-afk","node_id":"U_kgDOEWPjyg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/2636f280348a7d0120f0cde9566d88239e9c5ffe","node_id":"C_kwDORlXpldoAKDI2MzZmMjgwMzQ4YTdkMDEyMGYwY2RlOTU2NmQ4ODIzOWU5YzVmZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/969d27950d70d95f06d87ebc9aa917d953000bee","sha":"969d27950d70d95f06d87ebc9aa917d953000bee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/969d27950d70d95f06d87ebc9aa917d953000bee"}],"sha":"2636f280348a7d0120f0cde9566d88239e9c5ffe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/2636f280348a7d0120f0cde9566d88239e9c5ffe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/291759050?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boostera385-afk","id":291759050,"login":"boostera385-afk","node_id":"U_kgDOEWPjyg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/60c51df54999b13f4529dfb81bf3ab44c4df394f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T11:12:07Z","email":"boostera385@gmail.com","name":"M.Kashif"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T11:12:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Merge pull request #76 from pastry-marketing/feat/urgent-ai-verification\n\nShow the conversation check to everyone, advisory for the senior roles","tree":{"sha":"43064e34047361a4bf2de5d5e7789256e48b44e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/git/trees/43064e34047361a4bf2de5d5e7789256e48b44e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/past