://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/60c51df54999b13f4529dfb81bf3ab44c4df394f","node_id":"C_kwDORlXpldoAKDYwYzUxZGY1NDk5OWIxM2Y0NTI5ZGZiODFiZjNhYjQ0YzRkZjM5NGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/d8321d4b340b694d7ba9d685fcd75e07fde6e406","sha":"d8321d4b340b694d7ba9d685fcd75e07fde6e406","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/d8321d4b340b694d7ba9d685fcd75e07fde6e406"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/969d27950d70d95f06d87ebc9aa917d953000bee","sha":"969d27950d70d95f06d87ebc9aa917d953000bee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/969d27950d70d95f06d87ebc9aa917d953000bee"}],"sha":"60c51df54999b13f4529dfb81bf3ab44c4df394f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/60c51df54999b13f4529dfb81bf3ab44c4df394f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/291759050?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boostera385-afk","id":291759050,"login":"boostera385-afk","node_id":"U_kgDOEWPjyg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/969d27950d70d95f06d87ebc9aa917d953000bee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T11:09:09Z","email":"boostera385@gmail.com","name":"m.kashif"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T11:09:09Z","email":"boostera385@gmail.com","name":"m.kashif"},"message":"Show the conversation check to everyone, advisory for the senior roles\n\nadmin, processor and cs_admin were setting urgent_job in one click with no\ncomparison against the conversation at all. Measured: 31 of 133 urgent leads,\n23%, were last edited by one of those roles. By name, ''CS admin'' had 28 edits\non urgent leads and Umair 39.\n\nThat was the wrong group to exempt. The check exists to catch someone working\nfrom a half-filled record and marking urgent on reflex, and that is a\nprocessor or admin behaviour rather than a new CS member''s. Exempting the\nexperienced roles protected nobody; it just left the busiest dispatchers\nunchecked.\n\nSo the dialog now opens for every role that can set urgent_job, and the mode\ndecides what it means:\n\n  customer_service              enforced   findings block, CS Admin signs off\n  admin / processor / cs_admin  advisory   findings shown, they decide\n\nTwo seconds of information for the person making the call, and they keep the\nauthority. Nothing can strand urgent work.\n\nWHAT DID NOT CHANGE, DELIBERATELY\n\nThe database still exempts those three roles. That is the point of the split. The\nfront end decides what someone is shown, enforce_urgent_gate decides what they\nare permitted to do. If the front end were the thing enforcing this it would\ndefeat with one request, and if the trigger started blocking admins then a\ndispatch workflow or a direct API call could jam on work that genuinely cannot\nwait. Both halves have to exist and they have to disagree about nothing.\n\nTHE OVERRIDE PATH MUST NOT LOG A CLEAN CHECK\n\napprove_urgent_verification falls back to ''All verification checks passed'' when\nit is given no summary. Proceeding over findings without a summary would have\nwritten a clean verdict into the activity log for a check that found problems,\nwhich is the exact failure this whole workflow was built to avoid. The dialog now\npasses an explicit summary on both paths, and the override records what was\noverridden and why. Covered by a test.\n\nNew leads go through the same route for every role rather than only CS, so there\nis one path and one set of wording. The extension withholds urgent_job on insert\nfor everyone now and hands the mode back to the panel, since it already loads the\nprofile.\n\nSix new tests, including one asserting the mode helper agrees with\nbypassesUrgentGate for every role, and one for the enforced fallback on an\nunknown role, which is the safer of the two defaults.\n\n313 tests, tsc clean, lint clean on changed files, build clean.","tree":{"sha":"43064e34047361a4bf2de5d5e7789256e48b44e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/git/trees/43064e34047361a4bf2de5d5e7789256e48b44e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/git/commits/969d27950d70d95f06d87ebc9aa917d953000bee","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/291759050?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-a