ea7f65f18478fe0810c3c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/522cb19da877fb1ae4ea7f65f18478fe0810c3c0"}],"sha":"d8321d4b340b694d7ba9d685fcd75e07fde6e406","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/d8321d4b340b694d7ba9d685fcd75e07fde6e406"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/291759050?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boostera385-afk","id":291759050,"login":"boostera385-afk","node_id":"U_kgDOEWPjyg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/522cb19da877fb1ae4ea7f65f18478fe0810c3c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:28:38Z","email":"boostera385@gmail.com","name":"m.kashif"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:28:38Z","email":"boostera385@gmail.com","name":"m.kashif"},"message":"Stop the verification path orphaning a request in the review queue\n\nFound by reviewing the flow rather than by a failing test, which is the worst\nway to find it and the reason it got written at all.\n\nThe sequence:\n\n  A CS member marks a lead urgent. The check finds a genuine disagreement, so a\n  pending request is raised and the lead stays where it is. They fix the field\n  the AI flagged and re-check. It comes back clean, so approve_urgent_verification\n  sets the lead urgent.\n\nNothing touched the queue. The pending request is still there.\n\nA CS Admin then opens an entry for a lead that is already urgent. Approving is\nharmless, because review_urgent_request notices the lead is already urgent and\nskips the status write. Declining is not: the request is marked declined, the\nlead stays urgent, and the activity trail records a CS Admin declining an urgent\nrequest that is in fact urgent.\n\nThat is wrong in the record rather than in the data, which is the version that\nsurvives unnoticed until someone reads the trail and concludes the escalation was\nrefused when it was satisfied. The sidebar badge also counts the row, so a settled\nitem keeps looking like outstanding work.\n\nBoth apply paths now settle any pending request in the same transaction that marks\nthe lead urgent, so there is no window where the lead is urgent and a request is\nstill open. The request is closed as approved rather than deleted, because the\nrecord that a review was ever needed is worth keeping, and the note says it was\nsettled automatically. reviewed_by is left null: no human reviewed it, and\nattributing it to whoever applied the verification would put a false name against\na real decision.\n\nThe one-pending-per-lead index is what made this reachable. Re-running the check\nafter a fix updates the same row rather than adding another, so the stale entry is\nthe original one and carries the original findings, not the corrected state.\n\nHarness check 20 raises a real request, applies the verification path, and asserts\nnothing pending survives and that the row closed with no reviewer.\n\nAlso gave the client a fifteen second timeout. supabase.functions.invoke has none\nof its own, and the function''s eight second abort covers only the model call, not\nDNS, TLS or the hop to Supabase. Without it a stalled request leaves a CS member\nlooking at a spinner with no way out. The timeout lands in the same unavailable\nbranch as any other transport failure, since a check that did not complete is an\nunknown and not a pass.\n\n307 tests, tsc clean, build clean.","tree":{"sha":"fabca71b2aba0a91f32b137071cf6545e4ff5fa1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/git/trees/fabca71b2aba0a91f32b137071cf6545e4ff5fa1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/git/commits/522cb19da877fb1ae4ea7f65f18478fe0810c3c0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/291759050?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boostera385-afk","id":291759050,"login":"boostera385-afk","node_id":"U_kgDOEWPjyg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/522cb19da877fb1ae4ea7f65f18478fe0810c3c0","node_id":"C_kwDORlXpldoAKDUyMmNiMTlkYTg3N2ZiMWFlNGVhN2Y2NWYxODQ3OGZlMDgxMGMzYzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/6504fc914ec815a7160be740bad5a171