","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/10eea716329f4d22ef9003c460d723ad866e4ab2","node_id":"C_kwDORlXpldoAKDEwZWVhNzE2MzI5ZjRkMjJlZjkwMDNjNDYwZDcyM2FkODY2ZTRhYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/2efdcc860fabab89f29e83944cfe4f7ccf6ebc86","sha":"2efdcc860fabab89f29e83944cfe4f7ccf6ebc86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/2efdcc860fabab89f29e83944cfe4f7ccf6ebc86"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/6504fc914ec815a7160be740bad5a171a40a280e","sha":"6504fc914ec815a7160be740bad5a171a40a280e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/6504fc914ec815a7160be740bad5a171a40a280e"}],"sha":"10eea716329f4d22ef9003c460d723ad866e4ab2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/10eea716329f4d22ef9003c460d723ad866e4ab2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/291759050?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boostera385-afk","id":291759050,"login":"boostera385-afk","node_id":"U_kgDOEWPjyg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/6504fc914ec815a7160be740bad5a171a40a280e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:07:10Z","email":"boostera385@gmail.com","name":"m.kashif"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:07:10Z","email":"boostera385@gmail.com","name":"m.kashif"},"message":"Fix a BEGIN/EXCEPTION block closed with END IF\n\nCheck 11 could not parse. The block that raises its fixture request was closed\nwith END IF; where plpgsql requires END;, so the parser hit END IF with no open\nIF and stopped at line 673.\n\nNothing after that line had been parsed, which means the previous run''s 19 of 19\nwas only ever true up to the point of the error. The fix is one character, but\nthe lesson is that a passing total from a file that did not parse is not a\npassing total.\n\nAdded a nesting check rather than eyeballing it again. It models plpgsql\nproperly, including the part that made my first attempt useless: END \\$\\$ closes\nthe BEGIN/EXCEPTION block and the DO block together, so it decrements by two,\nnot one. My first version reported all nineteen blocks as unbalanced, which was\nthe checker being wrong rather than the file. Second version reports clean\nacross all nineteen.\n\nAlso dropped a declared-but-unused variable in check 10.","tree":{"sha":"0b43d0b215289fd37dd0c577a9a5bdf2484cea08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/git/trees/0b43d0b215289fd37dd0c577a9a5bdf2484cea08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/git/commits/6504fc914ec815a7160be740bad5a171a40a280e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason"