b64df7957a3ff912f6fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/291759050?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boostera385-afk","id":291759050,"login":"boostera385-afk","node_id":"U_kgDOEWPjyg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/a30b3689bb4adf1ec9a6679270dc929fdfd8cd39/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T06:37:47Z","email":"boostera385@gmail.com","name":"m.kashif"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T06:37:47Z","email":"boostera385@gmail.com","name":"m.kashif"},"message":"Carry is_good_tech through the technician search path\n\nReported as: an admin approves a Good Tech request and the star does not turn\ngold. It stayed grey whichever tab or role performed the change.\n\nThe database was correct throughout, confirmed before touching any code:\ntechnicians.updated_at advanced at the moment of the approval and the Good\nTech count had gone up. This was never a write that failed.\n\nThe search path lost the column. fetchTechniciansPage takes a different route\nwhenever a search term is active: it calls the search_technicians RPC, then\nfetches the columns the RPC does not return. is_good_tech was in neither:\n\n  pg_get_function_result(search_technicians) like ''%is_good_tech%''  -> false\n  supplementary select  ''id, code, opr_code, is_active, created_by, ...''\n                        -> no is_good_tech\n\nso every row arrived with it undefined, and the star rendered from a value\nthat was never there. The unfiltered path uses TECHNICIAN_SELECT, which has\nalways included the column, which is why this looked intermittent: it only\nhappened while a search was active.\n\nThree changes, since the column has to survive both halves of that path:\n\n  the supplementary select now asks for is_good_tech\n  the extra map carries it\n  the row assembly copies it onto the technician, defaulting to false\n\nThe default is false rather than undefined so a genuinely unflagged\ntechnician and a missing column cannot be confused for one another in a\nlater expression.\n\nThis also explains the \"already Good Tech\" rejection when clearing. A stale\nrow showed the star as unset, so clicking it asked to set Good Tech on a\ntechnician that already had it, and the database correctly refused a no-op.\nOne cause, three symptoms.\n\nTechnicians is now published to realtime and the page subscribes. Verified\nthat it was absent from supabase_realtime entirely, so an approval could\nnever reach an already-open Technicians page in another tab or session.\nInvalidating from the page that wrote only ever helped that page, and the\nperson who approves is rarely the person watching the list. The event is\nused purely as a refetch signal and nothing is read from the payload, so\nthe subscription grants no read access the table policies do not already\nallow.\n\nThe migration has to be applied before the subscription will deliver, which\nis why it is separate rather than assumed.\n\nVerified: tsc clean, 26 test files and 292 tests passing, production build\nclean. The three no-explicit-any errors in technicians.ts sit at lines 27,\n33 and 37, which this change does not touch.","tree":{"sha":"f674c8a4530027f550ddc22a3901344bf2b77fec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/git/trees/f674c8a4530027f550ddc22a3901344bf2b77fec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/git/commits/a30b3689bb4adf1ec9a6679270dc929fdfd8cd39","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/291759050?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boostera385-afk","id":291759050,"login":"boostera385-afk","node_id":"U_kgDOEWPjyg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/a30b3689bb4adf1ec9a6679270dc929fdfd8cd39","node_id":"C_kwDORlXpldoAKGEzMGIzNjg5YmI0YWRmMWVjOWE2Njc5MjcwZGM5MjlmZGZkOGNkMzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/fb8bf017ae8cebf2c97caf67880dc2cb8936d5a0","sha":"fb8bf017ae8cebf2c97caf67880dc2cb8936d5a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/fb8bf017ae8cebf2c97caf67880dc2cb8936d5a0"}],"sha":"a30b3689bb4adf1ec9a6679270dc929fdfd8cd39","url":"https://api.git