{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/fb8bf017ae8cebf2c97caf67880dc2cb8936d5a0","node_id":"C_kwDORlXpldoAKGZiOGJmMDE3YWU4Y2ViZjJjOTdjYWY2Nzg4MGRjMmNiODkzNmQ1YTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/9cb9fdc534034a77726f09c842673ff891770413","sha":"9cb9fdc534034a77726f09c842673ff891770413","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/9cb9fdc534034a77726f09c842673ff891770413"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/b117a4a8088372116004774908026f15c133bfe5","sha":"b117a4a8088372116004774908026f15c133bfe5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/b117a4a8088372116004774908026f15c133bfe5"}],"sha":"fb8bf017ae8cebf2c97caf67880dc2cb8936d5a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/fb8bf017ae8cebf2c97caf67880dc2cb8936d5a0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/291759050?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boostera385-afk","id":291759050,"login":"boostera385-afk","node_id":"U_kgDOEWPjyg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/b117a4a8088372116004774908026f15c133bfe5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T06:16:54Z","email":"boostera385@gmail.com","name":"m.kashif"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T06:16:54Z","email":"boostera385@gmail.com","name":"m.kashif"},"message":"Stop the edit dialog from writing Good Tech for a processor\n\nChecked the deactivate and Good Tech paths separately rather than assuming\nthe one I had tested covered both, and the edit dialog had a second Good\nTech control the approval work had missed.\n\nTechnicianDialog carries its own Good Tech star and always put\nis_good_tech in the save payload. For an admin that is unchanged and still\ncorrect. For a processor it was a bypass that did not exist as a bypass: the\ntrigger rejected the write, so the save failed with a raw database error and\nthe note or phone change went down with it.\n\nTwo fixes, because either alone leaves a problem:\n\nThe star is now disabled for non-admins with a title saying to request it\nfrom the Technicians list, which is where the request flow lives. Disabled\nrather than hidden so the flag is still visible, and a processor can see\nthat the state exists and who owns it.\n\nThe payload omits is_good_tech entirely for non-admins. Disabling the\nbutton is not enough on its own, because the payload would still carry the\nflag the dialog initialised at line 81, so an unrelated save would attempt\nthe write anyway.\n\nThat omission also closes a race. If an admin marks a technician Good Tech\nwhile a processor has the dialog open, the processor''s dialog still holds\nthe old value and saving would send it, which the trigger rejects. Now the\nkey is absent, so the column is left alone.\n\nChecked while investigating: is_good_tech is nullable but has no NULLs\ntoday, so the NULL-coerced-to-false hazard is latent rather than active.\nAnd is_active is never written by this dialog, so deactivate was never\naffected here; the deactivation path runs through ActiveFlagCell, which\nfollows the same request flow as Good Tech and is covered by the same\nchange types constraint.\n\nVerified: tsc clean, eslint clean, 26 test files and 292 tests passing,\nproduction build clean.","tree":{"sha":"65f89b39588c987c2a7a9e58ef4451c7dc5fbabe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/git/trees/65f89b39588c987c2a7a9e58ef4451c7dc5fbabe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/git/commits/b117a4a8088372116004774908026f15c133bfe5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/291759050?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boostera385-afk","id":291759050,"login":"boostera385-afk","node_id":"U_kgDOEWPjyg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/b117a4a8088372116004774908026f15c133bfe5","node_id":"C_kwDORlXpldoAKGIxMTdhNGE4MDg4MzcyMTE2MDA0Nzc0OTA4MDI2ZjE1YzEzM2JmZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/de628f8cc27c68e7bbf826fda8ddda9c36868103","sha":"de628f8cc27c68e7bbf826fda8ddda9c36868103","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/de628f8cc27c68e7bbf826fda8ddda9c36868103"}],"sha":"b117a4a8088372116004774908026f15c133bfe5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/b117a4a8088372116004774908026f15c133bfe5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/291759050?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boostera385-afk","id":291759050,"login":"boostera385-afk","node_id":"U_kgDOEWPjyg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/de628f8cc27c68e7bbf826fda8ddda9c36868103/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T06:10:36Z","email":"boostera385@gmail.com","name":"m.kashif"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T06:10:36Z","email":"boostera385@gmail.com","name":"m.kashif"},"message":"Refresh the technician list after an approval applies a flag\n\nReported as: a processor requests Good Tech, an admin approves it, and the\nstar on the Technicians page does not change.\n\nThe database was never wrong. Confirmed against the live table before\ntouching any code: technicians.updated_at had advanced at the moment of the\napproval, an update_technicians_updated_at trigger exists, and the Good Tech\ncount had gone up. review_technician_change had done its job.\n\nThe directory list is a paginated React query with a 30 second staleTime,\nand nothing invalidated it when a request was approved. So an admin who\napproves and navigates straight to Technicians is served the cached page and\nsees the old flag. The approval took effect and the page had not caught up,\nwhich reads exactly like a failed approval.\n\nThe same gap was in both new flag cells: an admin writing the flag directly\nalso left the list stale until the staleTime lapsed, so the star they had\njust filled stayed empty under the cursor.\n\nBoth now invalidate TECHNICIANS_ROOT_KEY after a write, and the approval\nalso invalidates the pending summary so the badge clears.\ninvalidateQueries prefix-matches, so the root key covers the paginated\nper-page queries underneath it.\n\nVerified: tsc clean, eslint clean, 26 test files and 292 tests passing,\nproduction build clean.","tree":{"sha":"ba24bc0446f03adc5de0bba0481f82014f0858f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/git/trees/ba24bc0446f03adc5de0bba0481f82014f0858f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/git/commits/de628f8cc27c68e7bbf826fda8ddda9c36868103","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/291759050?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boostera385-afk","id":291759050,"login":"boostera385-afk","node_id":"U_kgDOEWPjyg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/de628f8cc27c68e7bbf826fda8ddda9c36868103","node_id":"C_kwDORlXpldoAKGRlNjI4ZjhjYzI3YzY4ZTdiYmY4MjZmZGE4ZGRkYTljMzY4NjgxMDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commit/9cb9fdc534034a77726f09c842673ff891770413","sha":"9cb9fdc534034a77726f09c842673ff891770413","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/9cb9fdc534034a77726f09c842673ff891770413"}],"sha":"de628f8cc27c68e7bbf826fda8ddda9c36868103","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/de628f8cc27c68e7bbf826fda8ddda9c36868103"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/291759050?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boostera385-afk","id":291759050,"login":"boostera385-afk","node_id":"U_kgDOEWPjyg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boostera385-afk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pastry-marketing/Marshmallow/commits/9cb9fdc534034a77726f09c842673ff891770413/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T06:03:24Z","email":"boostera385@gmail.com","name":"m.kashif"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T06:03:24Z","email":"boostera385@gmail.com","name":"m.kashif"},"message":"Strip the default world grant the previous revoke failed to remove\n\n20261103050000 ran, reported success and changed nothing: the policies are\nstill TO public and the trigger function still carries anon=X.\n\nThe cause is the shape of the default grant. These functions were created\nwith proacl =X/postgres at the front, which is Postgres''s world grant. PUBLIC\nis an implicit group containing every role, so REVOKE FROM PUBLIC should\nremove it and on a normal database does. Here it did not, and rather than\nkeep guessing at ACL syntax across roles this removes each grant by ACL item\nposition instead of by grantee name, which is unambiguous however the entry\nwas represented.\n\nIt also explains why the migration reported success. Revoking from a group\nthe role is not actually a member of is a no-op rather than an error, so a\nmigration can apply cleanly and accomplish nothing. Only querying the\ncatalogue afterwards catches it, which is what found this.\n\nRESET ALL then an explicit grant is used instead of REVOKE, so the intent is\nreadable and cannot silently miss. The trigger still fires: resetting grants\non a function does not affect trigger execution by the table owner.\n\nPolicies are recreated TO authenticated with the expressions copied verbatim.\nanon holds no table grant, so this is defence in depth rather th