965fbfe966786c560a48ec0d952b3e6a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45405841?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/imran-siddique","id":45405841,"login":"imran-siddique","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NDA1ODQx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commits/f15b45510274e3a725abfa872e6301b6d22b504c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T19:22:42Z","email":"45405841+imran-siddique@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Imran Siddique"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T19:22:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Commit the lockfile and switch CI to npm ci with dependency caching (#9)\n\nNode is now installed on the authoring machine, so the suite runs locally in\nunder a second instead of costing a two-minute CI round trip to find out\nwhether it compiles. First local run: 100 passed, 5 skipped (the Redis suite,\ncorrectly skipped without REDIS_URL), tsc --build clean across five projects.\n\napp/package-lock.json is now committed, so:\n  - builds are reproducible rather than resolving fresh on every run\n  - CI uses npm ci instead of npm install\n  - setup-node dependency caching is re-enabled, which was disabled in the\n    earlier fix because the cache path pointed at a lockfile that did not exist\n\nOne thing worth recording for anyone else running this: npm 11 defers install\nscripts by default, and esbuild needs its postinstall to fetch the platform\nbinary or vitest cannot transform anything. `npm approve-scripts esbuild` once\nper machine. CI is unaffected because it runs an older npm.\n\nAlso adds a test:all script for the Redis integration suite.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"015ff0927c1f1ccebc5f38b787c7daeae4812566","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/git/trees/015ff0927c1f1ccebc5f38b787c7daeae4812566"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/git/commits/f15b45510274e3a725abfa872e6301b6d22b504c","verification":{"payload":"tree 015ff0927c1f1ccebc5f38b787c7daeae4812566\nparent 18b9a70363bf72688ebb8c9bbf42eec7abfc1c25\nauthor Imran Siddique <45405841+imran-siddique@users.noreply.github.com> 1785784962 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785784962 -0700\n\nCommit the lockfile and switch CI to npm ci with dependency caching (#9)\n\nNode is now installed on the authoring machine, so the suite runs locally in\nunder a second instead of costing a two-minute CI round trip to find out\nwhether it compiles. First local run: 100 passed, 5 skipped (the Redis suite,\ncorrectly skipped without REDIS_URL), tsc --build clean across five projects.\n\napp/package-lock.json is now committed, so:\n  - builds are reproducible rather than resolving fresh on every run\n  - CI uses npm ci instead of npm install\n  - setup-node dependency caching is re-enabled, which was disabled in the\n    earlier fix because the cache path pointed at a lockfile that did not exist\n\nOne thing worth recording for anyone else running this: npm 11 defers install\nscripts by default, and esbuild needs its postinstall to fetch the platform\nbinary or vitest cannot transform anything. `npm approve-scripts esbuild` once\nper machine. CI is unaffected because it runs an older npm.\n\nAlso adds a test:all script for the Redis integration suite.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcOqCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABOAQAI4ZQtrg8+syLAm+CUs0kk6B\nJ/4zsGnE6TbgiG4JGVb+dLfzqp8yzS2bm15ltP5s7sXt0DJ8nFKNcuGLxsOSGgOg\nbINpoenCMQ/9W3r3hAU0ZItFSxdAFZFJhSXE2afHWi7PUkMOpVoCerdW+3oHg4Nk\nFAZGsKLSNxpQHEc0NqBKmwq59DloXzG2uS+7bUNc/fxQ5KMbTqMQ9TWINBRqjt75\n5bhFBQseaWcSs4P8n/Xknr4mqWyXNBpgrmUw/7qaZx2l1v7luA2/mjFw0Bsnclsf\ngLPv2xmfoSheF6gCBP4TTRL2ZFKocHWl81PxWpsILxfdlN8keUkLUT0p7Bq8Nkdj\nAF3156uFgGj/KKoGkZyahMgVpI32/FzsI6ZITrvazu+PiyEJLgFjpc/6pO5h8NW/\ni+ELdkeUxE1cFHeif8BfH/zLe94XsozvU3sTQAg1ytmsXd1m27ml+FBurXFnBMPi\n+r93JHX9aJc5VWuv8Eb4LFRYIyw3yRdN9KTctOLD2Qa4ynY/CeTINHpstB329sIG\n9p86cBC6RkgXfmrECiZS5N3n5//SzMfHpki8l//ClqpWwyL9WqPyhVFwUcHc7NGd\nLh1JvbbgQllIqJgnj8pxZhf6HFpSElHr0ZHaMnfJnyOHed4v2EchWXrdDJAU9vNV\nrEltGZ+U76i2uSJr1B94\n=c74T\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-04T21:39:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commit/f15b45510274e3a725abfa872e6301b6d22b504c","node_id":"C_kwDORlo4M9oAKGYxNWI0NTUxMDI3NGUzYTcyNWFiZmE4NzJlNjMwMWI2ZDIyYjUwNGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commit/18b9a70363bf72688ebb8c9bbf42eec7abfc1c25","sha":"18b9a70363bf72688ebb8c9bbf42eec7abfc1c25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commits/18b9a70363bf72688ebb8c9bbf42eec7abfc1c25"}],"sha":"f15b45510274e3a725abfa872e6301b6d22b504c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commits/f15b45510274e3a725abfa872e6301b6d22b504c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45405841?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/imran-siddique","id":45405841,"login":"imran-siddique","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NDA1ODQx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commits/18b9a70363bf72688ebb8c9bbf42eec7abfc1c25/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T18:58:31Z","email":"45405841+imran-siddique@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Imran Siddique"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T18:58:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add the Chapter 5 micro-frontend shell (#8)\n\nThe back end is fine, which is the problem: 5.2MB gzipped, 2.8s of main-thread\nblocking, velocity down from daily to weekly, and 14 cross-team merge conflicts\na sprint. The constraint has moved from infrastructure to the organization.\n\nChapter 5 already had six extended notes explaining these ideas well. What the\ncode adds is enforcement, because each of these rules degrades quietly when it\nis only written down.\n\npackages/shell\n  - error-boundary.ts turns the Critical Path Doctrine into a CI check. Its\n    wording is that the page must survive EVERY enhancement failing at once,\n    not one, so the check replaces every enhancement''s render with a throw and\n    asserts the critical path still rendered. There is a test proving the check\n    itself fails when checkout is wired to a recommendations widget, which is\n    the realistic regression: harmless in review, invisible until the widget is\n    down. Registering an enhancement without a fallback is refused.\n  - event-bus.ts rejects a payload containing a function, and names the path.\n    The failure this prevents is gradual: one callback through the bus and the\n    bus is a coupling mechanism, and nobody notices the first instance.\n    Delivered payloads are frozen so one app cannot mutate another''s fact.\n  - state-ownership.ts refuses a second owner for the same key, converting the\n    State Ownership Rule into an error at the moment two teams would both reach\n    for it and neither would be wrong.\n  - budget.ts reports which TEAM owns each regression, since attribution rather\n    than size is Dave''s actual complaint, and separates \"report it\" from \"fail\n    the build\" per the Budget Visibility Rule.\n\nRuns in Node with no browser and no jsdom: the bus takes an injectable\nEventTarget and the render model is plain functions.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8b99dbe037263b03e3d2a075404948bee9f3a25f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/git/trees/8b99dbe037263b03e3d2a075404948bee9f3a25f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/git/commits/18b9a70363bf72688ebb8c9bbf42eec7abfc1c25","verification":{"payload":"tree 8b99dbe037263b03e3d2a075404948bee9f3a25f\nparent fbd7c0d2551389635dbbfb65d69db499ab41edaf\nauthor Imran Siddique <45405841+imran-siddique@users.noreply.github.com> 1785783511 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785783511 -0700\n\nAdd the Chapter 5 micro-frontend shell (#8)\n\nThe back end is fine, which is the problem: 5.2MB gzipped, 2.8s of main-thread\nblocking, velocity down from daily to weekly, and 14 cross-team merge conflicts\na sprint. The constraint has moved from infrastructure to the organization.\n\nChapter 5 already had six extended notes explaining these ideas well. What the\ncode adds is enforcement, because each of these rules degrades quietly when it\nis only written down.\n\npackages/shell\n  - error-boundary.ts turns the Critical Path Doctrine into a CI check. Its\n    wording is that the page must survive EVERY enhancement failing at once,\n    not one, so the check replaces every enhancement''s render with a throw and\n    asserts the critical path still rendered. There is a test proving the check\n    itself fails when checkout is wired to a recommendations widget, which is\n    the realistic regression: harmless in review, invisible until the widget is\n    down. Registering an enhancement without a fallback is refused.\n  - event-bus.ts rejects a payload containing a function, and names the path.\n    The failure this prevents is gradual: one callback through the bus and the\n    bus is a coupling mechanism, and nobody notices the first instance.\n    Delivered payloads are frozen so one app cannot mutate another''s fact.\n  - state-ownership.ts refuses a second owner for the same key, converting the\n    State Ownership Rule into an error at the moment two teams would both reach\n    for it and neither would be wrong.\n  - budget.ts reports which TEAM owns each regression, since attribution rather\n    than size is Dave''s actual complaint, and separates \"report it\" from \"fail\n    the build\" per the Budget Visibility Rule.\n\nRuns in Node with no browser and no jsdom: the bus takes an injectable\nEventTarget and the render model is plain functions.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcOTXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFdMQABjzYLwfFxuo37iAe6Lfb5jr\nUJqQrysk+gnKhQZMeFocCDiZ6E3gvtOdISiaD444/nmHzMrPWhHnKNl9Vq2FDYJi\nSw9w+qRslc2UaPQ8i0Iibr9+/SyJ76msrAzdapbhFVsUNGjtZ1hpiln85E3ChCt/\nI0C2PS0RsLZ72nWM9FeawOrdiBUixEQ7lyDCF7s377YIdwI18Z9we8n/j5BMNJ3g\nveskGWzpIvsYBF+jyWInMnIyK77oZ1x6hPJaY7qe5p9lWEvXclZB2MjweUuIig63\nqTiezvbqpZvZ8E8gpKlQ//ikrhR2iVU0HjX/EysjBbsitlQGvQkxgfR1phS7RcnG\n6VOAKVevyRouhOqGcjD565n3EZvLPDiU2paYYETXtdqEpbhip9YXTFjX3t2uwrHi\nMQhfvlU4Hfaf97IpfPAa74SQhdODYjMndLkhoU/Bp2dKAFkPDUYlVSFgTiJb0/Yx\nBlcLtK0Nwqm28QdCXTKOF2Gpgoz0lZ1awmPjSmxdKj0VK0iDJVMm6G+nHuiL/LIk\nUWy5GqPEVbBK9OsncH1XIgIZPpms7Fk/5Wz6UZydvW8zRRztnZKa8bbEVbyCsfam\ntPDxLXnoXahxZVbkTAeVougIX8KN5AZyqF9hLaqAp9us9FeqSwKaTRkW3HpkNufg\nOUTuFEoarVlp4GdF3Ynv\n=AZoq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-04T20:48:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commit/18b9a70363bf72688ebb8c9bbf42eec7abfc1c25","node_id":"C_kwDORlo4M9oAKDE4YjlhNzAzNjNiZjcyNjg4ZWJiOGM5YmJmNDJlZWM3YWJmYzFjMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commit/fbd7c0d2551389635dbbfb65d69db499ab41edaf","sha":"fbd7c0d2551389635dbbfb65d69db499ab41edaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commits/fbd7c0d2551389635dbbfb65d69db499ab41edaf"}],"sha":"18b9a70363bf72688ebb8c9bbf42eec7abfc1c25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commits/18b9a70363bf72688ebb8c9bbf42eec7abfc1c25"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45405841?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/imran-siddique","id":45405841,"login":"imran-siddique","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NDA1ODQx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commits/fbd7c0d2551389635dbbfb65d69db499ab41edaf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T17:19:27Z","email":"45405841+imran-siddique@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Imran Siddique"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T17:19:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Remove em dashes from all authored text (#7)\n\n* Remove em dashes from all authored text\n\nRepo-wide style change: 177 em dashes replaced with the punctuation the sentence\nactually wanted, rather than a blind substitution. Headings take a colon,\nconjunctions and relative clauses take a comma, independent clauses take a\nsemicolon or a full stop, and comma-chained lists became parenthetical.\n\nThe mechanical pass alone produced comma splices, which is its own writing\nflaw, so a second explicit pass repaired them by hand. Examples:\n\n  \"the git history is the argument, Chapter 2 onward is where it gets fixed\"\n    -> \"... is the argument: Chapter 2 onward ...\"\n  \"no steady state at all, wait time grows with\"\n    -> \"no steady state at all; wait time grows with\"\n  \"**1.1 The Diagnosis**, correlate p99 spikes\"\n    -> \"**1.1 The Diagnosis**: correlate p99 spikes\"\n  \"Shared infrastructure, the schema, the compose file, carries what ...\"\n    -> \"Shared infrastructure (the schema, the compose file) carries what ...\"\n\nIt also broke the root README''s chapter table: cells holding a lone em dash as\na \"none\" marker collapsed to \"||\". Repaired to empty cells.\n\nch*/prompts.md and PROMPTS.md are left untouched. They reproduce the book''s\nprompts verbatim and are not mine to restyle.\n\nThe pre-existing ch5 notes were included (26 instances) for consistency, since\na style rule that applies to some files is not a style rule. Easy to revert\nthat subset alone if only new text was meant.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Revert ch5/prompts.md: verbatim book text, not mine to restyle\n\nThe ch5 sweep used a ch5/*.md glob, which caught prompts.md and rewrote 7 em\ndashes inside prompt text reproduced verbatim from the book. The whole point of\nexcluding the prompt files is that their wording is the author''s, so this\nrestores it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix TypeScript operators corrupted by the table-repair regex\n\nThe em-dash sweep included a fix for markdown table cells that had collapsed to\n''||'', and I applied it to .ts and .js files as well as .md. Five TypeScript\nlines ending in the logical-or operator became ''|  |'', breaking the build:\n\n  typeof claims.sub !== ''string'' ||   ->   typeof claims.sub !== ''string'' |  |\n\nCI caught it. A markdown fix has no business running over source files, and the\nsweep should have been scoped by extension from the start.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"09ec798a37922d7405529443b7af83abd4843dd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/git/trees/09ec798a37922d7405529443b7af83abd4843dd6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/git/commits/fbd7c0d2551389635dbbfb65d69db499ab41edaf","verification":{"payload":"tree 09ec798a37922d7405529443b7af83abd4843dd6\nparent 1ce36a8a904760e69f00d52802c82ca89024cbd2\nauthor Imran Siddique <45405841+imran-siddique@users.noreply.github.com> 1785777567 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785777567 -0700\n\nRemove em dashes from all authored text (#7)\n\n* Remove em dashes from all authored text\n\nRepo-wide style change: 177 em dashes replaced with the punctuation the sentence\nactually wanted, rather than a blind substitution. Headings take a colon,\nconjunctions and relative clauses take a comma, independent clauses take a\nsemicolon or a full stop, and comma-chained lists became parenthetical.\n\nThe mechanical pass alone produced comma splices, which is its own writing\nflaw, so a second explicit pass repaired them by hand. Examples:\n\n  \"the git history is the argument, Chapter 2 onward is where it gets fixed\"\n    -> \"... is the argument: Chapter 2 onward ...\"\n  \"no steady state at all, wait time grows with\"\n    -> \"no steady state at all; wait time grows with\"\n  \"**1.1 The Diagnosis**, correlate p99 spikes\"\n    -> \"**1.1 The Diagnosis**: correlate p99 spikes\"\n  \"Shared infrastructure, the schema, the compose file, carries what ...\"\n    -> \"Shared infrastructure (the schema, the compose file) carries what ...\"\n\nIt also broke the root README''s chapter table: cells holding a lone em dash as\na \"none\" marker collapsed to \"||\". Repaired to empty cells.\n\nch*/prompts.md and PROMPTS.md are left untouched. They reproduce the book''s\nprompts verbatim and are not mine to restyle.\n\nThe pre-existing ch5 notes were included (26 instances) for consistency, since\na style rule that applies to some files is not a style rule. Easy to revert\nthat subset alone if only new text was meant.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Revert ch5/prompts.md: verbatim book text, not mine to restyle\n\nThe ch5 sweep used a ch5/*.md glob, which caught prompts.md and rewrote 7 em\ndashes inside prompt text reproduced verbatim from the book. The whole point of\nexcluding the prompt files is that their wording is the author''s, so this\nrestores it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix TypeScript operators corrupted by the table-repair regex\n\nThe em-dash sweep included a fix for markdown table cells that had collapsed to\n''||'', and I applied it to .ts and .js files as well as .md. Five TypeScript\nlines ending in the logical-or operator became ''|  |'', breaking the build:\n\n  typeof claims.sub !== ''string'' ||   ->   typeof claims.sub !== ''string'' |  |\n\nCI caught it. A markdown fix has no business running over source files, and the\nsweep should have been scoped by extension from the start.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcM2fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAs0sQAHyDRzMRyia7anXUcD09EuEr\nTXYeOTJt8HJIVc5Itz2/D6cX+0psNdmJpyvRXlNUoWEL1ggx3IjZUiwDxKD936/F\nI6VHwYp5gAjgKA9+LwHNy/W+3+6cMCOaqg/n7OFZy9o1mrKFH43OhwYL2YsVHjwN\nzQGPKJf4PFe+pJywxnPX6G/f4gRgMnfod2BExuT8HYp8Iaef6W6ZCpUQ9mkNPmEs\n5n0YYIhYzsvjEtFjwr88dWWoAMj2c7LYZQNi4Le0QvlYoeL3Tow5Qq9iZlk4MxF4\nXiJqFmKOIHnqC3tqkw2teJOYG74vChsRn8sIYSbqhHS9/xliXoh8QqBR6H6TZ/Oy\nG8H9j7wD4WZnqYUN1ONJo+005aloxBH2clgtknjmC1+bnTQiLkrjD6XIef9799HM\nnZAY6O26FPi4ZBhiX8NCHcnx3BO0IXgmvXtvBordFACsPOgGBm2t+ic6c/uJDcoG\nTYOA4P7b1MvHRsAW6lsxskO1tf3W1Eiw4YrYxMmvqK5+vEmjTwFJseRrXYih3OGe\n6Krzo1wjFbhgXigqk0wgRVWRv7G0ifOBX1PfcblEhZGz0SdpK3KpELHBr7kBHgo1\nN+dzK5kWDDZaYaXmqxZ3hOZrzVR0qelgf6vaC3WnfWsqsyuaZlnIcrYsiUibpnBn\nkTdSGUmEZlGpZRLsBtdm\n=kOB+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-04T04:13:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commit/fbd7c0d2551389635dbbfb65d69db499ab41edaf","node_id":"C_kwDORlo4M9oAKGZiZDdjMGQyNTUxMzg5NjM1ZGJiZmI2NWQ2OWRiNDk5YWI0MWVkYWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commit/1ce36a8a904760e69f00d52802c82ca89024cbd2","sha":"1ce36a8a904760e69f00d52802c82ca89024cbd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commits/1ce36a8a904760e69f00d52802c82ca89024cbd2"}],"sha":"fbd7c0d2551389635dbbfb65d69db499ab41edaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commits/fbd7c0d2551389635dbbfb65d69db499ab41edaf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45405841?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/imran-siddique","id":45405841,"login":"imran-siddique","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NDA1ODQx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commits/1ce36a8a904760e69f00d52802c82ca89024cbd2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T17:07:25Z","email":"45405841+imran-siddique@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Imran Siddique"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T17:07:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add the Chapter 4 edge tier: origin shield, stale-while-revalidate, steering (#6)\n\nZero Trust bought segmentation and paid for it in per-hop latency: 300ms global\nhandshake, availability at 92%, and the CFO asking why \"safe\" feels so \"slow\".\n\nThe edge code lives in packages/cache/src/edge rather than a new package,\nbecause Chapter 4''s origin shield and Chapter 9''s herd defence are the SAME\nmechanism at two tiers - OriginShield reuses Chapter 9''s SingleFlight directly.\nThat reuse is a more useful observation than either chapter makes alone: the\nherd is a property of any tier fronting a slower one, so wherever there is a\nfan-in there has to be a collapse.\n\norigin-shield.ts\n  Two tiers of collapse, neither sufficient alone: 200 users on one PoP become\n  one upstream call, and 50 PoPs missing at the same instant become exactly one\n  origin fetch. Also implements the Golden Rule as mechanism - when the origin\n  is down a stale entry is served rather than a 404, including to a PoP that\n  never held a local copy. And past the stale window it fails rather than lying\n  forever, because serving a price indefinitely is worse than serving an error.\n\ntraffic-steering.ts\n  The Baby-Step Steering Rule with the arithmetic that justifies it. A region\n  that buckles is caught at 1% weight, exposing 1% of requests; the identical\n  failure under a 100% flip exposes all of them. Rollback returns to the last\n  healthy rung rather than zero, since rolling fully back discards the knowledge\n  that the earlier weight was fine and a real failover still needs a target.\n\nshiftTraffic is structurally Chapter 16''s canary release. Noted in ch4/README\nbecause the safe-change primitive recurring across failover, feature rollout\nand architectural experiments is Chapter 16''s closing argument, and this is the\nfirst place it appears.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"78f8db8f91d319444ce1553b59de4b812c7170e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/git/trees/78f8db8f91d319444ce1553b59de4b812c7170e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/git/commits/1ce36a8a904760e69f00d52802c82ca89024cbd2","verification":{"payload":"tree 78f8db8f91d319444ce1553b59de4b812c7170e6\nparent 4d1de8a63126608d3dc6eaa8332bd965829ef167\nauthor Imran Siddique <45405841+imran-siddique@users.noreply.github.com> 1785776845 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785776845 -0700\n\nAdd the Chapter 4 edge tier: origin shield, stale-while-revalidate, steering (#6)\n\nZero Trust bought segmentation and paid for it in per-hop latency: 300ms global\nhandshake, availability at 92%, and the CFO asking why \"safe\" feels so \"slow\".\n\nThe edge code lives in packages/cache/src/edge rather than a new package,\nbecause Chapter 4''s origin shield and Chapter 9''s herd defence are the SAME\nmechanism at two tiers - OriginShield reuses Chapter 9''s SingleFlight directly.\nThat reuse is a more useful observation than either chapter makes alone: the\nherd is a property of any tier fronting a slower one, so wherever there is a\nfan-in there has to be a collapse.\n\norigin-shield.ts\n  Two tiers of collapse, neither sufficient alone: 200 users on one PoP become\n  one upstream call, and 50 PoPs missing at the same instant become exactly one\n  origin fetch. Also implements the Golden Rule as mechanism - when the origin\n  is down a stale entry is served rather than a 404, including to a PoP that\n  never held a local copy. And past the stale window it fails rather than lying\n  forever, because serving a price indefinitely is worse than serving an error.\n\ntraffic-steering.ts\n  The Baby-Step Steering Rule with the arithmetic that justifies it. A region\n  that buckles is caught at 1% weight, exposing 1% of requests; the identical\n  failure under a 100% flip exposes all of them. Rollback returns to the last\n  healthy rung rather than zero, since rolling fully back discards the knowledge\n  that the earlier weight was fine and a real failover still needs a target.\n\nshiftTraffic is structurally Chapter 16''s canary release. Noted in ch4/README\nbecause the safe-change primitive recurring across failover, feature rollout\nand architectural experiments is Chapter 16''s closing argument, and this is the\nfirst place it appears.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcMrNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiMwQAG/UfrQEfAqd7xrneres3HzR\nOt2Kxp6110/OEr5+oAe65MZiL+VbKMDBCyr3XRw/kqp1pP4AXMFXV7ka+k6XFHCR\nlXzONDrVUgSm4T/C/GaO7I2wE+utGTvzMr4UJyDuN3xaKq7lhDyB0yTClOSrtwjR\nI60F8KVsHmULe526/4YlDVc+KSwHrLWXI8pdinYIFF2P1GsfDByMDQlimNvkHdXU\nci3d/QFLxq2fYrDCLE8/7nEI+y2bU/QLpDnCkXfG5wmoojy0DCeHLTYRfXBISW9h\nHyHcGBegfxy/Eols2mwPiXyHv5jbcRu1NEN3f4bmhCpKi0gtVbep0/YjAonXfzwt\nnL5iJdEsTpcDmiMgxA5dL6OFWm8XNbC523sS5mOtHuYkgTVpq6d5hfTHje0FLcks\nKCMND/iZj9SMMqW7wggQMR2OVWwlWaucZzMSmYN2nJn4EGRe0JoZM74e+q8tZbKi\njAs0dp4ZS5vLc+JFstAqAocg+kjK6nsPN6C3ENIxdXuO2CfvJab89TnHB8ji6W38\n0mHf4s8XdBv0g25YEiWj9DCWhEvnNnUqCQuOJ0xjis1rQKMbzxAzvCBpUPBZodrj\nQ++uM6QebERtWfclbxrMJ3ow2F/osPpL8ZWinm5r9Hda+D4LpSN3MPONqet0eoLF\n14azjPGcqK5X6xUiEVew\n=T067\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-04T02:00:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commit/1ce36a8a904760e69f00d52802c82ca89024cbd2","node_id":"C_kwDORlo4M9oAKDFjZTM2YThhOTA0NzYwZTY5ZjAwZDUyODAyYzgyY2E4OTAyNGNiZDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commit/4d1de8a63126608d3dc6eaa8332bd965829ef167","sha":"4d1de8a63126608d3dc6eaa8332bd965829ef167","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commits/4d1de8a63126608d3dc6eaa8332bd965829ef167"}],"sha":"1ce36a8a904760e69f00d52802c82ca89024cbd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commits/1ce36a8a904760e69f00d52802c82ca89024cbd2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45405841?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/imran-siddique","id":45405841,"login":"imran-siddique","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NDA1ODQx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commits/4d1de8a63126608d3dc6eaa8332bd965829ef167/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T16:52:11Z","email":"45405841+imran-siddique@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Imran Siddique"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T16:52:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add the Chapter 3 Zero Trust primitives (#5)\n\nThe perimeter failed: 50,000+ connections, ~90% malicious, availability at 40%\nfor legitimate users while the infrastructure sat healthy and busy serving\nattackers. Chapter 3 replaces trust-by-network-location with trust-by-identity.\n\npackages/security\n  - workload-identity.ts implements Figure 3.3''s handshake with real Ed25519\n    signing. Every verification step is separate and separately tested, because\n    each one is a check an attacker gets to skip if it is omitted: signature,\n    issuer, audience, lifetime cap, expiry, not-before, clock skew.\n  - policy.ts is the default-deny allowlist. Wildcard operations and\n    unjustified grants throw at CONSTRUCTION, not at review time, because\n    review is optional and construction is not.\n  - blast-radius.ts turns Figure 3.1 into arithmetic: compromise a workload\n    and count what it reaches under each model.\n\nThe three principles are asserted rather than described. Verify Explicitly: a\nvalid token issued for Inventory is refused by Payments (confused deputy), and\nthe verifier caps token lifetime so a compromised issuer cannot extend the\nexposure window. Least Privilege: an unlisted call is denied, and a new service\ninherits nothing. Assume Breach: worst-case reachability is 100% of the fleet\nunder the perimeter model versus 2 of 6 under Zero Trust - which is the actual\nframing of the ~20ms mTLS cost the chapter''s skeptic objects to.\n\nworkload-identity.ts carries a prominent warning NOT to use it, pointing at\nplatform workload identity and a vetted JWT library instead. A security\nchapter whose sample code invites copy-paste into production has done harm,\nand the honest place to say so is in the file.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"035d526f6c8ce7ce5fed266298d918a46fa276bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/git/trees/035d526f6c8ce7ce5fed266298d918a46fa276bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/git/commits/4d1de8a63126608d3dc6eaa8332bd965829ef167","verification":{"payload":"tree 035d526f6c8ce7ce5fed266298d918a46fa276bd\nparent 18bf6e44f2eba446101d7f2dd3549489df7b97d5\nauthor Imran Siddique <45405841+imran-siddique@users.noreply.github.com> 1785775931 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785775931 -0700\n\nAdd the Chapter 3 Zero Trust primitives (#5)\n\nThe perimeter failed: 50,000+ connections, ~90% malicious, availability at 40%\nfor legitimate users while the infrastructure sat healthy and busy serving\nattackers. Chapter 3 replaces trust-by-network-location with trust-by-identity.\n\npackages/security\n  - workload-identity.ts implements Figure 3.3''s handshake with real Ed25519\n    signing. Every verification step is separate and separately tested, because\n    each one is a check an attacker gets to skip if it is omitted: signature,\n    issuer, audience, lifetime cap, expiry, not-before, clock skew.\n  - policy.ts is the default-deny allowlist. Wildcard operations and\n    unjustified grants throw at CONSTRUCTION, not at review time, because\n    review is optional and construction is not.\n  - blast-radius.ts turns Figure 3.1 into arithmetic: compromise a workload\n    and count what it reaches under each model.\n\nThe three principles are asserted rather than described. Verify Explicitly: a\nvalid token issued for Inventory is refused by Payments (confused deputy), and\nthe verifier caps token lifetime so a compromised issuer cannot extend the\nexposure window. Least Privilege: an unlisted call is denied, and a new service\ninherits nothing. Assume Breach: worst-case reachability is 100% of the fleet\nunder the perimeter model versus 2 of 6 under Zero Trust - which is the actual\nframing of the ~20ms mTLS cost the chapter''s skeptic objects to.\n\nworkload-identity.ts carries a prominent warning NOT to use it, pointing at\nplatform workload identity and a vetted JWT library instead. A security\nchapter whose sample code invites copy-paste into production has done harm,\nand the honest place to say so is in the file.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcMc7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARS8QAGl96Zh+0dVsXdgtQ0iUiUwJ\n5yoTb1b9INWI4AhO+pS7VsWwsimGRyrOF917yWfja20yfQzKKcyzIgUsjAMOs8yb\nQcait2qdL9IcW/Mluddvz7oA0Y6JTZKn3lEIrMSn8TDkno/6y0DoQ0Z9eXJjbWGE\nvU5qjyEbvWB3hR0ASciC5c+qrCG/GlorX1gYPgZ16ZxoJ/EjehsxxzB7NcoGQOIj\nZJcAVnUtf4c4Sxvxd4QXcBIQXr9JoZbahHTWThVlO2cyVqa84NT19DIs7BCDtl6f\nCxJwyRKAuFti47qmqKriG6AogcmkVHkoi75Y4RnR1CvUGIoizqHgPO6750buLOoV\nCQBF9FrpLhPQONYjVyBXwT/7zLkEZ76Pu7F+1n+s4DLmtbNFg52K0xw3XfN+2w0Z\nuZkRLC3vjyH3TF3Qr6ptAINCN1WGhWSnGjxZAq79Xau9bg5BJyVCEDfeWLCt3i04\nQ5l4CYyhbVG6oOode0DcLV2TSFNf5Be+I2vUQ+7j0NR0QIMcycNa6gWLpO2gB7bX\n6gVsZJjnbt+CIbhI7TxzSxxuDi7sut5B600guOZYOoTKM2SsSYseIr84iwZOBblq\n23qXPqji402HKtOult+5AzADdI+Axorj7oG1xhzifaS61FE3kOuQE7iWEc01/DND\nWzVxAe4ZC1Y9OeAzPCq4\n=7LVV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T23:30:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commit/4d1de8a63126608d3dc6eaa8332bd965829ef167","node_id":"C_kwDORlo4M9oAKDRkMWRlOGE2MzEyNjYwOGQzZGM2ZWFhODMzMmJkOTY1ODI5ZWYxNjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commit/18bf6e44f2eba446101d7f2dd3549489df7b97d5","sha":"18bf6e44f2eba446101d7f2dd3549489df7b97d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commits/18bf6e44f2eba446101d7f2dd3549489df7b97d5"}],"sha":"4d1de8a63126608d3dc6eaa8332bd965829ef167","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commits/4d1de8a63126608d3dc6eaa8332bd965829ef167"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45405841?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/imran-siddique","id":45405841,"login":"imran-siddique","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NDA1ODQx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/imran-siddique","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/commits/18bf6e44f2eba446101d7f2dd3549489df7b97d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T16:42:07Z","email":"45405841+imran-siddique@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Imran Siddique"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T16:42:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add the Chapter 2 platform primitives: statelessness and the correlation ID (#4)\n\nVertical scaling bought headroom and changed nothing structural - 450/500\nconnections became 4,800/5,000 on ten times the hardware. Chapter 2 adds the\ntwo preconditions for going horizontal. Neither is a performance fix.\n\npackages/platform\n  - session/session-store.ts, the read-or-create lookup that replaces every\n    read against instance memory. TTL is mandatory; a session that never\n    expires is an auth bug with a long fuse.\n  - session/fleet.ts models sticky vs stateless routing so Figure 2.2 can be\n    run rather than asserted\n  - correlation/correlation-id.ts implements \"generate at the edge, trust but\n    verify\" - absent mints, valid preserves, malformed REGENERATES. The third\n    case is the one teams skip and the one that makes it a security control.\n  - correlation/middleware.ts mounts first and echoes the ID on the response,\n    so a customer reporting a failure can hand over the exact identifier\n\nFigure 2.2 as a controlled experiment: identical fleet, traffic and instance\nfailure, differing only in where state lives. Sticky loses carts for everyone\npinned to the dead instance and goes lopsided under one 10x bot; the shared\nstore loses zero sessions and stays balanced within 1.5x. Both of the chapter''s\nobjections are consequences of the routing rule, not matters of taste.\n\nThe correlation tests fire eight hostile values at the resolver - a 5,000-char\ncardinality bomb, a newline-injected fake log entry, DROP TABLE, path traversal\n- and assert each is replaced rather than sanitized and kept. outboundHeaders()\nthrows on an invalid ID: a trace that is quietly wrong gets trusted.\n\nThe monolith now mounts the middleware and reports its correlation ID. Its\nsearch route is deliberately still broken - the chapter''s own sequencing point\nis that decoupling state comes before fixing the query.\n\nAlso replaces the tag instructions in app/README.md, which promised a\n`git checkout ch1-monolith` that does not work. Chapters were written as the\nmanuscript finished rather than in order, so the history is not in chapter\norder and a ch1 tag would point at a tree already containing Chapter 9. A\nper-chapter code table replaces it until all sixteen states can be laid down.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c43e9ef465914361915775234cd324ee569da9a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/git/trees/c43e9ef465914361915775234cd324ee569da9a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/imran-siddique/Architecting-at-Scale/git/commits/18bf6e44f2eba446101d7f2dd3549489df7b97d5","verification":{"payload":"tree c43e9ef465914361915775234cd324ee569da9a1\nparent cdda5a1f27b2406262d97fe96662bf052e1874c1\nauthor Imran Siddique <45405841+imran-siddique@users.noreply.github.com> 1785775327 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785775327 -0700\n\nAdd the Chapter 2 platform primitives: statelessness and the correlation ID (#4)\n\nVertical scaling bought headroom and changed nothing structural - 450/500\nconnections became 4,800/5,000 on ten times the hardware. Chapter 2 adds the\ntwo preconditions for going horizontal. Neither is a performance fix.\n\npackages/platform\n  - session/session-store.ts, the read-or-create lookup that replaces every\n    read against instance memory. TTL is mandatory; a session that never\n    expires is an auth bug with a long fuse.\n  - session/fleet.ts models sticky vs stateless routing so Figure 2.2 can be\n    run rather than asserted\n  - correlation/correlation-id.ts implements \"generate at the edge, trust but\n    verify\" - absent mints, valid preserves, malformed REGENERATES. The third\n    case is the one teams skip and the one that makes it a security control.\n  - correlation/middleware.ts mounts first and echoes the ID on the response,\n    so a customer reporting a failure can hand over the exact identifier\n\nFigure 2.2 as a controlled experiment: identical fleet, traffic and instance\nfailure, differing only in where state lives. Sticky loses carts for everyone\npinned to the dead instance and goes lopsided under one 10x bot; the shared\nstore loses zero sessions and stays balanced within 1.5x. Both of the chapter''s\nobjections are consequences of the routing rule, not matters of taste.\n\nThe correlation tests fire eight hostile values at the resolver - a 5,000-char\ncardinality bomb, a newline-injected fake log entry, DROP TABLE, path traversal\n- and assert each is replaced rather than sanitized and kept. outboundHeaders()\nthrows on an invalid ID: a trace that is quietly wrong gets trusted.\n\nThe monolith now mounts the middleware and reports its correlation ID. Its\nsearch route is deliberately still broken - the chapter''s own sequencing point\nis that decoupling state comes before fixing the query.\n\nAlso replaces the tag instructions in app/README.md, which promised a\n`git checkout ch1-monolith` that does not work. Chapters were written as the\nmanuscript finished rather than in order, so the history is not in chapter\norder and a ch1 tag would point at a tree already containing Chapter 9. A\nper-chapter code table replaces it until all sixteen states can be laid down.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcMTfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiQ0QACtKhhOYtX47QZKI5WOP2cHq\nqAlKhzqmybipebcu05do+b9q4hlxhUZWP4Jx1dBqli5ZRMQIFFOh0bnn9oOS08IV\n2Ot849XUwf+HW1C2CmFnB/hCdRw6ZgzDgXLscL2A/feq0uRo4UUMMENrnrprYX+n\npRY2CAeaRBf5UgYH9Wr9nkt2Br7ibJL3LmyOqW9w/BjxhFfCwCuvTTLnkMaNRKtE\nRbay17Y3rYAQiA6fpUy5jm5xADO9OzGXovSaf7vvZlo2TeU/EGBI1dLy8hA5Bfjn\nhdzqPrQXU6MeLr1WwIG9+rD48Tv7kOWjwZfwvdWnMKqRTDawRUJh9hp7/FTzfQW2\nYdhWRR7YPzAj5NpvuOpxde+HxZm3bHvGeFWiAAOJBjan53SkFlpfcjCWvN4AdC12\n8o2Uit1hzD6pdfa78GEZfZzjU0touhiJChMs3t2IbfzKJPlLDYModipwySxLNTfV\ndlXjfZJ0/VDc3UcSwgQOuee5ApktpRMRVbNv3ER4mIMNqvOXEW/UPSBXPGpHztJr\nh625c0C66zDeKoLV7vswASbHziTT+QA4mA+wHjGYy5vRMEohN82OlIPnbhqu6sGE\nPqIvFVfbJ5+qNW+MrrTBEgHfCvMEXBx78JOkF+KAEUdE2SQ5V9nTWLIFvClosg2e\nRpvuoSKOI1g0IErIfFyC\n=5pID\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T23:28:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_e