om/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/f4f1065b81916e4f6577cd8d19ff6906785874e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:18:12Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:18:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Settlement parser: join amounts OCR split after the decimal comma (#1465)\n\nOCR sometimes puts a space after the decimal comma (\"EUR -1.234, 56\").\nThe amount pattern then stopped at the comma and read the thousands\ngroup alone, so a net of one thousand and change came out as a round\nthousand and the statement disagreed with its booking.\n\nSuch amounts are joined before reading, but only where the left part\nis plainly an amount: it has thousands groups, or a currency stands in\nfront of it.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"560b80602f8a8a9db7a92d3befdca7928714b25b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/560b80602f8a8a9db7a92d3befdca7928714b25b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/f4f1065b81916e4f6577cd8d19ff6906785874e7","verification":{"payload":"tree 560b80602f8a8a9db7a92d3befdca7928714b25b\nparent 1397ff616c590deca668e08d80e9f01890117353\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791386292 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791386292 +0200\n\nSettlement parser: join amounts OCR split after the decimal comma (#1465)\n\nOCR sometimes puts a space after the decimal comma (\"EUR -1.234, 56\").\nThe amount pattern then stopped at the comma and read the thousands\ngroup alone, so a net of one thousand and change came out as a round\nthousand and the statement disagreed with its booking.\n\nSuch amounts are joined before reading, but only where the left part\nis plainly an amount: it has thousands groups, or a currency stands in\nfront of it.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxmK0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATm8QAACaZUR9JFZN0vsMPKPXPWLf\nCDlEmKgrX4PQWtNmG6tmqdbE8Qv8Dt48j+ciG/4ObR+6TNnKCgwNyevPL/y7DYTK\n7M82I+8wmD/6bEP8HJaJH8Em1jlrS8vCWhqjVx6V7o6zn6B9xfnkjb2Xgw/4DSZD\nEMreM1FdiuIpWCR1v4QqM1hHAXADWUGysEQgZFrC8RXMgLj5Un7HPVy7ZYzTlLC3\nsBJIrGIcJdhpxHBN0R48IXGrTFRYFr6ARjZUOceBE/fRHkMfQqKdAxjzguC7qxLT\nskUM/ML94Si1bcjgMhgu1RfYWFDkXlHgOrgc4L3Tnri7SbZFEjKDEeX4ntGs0vDi\nwVQHtdbxVDQVq+IOPADpCYPqP7u/H9yW3dq9rh6F8qRtRT+c1fxlnfmz/03l7u7e\nAbXJ9Pr4BRlQ+CM/P1bD/Dxu8c7PXhRPnAvVZ3Meni3QPnOSexxlENg/Z9KI8a0H\nBFCePpuxMcAuvnFCXYmhlmXldObXUPdtnDLrroLxXEvFYI7+WsOUq3iIziMJrppc\ngpkspwCmh52OqfuCOz3Ta3e0Nqwh73zjn7Y4TiuAfr3QYUKb7M1uPWMVExvB6eK6\nnrORoJME3omDWQS4NIhPqhbeq2pE3ojP5bZxLVAGATNsi3JS49VagjbBZqqlG3HO\n7/dWefMtdPOBdi5ej0Ih\n=Zh5M\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T15:18:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/f4f1065b81916e4f6577cd8d19ff6906785874e7","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKGY0ZjEwNjViODE5MTZlNGY2NTc3Y2Q4ZDE5ZmY2OTA2Nzg1ODc0ZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/1397ff616c590deca668e08d80e9f01890117353","sha":"1397ff616c590deca668e08d80e9f01890117353","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/1397ff616c590deca668e08d80e9f01890117353"}],"sha":"f4f1065b81916e4f6577cd8d19ff6906785874e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/f4f1065b81916e4f6577cd8d19ff6906785874e7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/1397ff616c590deca668e08d80e9f01890117353/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:53:08Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T14:53:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"iOS: collage swaps that swap, caption alignment, and Photos-style swipe-to-select (#1464)\n\nSwapping two collage photos now changes the picture. Each tile carries `.id(photo.id)`, so a cell that gets a new photo also gets a new image loader instead of keeping its old one in `@State`. The editor replaces the layout picker in place instead of being pushed, so changes to its state always reach the screen.\n\nA caption''s frame is always 90 % of the canvas. Left and right alignment place even a single short line at the frame''s edges, in the iOS preview and render and in the web dialog.\n\nSelection in the photo grids works as in Photos. A swipe that starts sideways selects and may then continue in any direction; one that starts up or down scrolls. While selecting, the scroll view and the navigation back-swipe wait for the swipe to fail, and holding near an edge scrolls the grid by itself with the selection following.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016LiwkGCxsp2BNzCigrvHiH","tree":{"sha":"ad0a20c877b06706cebb13aecd7abf1b636e49a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/ad0a20c877b06706cebb13aecd7abf1b636e49a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/1397ff616c590deca668e08d80e9f01890117353","verification":{"payload":"tree ad0a20c877b06706cebb13aecd7abf1b636e49a3\nparent fa3a4fe48b76417bff126efa44116f4aa0015166\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791384788 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791384788 +0200\n\niOS: collage swaps that swap, caption alignment, and Photos-style swipe-to-select (#1464)\n\nSwapping two collage photos now changes the picture. Each tile carries `.id(photo.id)`, so a cell that gets a new photo also gets a new image loader instead of keeping its old one in `@State`. The editor replaces the layout picker in place instead of being pushed, so changes to its state always reach the screen.\n\nA caption''s frame is always 90 % of the canvas. Left and right alignment place even a single short line at the frame''s edges, in the iOS preview and render and in the web dialog.\n\nSelection in the photo grids works as in Photos. A swipe that starts sideways selects and may then continue in any direction; one that starts up or down scrolls. While selecting, the scroll view and the navigation back-swipe wait for the swipe to fail, and holding near an edge scrolls the grid by itself with the selection following.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016LiwkGCxsp2BNzCigrvHiH","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxlzUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFvwQAKHpidIWYyTBlNHTpO+CH4KR\n8HUrOhkZ1IKlQxR2RnpeAQ7e8oNu8JvZNd0kO6eByM2SrlRPfXR8AFrViEW/7FLq\nI0JKcomxaHv5DmGViN84nIvkYYiXtoKhSUMZPnaSIx1DfAVb8h6u4dvqiI+cuWkc\nEJjq8D2wiemlzWy74PSD6yqK0GEgz12ERKDLTCKtTDMTB1IVbDV81RMmmqAY9I9q\n0BAQHOqP/Yf4pqZt9w4tBfPswwOHWS98K2xuLa14ITGZ5wBk8ZGWBHDfNeaWV3Dp\nsvSFfy4Jw/prxUmwhIloDPU7CvodDEununeqkUPFn8fB+tBuvfSGakV5Njhg0ctW\nnFrsJGUf84MBoiGr/mbJW2NmS5XcMtcSmXasVn9qjGJr+U/M1lM082oLtArVseca\n1mTNZscDnMnQzrxaa5ySz2SDD8116sR3Ac2ZLEh1LOCrUdqYLJ6Am0k8BLK890u7\n53W940lSfrTTiAftfTTOI1