ogin":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/98d2f6e0f9e9aabb6688dcbb19b1363c6a4b0472","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDk4ZDJmNmUwZjllOWFhYmI2Njg4ZGNiYjE5YjEzNjNjNmE0YjA0NzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/d3a2158d9fdc419672ff306cf2190273dbc15524","sha":"d3a2158d9fdc419672ff306cf2190273dbc15524","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/d3a2158d9fdc419672ff306cf2190273dbc15524"}],"sha":"98d2f6e0f9e9aabb6688dcbb19b1363c6a4b0472","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/98d2f6e0f9e9aabb6688dcbb19b1363c6a4b0472"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/d3a2158d9fdc419672ff306cf2190273dbc15524/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:42:16Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:42:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Portfolio: derive bookings of positions closed before the first snapshot (#1458)\n\n* Portfolio: derive bookings of positions closed before the first snapshot\n\nGiro bookings were only turned into depot transactions when a holdings\nsnapshot on the bankcontact carried the security. A position sold before\nthe first sync never has one, so its buys and sells on the settlement\naccount were skipped and the position showed only what its documents\nprovided.\n\n- Fall back to the one depot on the bankcontact that already has\n  transactions of the security (e.g. read from settlement documents).\n  Two depots with such rows: no guess.\n- Read an ISIN the booking text prints with a space inside, accepted only\n  when its check digit holds. The checksum moves next to the extraction.\n- Re-derive after reading documents created new rows, so the bookings of\n  such a position appear without waiting for the next sync.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n* Portfolio: unknown cost instead of zero after a buy without quantity\n\nA buy derived from a bank booking alone carries no quantity or price.\nThe realized walk skipped it, so the next sale was costed against what\nthe priced buys left — often nothing — and its whole proceeds showed as\ngain.\n\n- A buy with quantity but no price makes later sales'' costs unknown until\n  the known quantity is sold out; one without quantity makes them unknown\n  for good, since there is no telling when the inventory is empty.\n- Such a sale reports cost, cost per unit and gain as null, is left out\n  of the realized sum and marks it incomplete; its year still counts it.\n- The position page shows \"–\" with a hint for those sales, and marks a\n  year whose sum leaves one out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n* Tests: replace the real security in finance fixtures with an invented one\n\nThe derivation, holdings, depot-transaction and statement tests used a\nreal listed company''s name, ISIN and WKN. They now use an invented\nsecurity (name SONNENOBST, ISIN XF00SONNE005 with a valid check digit,\nWKN SNN001); the code comments that named it follow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d0de7da272e06cb61633be967fa29377e0e98f14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/d0de7da272e06cb61633be967fa29377e0e98f14"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/d3a2158d9fdc419672ff306cf2190273dbc15524","verification":{"payload":"tree d0de7da272e06cb61633be967fa29377e0e98f14\nparent 2f7f79abc4bd0f28fcb29bf3de343e31af8fdb6f\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791294136 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791294136 +0200\n\nPortfolio: derive bookings of positions closed before the first snapshot (#1458)\n\n* Portfolio: derive bookings of positions closed before the first snapshot\n\nGiro bookings were only turned into depot transactions when a holdings\nsnapshot on the bankcontact carried the security. A position sold before\nthe first sync never has one, so its buys and sells on the settlement\naccount were skipped and the position showed only what its documents\nprovided.\n\n- Fall back to the one depot on the bankcontact that already has\n  transactions of the security (e.g. read from settlement documents).\n  Two depots with such rows: no guess.\n- Read an ISIN the booking text prints with a space inside, accepted only\n  when its check digit holds. The checksum moves next to the extraction.\n- Re-derive after reading documents created new rows, so the bookings of\n  such a position appear without waiting for the next sync.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n* Portfolio: unknown cost instead of zero after a buy without quantity\n\nA buy derived from a bank booking alone carries no quantity or price.\nThe realized walk skipped it, so the next sale was costed against what\nthe priced buys left — often nothing — and its whole proceeds showed as\ngain.\n\n- A buy with quantity but no price makes later sales'' costs unknown until\n  the known quantity is sold out; one without quantity makes them unknown\n  for good, since there is no telling when the inventory is empty.\n- Such a sale reports cost, cost per unit and gain as null, is left out\n  of the realized sum and marks it incomplete; its year still counts it.\n- The position page shows \"–\" with a hint for those sales, and marks a\n  year whose sum leaves one out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n* Tests: replace the real security in finance fixtures with an invented one\n\nThe derivation, holdings, depot-transaction and statement tests used a\nreal listed company''s name, ISIN and WKN. They now use an invented\nsecurity (name SONNENOBST, ISIN XF00SONNE005 with a valid check digit,\nWKN SNN001); the code comments that named it follow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCA