erever one is near enough; a journey takes a\nfind only when no stay is, which is a place on the way. Both callers\n(a shared find, a shared article''s proposals) pass the leg''s kind.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b1e1439a04f1b8244293d2cf19cf2cbcc525da0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/b1e1439a04f1b8244293d2cf19cf2cbcc525da0a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/2f7f79abc4bd0f28fcb29bf3de343e31af8fdb6f","verification":{"payload":"tree b1e1439a04f1b8244293d2cf19cf2cbcc525da0a\nparent c4a2913027e91bc96b9938794cbe76a15231d66f\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791236785 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791236785 +0200\n\nTrip planner: a shared find goes to the stay, not to the journey arriving there (#1457)\n\nA journey (§22.7) is anchored where it arrives — the stay''s own anchor\n— so by distance alone the two tied, and a spot shared for a port\nlanded in \"Weiterreise nach …\", where nobody looks for it. chooseLeg\nnow prefers a stay wherever one is near enough; a journey takes a\nfind only when no stay is, which is a place on the way. Both callers\n(a shared find, a shared article''s proposals) pass the leg''s kind.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxBqxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAB2EQABlJ7dNFXJ8dAZvikfIYLF8m\nDjyUtKMXXaxTBRiTi3vXGeJFUpDTGQ7t5OxIgqBzuYJPeCNXYLbmRUIp0hFpnSyw\njCPmcZUaOX2UZabgdJqTDit8z0b2KNiqV6QoikvY03D3rVNd14miG1bsPivAeNQA\n6Pe6vxOW3zvNVWQ9Blc1pA1HcBni2gRntoT7NcHb9KWd5VlCbhH+TZJBDrv42plT\nrrNPxvOSd8gLAU8ehxi9L/5VHHoEg8RRAW6eRH3uhz06iHaOij+gKquemEiFu07I\np+QCYd2ACshUTxR3gTsWYaWIt6fL/frwwebCVj83jOvUrS+Z0nCjgSlphhCAUFKL\n1LuVRXhqyuKR6X1g1B+3eZO1iGDnSI2LeM+ho+OPergmpxTFe9n8rdhbizM1dRx8\nG5XaVON35t1SCfx