c32e0bd02d8eb4c26eb643","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/8cd214dc0480fc2febc32e0bd02d8eb4c26eb643"}],"sha":"5c518fdb61d0a841bf6263ad24e690e3010a52ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/5c518fdb61d0a841bf6263ad24e690e3010a52ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/8cd214dc0480fc2febc32e0bd02d8eb4c26eb643/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T19:25:09Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T19:25:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Depot documents: accumulation tax, settlement-account bookings, per-paper fields (#1454)\n\n* Accumulation notices: no tax when none was deducted; no amounts from legal references\n\nNotices of accumulated income still listed wrong \"correct\" values:\n\n- A fund abroad: the notice says no tax was deducted (\"kein\n  Steuerabzug\"), yet a tax was read from a legal reference in the\n  boilerplate (\"Kirchensteuer nach § …a EStG\"). A number named by §,\n  Abs., Nr. or Art. is never an amount now, and a notice saying no tax\n  was deducted charges nothing — such a misbooked dividend is removed on\n  correction instead of rebooked.\n- The model''s amount on such a notice is the income kept, never a net;\n  only its tax counts.\n- The inspection took the net of the row a document is linked to as the\n  account booking even when that row was created from the document\n  itself, so a wrong reading \"matched the booking\". Only a row an\n  account booking or another source confirmed decides now.\n- Names: \"Vermögensdepot\" is a label, and an OCR''d \"Stiick <n>\" prefix\n  is the quantity column.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n* Settlement account: only its securities bookings reach the depots\n\nA depot''s settlement account books more than trades: fees, taxes on\nincome a fund kept, transfers, interest. Two leaks:\n\n- Giro derivation: without the bank''s transaction code (MT940, manual\n  import) every booking that named a security was a buy or a sale by\n  its sign — a custody fee became a buy, a dividend a sale. The text\n  now decides: a trade''s wording wins; fees, charges and taxes are\n  skipped; a payout is a dividend.\n- Documents: an account statement whose settlement words stand only in\n  the back page''s boilerplate is not a settlement (\"account_statement\")\n  and leaves the depot review; one that carries a trade''s booking still\n  is.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n* Depot documents: each kind of paper with its own fields, hint and matching\n\nTrades, dividend credit notes, tax statements and notices of accumulated\nincome print different things, but were read, shown and matched as if\nthey were the same paper.\n\n- PaperType (trade, dividend, tax_statement, accumulation) from what the\n  rules recognised.\n- The model is told which kind of paper it reads and what each field\n  means there (per-share amount on a credit note, before/after taxes on\n  a tax statement, only the tax charged on an accumulation notice).\n  Answers already stored are not asked again.\n- Matching: a dividend whose amount is not the one booked (before or\n  after taxes, another currency) is found by its quantity and days\n  instead of reported as a conflict; the booking''s amount stays.\n- Dialog: each kind shows only the fields it prints, under its own\n  labels (\"Betrag je Stück\", \"Betrag vor/nach Steuern\", \"Abgeführte\n  Steuer\"), and only the checks it can be put through.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1d19a08ce78de69ea7f27e46687fa5b424acbb30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/1d19a08ce78de69ea7f27e46687fa5b424acbb30"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/8cd214dc0480fc2febc32e0bd02d8eb4c26eb643","verification":{"payload":"tree 1d19a08ce78de69ea7f27e46687fa5b424acbb30\nparent fc4f595cba057b620336eee4abc02c568d046630\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791228309 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791228309 +0200\n\nDepot documents: accumulation tax, settlement-account bookings, per-paper fields (#1454)\n\n* Accumulation notices: no tax when none was deducted; no amounts from legal references\n\nNotices of accumulated income still listed wrong \"correct\" values:\n\n- A fund abroad: the notice says no tax was deducted (\"kein\n  Steuerabzug\"), yet a tax was read from a legal reference in the\n  boilerplate (\"Kirchensteuer nach § …a EStG\"). A number named by §,\n  Abs., Nr. or Art. is never an amount now, and a notice saying no tax\n  was deducted charges nothing — such a misbooked dividend is removed on\n  correction instead of rebooked.\n- The model''s amount on such a notice is the income kept, never a net;\n  only its tax counts.\n- The inspection took the net of the row a document is linked to as the\n  account booking even when that row was created from the document\n  itself, so a wrong reading \"matched the booking\". Only a row an\n  account booking or another source confirmed decides now.\n- Names: \"Vermögensdepot\" is a label, and an OCR''d \"Stiick <n>\" prefix\n  is the quantity column.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n* Settlement account: only its securities bookings reach the depots\n\nA depot''s settlement account books more than trades: fees, taxes on\nincome a fund kept, transfers, interest. Two leaks:\n\n- Giro derivation: without the bank''s transaction code (MT940, manual\n  import) every booking that named a security was a buy or a sale by\n  its sign — a custody fee became a buy, a dividend a sale. The text\n  now decides: a trade''s wording wins; fees, charges and taxes are\n  skipped; a payout is a dividend.\n- Documents: an account statement whose settlement words stand only in\n  the back page''s boilerplate is not a settlement (\"account_statement\")\n  and leaves the depot review; one that carries a trade''s booking still\n  is.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n* Depot documents: each kind of paper with its own fields, hint and matching\n\nTrades, dividend credit notes, tax statements and notices of accumulated\nincome print different things, but were read, shown and matched as if\nthey were the same paper.\n\n- PaperType (trade, dividend, tax_statement, accumulation) from what the\n  rules recognised.\n- The model is told which kind of paper it reads and what each field\n  means there (per-share amount on a credit note, before/after taxes on\n  a tax statement, only the tax charged on an accumulation notice).\n  Answers already stored are not asked again.\n- Matching: a dividend whose amount is not the one booked (before or\n  after taxes, another currency) is found by its quantity and days\n  instead of reported as a conflict; the booking''s amount stays.\n- Dialog: each kind shows only the fields it prints, under its own\n  labels (\"Betrag je Stück\", \"Betrag vor/nach Steuern\", \"Abgeführte\n  Steuer\"), and only the checks it can be put through.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw/mVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZEIQAKi0voFzw41vuPrz6sXrz02Q\nDXR1WU140pluFmEgCHlCLQZj7kjhGfC1WRib4whPxCVHYuIIG1KnUEWmHgVY3umB\nkRruObBwNbKfQ+wjiQ/J32sbHh+D6QE90MyxR46/Ag4RpRHX/9IeNDAa7gQKfQDw\nthuz+qQpOxyarqZUWoumB0KJ7thDKCKaDZ7KdZPaGy22XXWhkwJ1AIYwM2eNIXEP\n7OhkjlIcvD+BWFXT7iuniwOMgYwuqV4yIbsQV4vpUrGkgb3H2uip30cLShRW8MVd\nNAZ78g2IdMWhXVNCmKYEsNqV8ibN374YlPlFHqv+HhbdiDjc2wuuswqBR12IQz46\nl1im0CeJtxTBlGDAyFlOsfMi5Mcnd/GGtJJGaP7do5bcXCwZNWj8exmOzhlYaTLY\nvz3Hk1abwIDL6CVoagruloiU5aOWvjapPiVpILuRFGjrFjxRXasBgGOEmyiZGqR6\neiUYD2n8dvULvpWplmBMnwyTbU+Q8BJagQnc5m+VcgOv7CZVN9xCDURQSRCqaXFw\nH+S7EmIY6ARIeBvMnJ+vemFd3O2Covo6Tq5sgx0HIviR2dnd47ACVdmtO3gAz0uZ\nLYlMpAmFAaBox1u8femtrukQdVw1PlCfp6qhtfe0xfj1EJpyukdB9obvtvbJu+WJ\nIqNg9D0WaFdzzgk8VgPq\n=Yt3w\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T19:25:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/8cd214dc0480fc2febc32e0bd02d8eb4c26eb643","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDhjZDIxNGRjMDQ4MGZjMmZlYmMzMmUwYmQwMmQ4ZWI0YzI2ZWI2NDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/fc4f595cba057b620336eee4abc02c568d046630","sha":"fc4f595cba057b620336eee4abc02c568d046630","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/fc4f595cba057b620336eee4abc02c568d046630"}],"sha":"8cd214dc0480fc2febc32e0bd02d8eb4c26eb643","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/8cd214dc0480fc2febc32e0bd02d8eb4c26eb643"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/fc4f595cba057b620336eee4abc02c568d046630/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T19:15:45Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T19:15:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Trip planner: the trip limit counts places to stay; the meal block offers the candidates (#1455)\n\n* Trip planner: the trip limit counts places to stay, not journeys\n\nA trip could have ten legs, and since journeys became legs (§22.7)\nthe way there, the way home and the journeys between counted too: six\ncities with their journeys were already twelve, and \"Stadt\nhinzufügen\" went grey at six. The limit is twenty places to stay now,\non the server (adding a leg, creating a plan) and in the app; the\njourneys are bounded by the stays.\n\nBuild 1698.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* iOS trip planner: the meal block offers the candidates and shows its stop\n\nThe lunch block had one way in — \"Essen in der Nähe\" — and none from\nthe candidates, so a restaurant somebody added by hand could only be\nplaced into a sightseeing block; and a stop placed into the meal\nblock was not drawn at all. The block now lists its stop like any\nother, offers \"Aus den Kandidaten\" when the pool holds somewhere to\neat, and the pool opened for a block shows only what may go into it:\nrestaurants and cafés for a meal, no restaurant for a sightseeing\nblock.\n\nBuild 1699.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dadf70369fdb908aa40b99056a55b2c9b41b7d9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/dadf70369fdb908aa40b99056a55b2c9b41b7d9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/fc4f595cba057b620336eee4abc02c568d046630","verification":{"payload":"tree dadf70369fdb908aa40b99056a55b2c9b41b7d9a\nparent 981ee1f844c3c05770fcf1cd7d74fcd708c00c86\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791227745 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791227745 +0200\n\nTrip planner: the trip limit counts places to stay; the meal block offers the candidates (#1455)\n\n* Trip planner: the trip limit counts places to stay, not journeys\n\nA trip could have ten legs, and since journeys became legs (§22.7)\nthe way there, the way home and the journeys between counted too: six\ncities with their journeys were already twelve, and \"Stadt\nhinzufügen\" went grey at six. The limit is twenty places to stay now,\non the server (adding a leg, creating a plan) and in the app; the\njourneys are bounded by the stays.\n\nBuild 1698.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* iOS trip planner: the meal block offers the candidates and shows its stop\n\nThe lunch block had one way in — \"Essen in der Nähe\" — and none from\nthe candidates, so a restaurant somebody added by hand could only be\nplaced into a sightseeing block; and a stop placed into the meal\nblock was not drawn at all. The block now lists its stop like any\nother, offers \"Aus den Kandidaten\" when the pool holds somewhere to\neat, and the pool opened for a block shows only what may go into it:\nrestaurants and cafés for a meal, no restaurant for a sightseeing\nblock.\n\nBuild 1699.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SI