s19git67/fk-encore/commit/5a9d1b94c8b2d0adc766e7fe97d1eda660305508","sha":"5a9d1b94c8b2d0adc766e7fe97d1eda660305508","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/5a9d1b94c8b2d0adc766e7fe97d1eda660305508"}],"sha":"c347198a83390d50a4163b0e280d4a442684be1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/c347198a83390d50a4163b0e280d4a442684be1b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/5a9d1b94c8b2d0adc766e7fe97d1eda660305508/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T11:12:48Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T11:12:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"iOS trip planner: leg chips shaped like the day chips; pin sheets grow to full height (#1450)\n\n* iOS trip planner: leg chips shaped like the day chips\n\nCapsules over rounded rectangles read as two controls. A leg''s chip\nis now the day''s: two lines (the name, then \"3 Tage\" or the journey''s\ntransport), the same corner radius, the same highlight, nothing\nbehind an unselected one.\n\nBuild 1695.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* iOS trip maps: the pin sheet grows to full height and leaves the map bright\n\nThe sheet behind a pin on the day map, the pool map and the ballot\nmap was stuck at half height, and the system dimmed the map under\nit so the whole screen looked switched off. Medium and large detents\nnow, and background interaction up through medium, which keeps the\nmap bright and usable.\n\nBuild 1696.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"971747891e2b401110f7b680db8fa78174fb2ecf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/971747891e2b401110f7b680db8fa78174fb2ecf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/5a9d1b94c8b2d0adc766e7fe97d1eda660305508","verification":{"payload":"tree 971747891e2b401110f7b680db8fa78174fb2ecf\nparent e2e2484c5c04688820c17fe1af5e1a7433680521\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791198768 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791198768 +0200\n\niOS trip planner: leg chips shaped like the day chips; pin sheets grow to full height (#1450)\n\n* iOS trip planner: leg chips shaped like the day chips\n\nCapsules over rounded rectangles read as two controls. A leg''s chip\nis now the day''s: two lines (the name, then \"3 Tage\" or the journey''s\ntransport), the same corner radius, the same highlight, nothing\nbehind an unselected one.\n\nBuild 1695.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* iOS trip maps: the pin sheet grows to full height and leaves the map bright\n\nThe sheet behind a pin on the day map, the pool map and the ballot\nmap was stuck at half height, and the system dimmed the map under\nit so the whole screen looked switched off. Medium and large detents\nnow, and background interaction up through medium, which keeps the\nmap bright and usable.\n\nBuild 1696.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw4YwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAO44QAFWdrlMAAJn34i3rBdF+naXP\nFpvVIbN+43IMioKK5IIOQZ/82FuEnhUWu+QmdeGoSzhRSuTrPLg0pi8U6aPyh+oC\ntk67ojhLZBU6pIwfS1AcG44kswJrN1vitPrrWk2y4+IUXHb9Lu5bCAT2F8WwmhJ7\n4QNYvXGl9DYuR04QXrOf2VZQ8oKQd+uPJoBtHQWHmTAkcUyAO52YJxfGbyheQ0hx\nTqDBvG5OOia3BNI1Bn+SctGW1rfpTrPqGAMEnkYSh1L29pTL2DhKDWFwzf+N0l8Q\n2eSEwDdhre/NTS2ulLziJlvp49TB6PFwAvhcklEghyv2i4qOSS567St4w37Yuceb\nxd3U4pWU8xtvOcsbCfDSAJzKbYaRtQ+YYFAdgF7u1K/C4EL2FV8zll2WxHKYnJuO\neEv7ZZs4gr0EdkieLKzTomNKG7yEwWTVkOpZcnbU2RsmiLKIV15bLm6JdEZVrjTh\np9GG0ocMyBOuwbCkYrpfLQSS8gLD8ZElwTHKP1VGf8/mDdVmtNeCHP9UtqOADPu0\nYvaDXuS3jeDbcX0ym7G30cazVy1Wxd/6CUgPduPf/2EXfrY9iRPvS/M8r8bVWS6V\nJigEX4WlTHxgKmUBFAPQZYgWaUwF4enzvdQr0RW1o8dUa9nDdJhA90yS5HI96MfQ\nD+zkqUSx7nw4kq1okl/f\n=GRR9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T11:12:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/5a9d1b94c8b2d0adc766e7fe97d1eda660305508","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDVhOWQxYjk0YzhiMmQwYWRjNzY2ZTdmZTk3ZDFlZGE2NjAzMDU1MDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/e2e2484c5c04688820c17fe1af5e1a7433680521","sha":"e2e2484c5c04688820c17fe1af5e1a7433680521","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/e2e2484c5c04688820c17fe1af5e1a7433680521"}],"sha":"5a9d1b94c8b2d0adc766e7fe97d1eda660305508","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/5a9d1b94c8b2d0adc766e7fe97d1eda660305508"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/e2e2484c5c04688820c17fe1af5e1a7433680521/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T10:04:11Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T10:04:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Holding reconciliation: a trade valued after the snapshot that shows it still explains it (#1449)\n\n* Holding reconciliation: a trade valued after the snapshot that shows it still explains it\n\nDepot rows derived from an account booking carry the value date, which\noften falls a day or two after the snapshot that already shows the new\nshare count. Transactions were only handed to snapshots on or after\ntheir date, so such a change was listed under \"holding without matching\ntransaction\" while the trade waited for the next change.\n\nWhen the pooled transactions do not explain a change, the ones dated up\nto five days after the snapshot are taken too — but only if they then\nexplain it exactly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n* Trip planner tests: unique test-user emails instead of Date.now()\n\nThe beforeEach hooks created a user named after Date.now(). Two tests\nstarting within the same millisecond inserted the same email and failed\non users_email_unique (seen in CI on trip-planner/wiki-article.test.ts).\ncrypto.randomUUID() cannot collide.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f8c3fcb16fe339c8f61663f2ed3ae25401c423a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/f8c3fcb16fe339c8f61663f2ed3ae25401c423a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/e2e2484c5c04688820c17fe1af5e1a7433680521","verification":{"payload":"tree f8c3fcb16fe339c8f61663f2ed3ae25401c423a0\nparent 63f2905275be0dbd050efb212e033aed5eb6c0a2\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791194651 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791194651 +0200\n\nHolding reconciliation: a trade valued after the snapshot that shows it still explains it (#1449)\n\n* Holding reconciliation: a trade valued after the snapshot that shows it still explains it\n\nDepot rows derived from an account booking carry the value date, which\noften falls a day or two after the snapshot that already shows the new\nshare count. Transactions were only handed to snapshots on or after\ntheir date, so such a change was listed under \"holding without matching\ntransaction\" while the trade waited for the next change.\n\nWhen the pooled transactions do not explain a change, the ones dated up\nto five days after the snapshot are taken too — but only if they then\nexplain it exactly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n* Trip planner tests: unique test-user emails instead of Date.now()\n\nThe beforeEach hooks created a user named after Date.now(). Two tests\nstarting within the same millisecond inserted the same email and failed\non users_email_unique (seen in CI on trip-planner/wiki-article.test.ts).\ncrypto.randomUUID() cannot collide.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw3YbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAER8QAE59H3Mi1yyoVg8Zpb2Fgsxu\nX4PmMn+3AUSBS4iRiLSmJZ5GJrq0jlgD1P4JopNSYVvkNkXLpAKXCvfJiILLWia9\nigVp0OzWaiwaTn8oDM+nAAtSNS/jdvf+t61LS7Uxpl/9iIWb3Oe/91fWKHWIYWVF\nZj5BtlVZ4q6QU2xbIal0pDpYUsfFhxMTrp3GcRvlgZqBDeG0r2XzDD51kt+Ff364\nGo5AhFupdwysES0lWE/qOKHvOiKTyJs+I8by7PpZq8bSjvtnTErJ0vQRXtUS9S5n\nyNk7FqMXHe4VDA+H/0J2ZtMrwNiQV0HhAiqDROYUs6Y/q2TWIuQ/0F0/Uc4DG/na\nRCMmVJPyWMHc6x3irtB37dEmkVlbiib6oZmSkWMdUNDMUfrIeXgMIB1oNCR+eJCm\n3olXzxKKviqskPXIaDUm7xTP18ySW8fX84e3g2AVZ