TI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/69be4d76676d0744dba3dfdccc4c4c1e4700ac9b","sha":"69be4d76676d0744dba3dfdccc4c4c1e4700ac9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/69be4d76676d0744dba3dfdccc4c4c1e4700ac9b"}],"sha":"63f2905275be0dbd050efb212e033aed5eb6c0a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/63f2905275be0dbd050efb212e033aed5eb6c0a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/69be4d76676d0744dba3dfdccc4c4c1e4700ac9b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T08:11:23Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T08:11:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Trip planner: languages not to translate, the original behind a switch, and a daily revision check (§25, stage C) (#1448)\n\n* Trip planner: languages not to translate, and the original behind a switch (§25, stage C)\n\nThe server translated every article that was not German — wrong for a\nreader who has English or Italian and would rather read the text as\nwritten. Two things:\n\n- A trip setting \"Wikipedia-Artikel › Nicht übersetzen\": the languages\n  the reader can read, kept on the device and sent with every article\n  request as keepLanguages. An article in one of them is answered as\n  written (translation \"skipped\") and no translation is started; a\n  later reader without that language gets the translation, from the\n  cached text, without asking Wikipedia again.\n- A finished translation keeps the original (description and\n  sections) beside it. The article screen shows a segmented switch\n  \"Deutsch | Original (Italienisch)\"; it opens on the original for a\n  language the reader keeps, on German otherwise.\n\nBuild 1694.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* Trip planner: a kept article is checked against Wikipedia''s revision once a day\n\nA kept article was read again only after a month, and then translated\nanew whether or not it had changed. Now it carries the page''s revision\nid. When somebody opens an article kept for more than a day, the\nserver asks Wikipedia for the revision id alone; only a changed id\nfetches the article again and, where it has to, translates it anew —\nin the background, so the reader gets the kept text at once and the\nnew one on the next opening. A failed check changes nothing; the\nmonth stays as the outer limit. The reader shows \"Stand: <date>\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"51927d7180ad1fd54d563a4b5ecf301fbf3cfb8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/51927d7180ad1fd54d563a4b5ecf301fbf3cfb8d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/69be4d76676d0744dba3dfdccc4c4c1e4700ac9b","verification":{"payload":"tree 51927d7180ad1fd54d563a4b5ecf301fbf3cfb8d\nparent a364b07ff21ab3e24dd4daba313075080e3a6fd5\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791187883 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791187883 +0200\n\nTrip planner: languages not to translate, the original behind a switch, and a daily revision check (§25, stage C) (#1448)\n\n* Trip planner: languages not to translate, and the original behind a switch (§25, stage C)\n\nThe server translated every article that was not German — wrong for a\nreader who has English or Italian and would rather read the text as\nwritten. Two things:\n\n- A trip setting \"Wikipedia-Artikel › Nicht übersetzen\": the languages\n  the reader can read, kept on the device and sent with every article\n  request as keepLanguages. An article in one of them is answered as\n  written (translation \"skipped\") and no translation is started; a\n  later reader without that language gets the translation, from the\n  cached text, without asking Wikipedia again.\n- A finished translation keeps the original (description and\n  sections) beside it. The article screen shows a segmented switch\n  \"Deutsch | Original (Italienisch)\"; it opens on the original for a\n  language the reader keeps, on German otherwise.\n\nBuild 1694.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* Trip planner: a kept article is checked against Wikipedia''s revision once a day\n\nA kept article was read again only after a month, and then translated\nanew whether or not it had changed. Now it carries the page''s revision\nid. When somebody opens an article kept for more than a day, the\nserver asks Wikipedia for the revision id alone; only a changed id\nfetches the article again and, where it has to, translates it anew —\nin the background, so the reader gets the kept text at once and the\nnew one on the next opening. A failed check changes nothing; the\nmonth stays as the outer limit. The reader shows \"Stand: <date>\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw1urCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABMwQAGXyITe1ds4V/kXh7HxO9sRp\nP3Q4ofBNTqNrI6sxjltjPUx0o5X0LMl/GyIdCTcjX2/Uepz3kJaWy8Ybh05Bxdki\nMzdjRTKYhiXVibp9DGR3Ig0qZq2TwlMK3LB+J0170Afgi2opp6de+5laJGvWQKCl\nV6ybP4lpwjfzU/KghQF5ZYl8BxvVR7Z6Q2+o0fmpIMe+IT5PQf/bC6zuy8kxrgSU\nL6bR4nhi2oEbx02AWtI33zY2EqIr8SL195USmglXkStgYcpKGQAiArl//oAkMln2\nBV0rSGfv4PEQNxSTkIF2lOsUGFSH/hGn5/g4CloGjKJfK070zVorfqFpdURpSkQT\nXveDzgZzIvq43gXffRKDeChbmxLrbCs5zlqJPHI1mUeIePH4mkiTTVWXw+jurHaS\naSVDBg/fuS3jfxOiTWW4Ex1QekoF5QiXOdyTDwmLOP9yCFJcJ18RqARPNjGXRe/I\n/Wx6/oQGny5YaU3mL5qonOuBlhu/xZCQaBYFNIsUkFxWnxKxyK+y5uSwmL5cJIEi\nXsnNFjBb1eW5fm6V35dWCyJ2tYjNyiljGhWAMlrvPFH6b14qMmQCSHFoR21KTi/Z\n7zHnbfn/lWnmVG774en9wsT24dVABjWuSkm/h8yFEkFBb30YEtllNusDexs2a54u\nWU3q7H834Kb9H/pUxF2X\n=LFFY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T08:11:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/69be4d76676d0744dba3dfdccc4c4c1e4700ac9b","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDY5YmU0ZDc2Njc2ZDA3NDRkYmEzZGZkY2NjNGM0YzFlNDcwMGFjOWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/a364b07ff21ab3e24dd4daba313075080e3a6fd5","sha":"a364b07ff21ab3e24dd4daba313075080e3a6fd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/a364b07ff21ab3e24dd4daba313075080e3a6fd5"}],"sha":"69be4d76676d0744dba3dfdccc4c4c1e4700ac9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/69be4d76676d0744dba3dfdccc4c4c1e4700ac9b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/a364b07ff21ab3e24dd4daba313075080e3a6fd5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:33:36Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:33:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"iOS trip planner: leg strip as tall as the day strip, a pencil that reads as a button (#1447)\n\nFrom the device: the leg chips sat on a lower row than the day chips,\nand the pencil was a thin glyph. Both strips now share one chip height\n(48 pt) and the same vertical padding; a day''s \"not yet planned\" mark\nmoves beside the date so every day chip is two lines. The pencil is\ntitle-sized and semibold on its own disc, as tall as the chips.\n\nBuild 1693.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6b077c42318f1745e373ba80408fad80cd5933b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/6b077c42318f1745e373ba80408fad80cd5933b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/a364b07ff21ab3e24dd4daba313075080e3a6fd5","verification":{"payload":"tree 6b077c42318f1745e373ba80408fad80cd5933b1\nparent fc2582c600fa2594d42abd1648dec60dceb51f2d\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791185616 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791185616 +0200\n\niOS trip planner: leg strip as tall as the day strip, a pencil that reads as a button (#1447)\n\nFrom the device: the leg chips sat on a lower row than the day chips,\nand the pencil was a thin glyph. Both strips now share one chip height\n(48 pt) and the same vertical padding; a day''s \"not yet planned\" mark\nmoves beside the date so every day chip is two lines. The pencil is\ntitle-sized and semibold on its own disc, as tall as the chips.\n\nBuild 1693.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw1LQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAZMQAFqrdsuD3Q4eZ1Vn6w4rU0Ku\nvzhu0UyC9CCIaR3tGTd1qKkdrN7G59IANyoYk2/OwX/OSiARqekioygRvkRJCiMb\np5uL3iYoAp3C8Eqgs88Bo1TLdAI6TZiI535E0aCO5CvXXsDeNA6X+TDbRVngC299\nDXDDdthAoA0dyOox1O4M9TGToB5l7t7CcImQSRJd4JfRkepQyHB4tBcX0cnlzkc8\non7rIQx+V7GFHNJ/X6h4e2Vou3V1sGeZmb4PUechG1F7tAbTF/pDttiA6EC2KDmn\nYJ9OOalPuH51B+BiKw7U3HSdPftrlexEkrFb2WEae6HrUPVEc9cF5b1DVgs31aDU\nJWMLBU9vQ5hPo0xGNIR8if4Yo9ahbZEuh3bAROspQ5PyF3Mx8TS3p4DmDw3YnM2B\nkHOk2Lq7ioaTrB/X3WZ2Sy/4ofWgzcb68pSJ43PezH/QRZry359e/B2wuY3Vk+kA\nhD6r01nSI8CWEO2RyunmeCS9uY4oBnsGOtkiToiEyk7QQwj2rT28x7bKGRJp9/L3\nupZhJb0SdfqWZaRx9LlKzoACis2WnLCRkxob1QzySF07RrUhEntsv2U2Xeqe5UJQ\nrqfjximl3zX+PenlpTnmrHnPxQAIJ/tmX6ptCq5eax/3d1kg8UneHDJXyE58DpIa\nFgZN3Z8gHmYX57ign7L+\n=Hq0B\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T07:33:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/a364b07ff21ab3e24dd4daba313075080e3a6fd5","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKGEzNjRiMDdmZjIxYWIzZTI0ZGQ0ZGFiYTMxMzA3NTA4MGUzYTZmZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/fc2582c600fa2594d42abd1648dec60dceb51f2d","sha":"fc2582c600fa2594d42abd1648dec60dceb51f2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/fc2582c600fa2594d42abd1648dec60dceb51f2d"}],"sha":"a364b07ff21ab3e24dd4daba313075080e3a6fd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/a364b07ff21ab3e24dd4daba313075080e3a6fd5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/fc2582c600fa2594d42abd1648dec60dceb51f2d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:12:18Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:12:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Depot documents: one transaction from credit note and tax statement; security names (#1445)\n\n* Depot documents: combine a credit note and its tax statement into one transaction\n\nA bank sends two papers for one dividend: the credit note (quantity,\ngross, withholding tax, the amount before taxes) and the tax statement\n(the taxes withheld in Germany and the amount after them, which is what\nthe account is credited). They were read as unrelated documents.\n\nParser:\n- A statement in a foreign currency is converted at the rate it prints\n  (\"Devisenkurs EUR/USD ...\"); its net is the euro amount booked next to\n  the rate. The transaction then carries one currency, and Kurswert,\n  taxes and booking can be checked against each other.\n- taxPending: a credit note that prints \"Zu Ihren Gunsten vor Steuern\"\n  and no amount after taxes.\n- A footnote marker between a tax label and its amount (\"(1)\") is\n  skipped and never read as an amount; \"Devisenkurs\" is not a price;\n  a per-share amount printed in front of its label and \"zahlbar ab\"\n  are read.\n\nReader: the model''s answer in the foreign currency is converted at the\nsame printed rate before it is compared with the rules.\n\nEnrichment: a tax statement and a credit note awaiting one join the\ntransaction of the same security, kind and quantity (their amounts are\nbefore or after taxes, so they are not compared). The transaction then\ntakes its values from all documents linked to it: tax = credit note''s\ntax + tax statement''s, net = amount after taxes. A net confirmed by an\naccount booking is kept. The result is the same whichever document is\nread first.\n\nDialog: a credit note before taxes says so and labels its net\n\"Betrag vor Steuern\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n* Portfolio: security names from the bank''s holding first, never a label or a person\n\nPositions showed whatever name the last transaction carried. Names read\noff documents included the holding''s date column (\"per <date> <name>\"),\nlabels, and occasionally the holder''s name from the address block.\n\n- A position takes its name from the bank holding when there is one; a\n  transaction''s name only stands in when no holding names the security,\n  and the first fit one wins.\n- cleanSecurityName drops the date, quantity and identifier columns a\n  table row prints next to the name and rejects labels.\n- isPersonName: a name made of a user''s name is the address block, not\n  a security. Such names are neither stored nor shown.\n- The transaction list shows the cleaned name too, so names already\n  stored are fixed without touching the data.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n* Settlement parser: read tax tables that come out column by column\n\nText read off a scanned two-column table lists the labels with their\ncurrency (\"abgeführte Steuern EUR\") and the amounts later, one per line.\nThe amount pattern could reach across a line break, so a label took the\nfirst number of the next line: the amount after taxes became the one\nbefore, and a tax label on a later page added a year-to-date figure.\n\n- An amount never crosses a line break.\n- rejoinColumnAmounts puts a run of amount-only lines back after the\n  labels waiting for one, in order, when their numbers match.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n* Settlement parser: a credit note''s sub-heading and a date are no end and no amount\n\n- The settlement block ended at the next heading with a settlement word.\n  A credit note that repeats its kind above its figures (\"Abrechnung\n  Dividendengutschrift\") lost gross, tax, rate and net that way. A\n  heading now ends the block only once a final amount was printed.\n- A number that a date continues (\"01.01.26\") is never an amount, so a\n  per-share label followed by a fiscal-year range no longer reads the\n  day as the price; the amount printed in front of the label is used.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ed25abd118ccb1fedf8e5ffd7c052005bb8465bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/ed25abd118ccb1fedf8e5ffd7c052005bb8465bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/fc2582c600fa2594d42abd1648dec60dceb51f2d","verification":{"payload":"tree ed25abd118ccb1fedf8e5ffd7c052005bb8465bc\nparent ccbb40df9f4dc30028d2eae9a2bacadc8157e33e\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791184338 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791184338 +0200\n\nDepot documents: one transaction from credit note and tax statement; security names (#1445)\n\n* Depot documents: combine a credit note and its tax statement into one transaction\n\nA bank sends two papers for one dividend: the credit note (quantity,\ngross, withholding tax, the amount before taxes) and the tax statement\n(the taxes withheld in Germany and the amount after them, which is what\nthe account is credited). They were read as unrelated documents.\n\nParser:\n- A statement in a foreign currency is converted at the rate it prints\n  (\"Devisenkurs EUR/USD ...\"); its net is the euro amount booked next to\n  the rate. The transaction then carries one currency, and Kurswert,\n  taxes and booking can be checked against each other.\n- taxPending: a credit note that prints \"Zu Ihren Gunsten vor Steuern\"\n  and no amount after taxes.\n- A footnote marker between a tax label and its amount (\"(1)\") is\n  skipped and never read as an amount; \"Devisenkurs\" is not a price;\n  a per-share amount printed in front of its label and \"zahlbar ab\"\n  are read.\n\nReader: the model''s answer in the foreign currency is converted at the\nsame printed rate before it is compared with the rules.\n\nEnrichment: a tax statement and a credit note awaiting one join the\ntransaction of the same security, kind and quantity (their amounts are\nbefore or after taxes, so they are not compared). The transaction then\ntakes its values from all documents linked to it: tax = credit note''s\ntax + tax statement''s, net = amount after taxes. A net confirmed by an\naccount booking is kept. The result is the same whichever document is\nread first.\n\nDialog: a credit note before taxes says so and labels its net\n\"Betrag vor Steuern\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n* Portfolio: security names from the bank''s holding first, never a label or a person\n\nPositions showed whatever name the last transaction carried. Names read\noff documents included the holding''s date column (\"per <date> <name>\"),\nlabels, and occasionally the holder''s name from the address block.\n\n- A position takes its name from the bank holding when there is one; a\n  transaction''s name only stands in when no holding names the security,\n  and the first fit one wins.\n- cleanSecurityName drops the date, quantity and identifier columns a\n  table row prints next to the name and rejects labels.\n- isPersonName: a name made of a user''s name is the address block, not\n  a security. Such names are neither stored nor shown.\n- The transaction list shows the cleaned name too, so names already\n  stored are fixed without touching the data.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n* Settlement parser: read tax tables that come out column by column\n\nText read off a scanned two-column table lists the labels with their\ncurrency (\"abgeführte Steuern EUR\") and the amounts later, one per line.\nThe amount pattern could reach across a line break, so a label took the\nfirst number of the next line: the amount after taxes became the one\nbefore, and a tax label on a later page added a year-to-date figure.\n\n- An amount never crosses a line break.\n- rejoinColumnAmounts puts a run of amount-only lines back after the\n  labels waiting for one, in order, when their numbers match.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n* Settlement parser: a credit note''s sub-heading and a date are no end and no amount\n\n- The settlement block ended at the next heading with a settlement word.\n  A credit note that repeats its kind above its figures (\"Abrechnung\n  Dividendengutschrift\") lost gross, tax, rate and net that way. A\n  heading now ends the block only once a final amount was printed.\n- A number that a date continues (\"01.01.26\") is never an amount, so a\n  per-share label followed by a fiscal-year range no longer reads the\n  day as the price; the amount printed in front of the label is used.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw03SCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgGYQAFHpc2wRKyAfEH9cbSkadSOn\nnHbenCSR5SyJmroXsVErAlNPaxMXGJnbCp8dLJQcpZ1OwB4puGN8ks5s/hSVT3WR\nvnB5Kc1MWBXn3wj4cgIRtUl/SAZGHdisiJ0tG+CZA52IMKu96F6sWZpMc4KN+35X\nSrWO7JmvCGAKIZowSiBcKuIk+oSP45304vQxUFFk8VIsNieVcctj4sJ7SUMNXJKK\nSjSfQKDjqhp9zHQS2gom3cblLyr370cusuKmzKdnJgdghf06AF5sCQbLDt3oPbUq\nLDrF0RAp8ta7VaqFAdM0dCI8t2apOzpYW6G5BGPkYpXj4V0ChyDYW7mj6JWZK2WV\nvmBZ1gXYc7PvJYjwWdUOHhVcRmfygMa6BBbeflXkVpBCIekKT3ZdL36nV9L7/eNy\n/SoWth+sroui4YiiSFmrW7RR/TTo4+7cCREKCIVpuUJjER8Y06hx2inHicqA66Pk\n8BL4XFldKNyiTGqa910/paK5gg6Kt3iJ7Fd/heK+5zq//O3WZyzcov88lBg6NFg3\ncR8be0hyNwFEEXrNpOu7o0mXKJrktbXw2nCNNQPBQcEWk3rKE1TUtIvhA4j3ONwA\nqwK144Ny670m6++KiGi52Plp/OyFOli+zG4WuP/nibLabIkJzNLTFvH8uuX+hMp+\nlf25EJg6dD/VYm+qT+Yk\n=rv2f\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T07:12:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/fc2582c600fa2594d42abd1648dec60dceb51f2d","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKGZjMjU4MmM2MDBmYTI1OTRkNDJhYmQxNjQ4ZGVjNjBkY2ViNTFmMmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/ccbb40df9f4dc30028d2eae9a2bacadc8157e33e","sha":"ccbb40df9f4dc30028d2eae9a2bacadc8157e33e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/ccbb40df9f4dc30028d2eae9a2bacadc8157e33e"}],"sha":"fc2582c600fa2594d42abd1648dec60dceb51f2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/fc2582c600fa2594d42abd1648dec60dceb51f2d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/ccbb40df9f4dc30028d2eae9a2bacadc8157e33e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T06:38:59Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T06:38:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"iOS trip planner: a spot added from the leg sheet shows up at once (#1446)\n\n* iOS trip planner: a spot added from the leg sheet shows up at once\n\n\"Ort suchen\", \"Strecke anlegen\" and \"Strecken in der Nähe\" wrote to\nthe server and left the plan in memory as it was, so the leg''s\ncandidate count, the pool and the ballot showed the new spot only\nafter the next reload of the trip. The three screens now take an\nonChanged callback, called after every successful add; the leg sheet\nand the day''s \"Ort suchen\" row reload the plan with it.\n\nBuild 1692.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* iOS nearby routes: the change callback belongs to the view, not the model\n\nThe property landed in TripNearbyRoutesModel while the initialiser\nand the call sit in TripNearbyRoutesView; the iOS build failed on it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8696c15a696c953dbfb38aff1ad24b9683b68b4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/8696c15a696c953dbfb38aff1ad24b9683b68b4f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/ccbb40df9f4dc30028d2eae9a2bacadc8157e33e","verification":{"payload":"tree 8696c15a696c953dbfb38aff1ad24b9683b68b4f\nparent 8bd9b55ba65b7ecef53829f3d1cf4a495fad075d\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791182339 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791182339 +0200\n\niOS trip planner: a spot added from the leg sheet shows up at once (#1446)\n\n* iOS trip planner: a spot added from the leg sheet shows up at once\n\n\"Ort suchen\", \"Strecke anlegen\" and \"Strecken in der Nähe\" wrote to\nthe server and left the plan in memory as it was, so the leg''s\ncandidate count, the pool and the ballot showed the new spot only\nafter the next reload of the trip. The three screens now take an\nonChanged callback, called after every successful add; the leg sheet\nand the day''s \"Ort suchen\" row reload the plan with it.\n\nBuild 1692.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* iOS nearby routes: the change callback belongs to the view, not the model\n\nThe property landed in TripNearbyRoutesModel while the initialiser\nand the call sit in TripNearbyRoutesView; the iOS build failed on it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw0YDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8+AQAB/va52p5fi4N6RyVGsx1uRa\nYUlGAb8s8E0sMvowOCH9459esbh60QFWdLudeTJwKOTsw4ILrzFc8Q6zOSBLfEhm\nBsRYrhoW4Ak+9WIzrZ4p0iYRnh1N9MEzFW2q/rg9+ynYjJK/onEX/xen/BF6LRPS\ndxyBifLoID11UuDD/Gc/Kb58BzUPgIKAii8nyG1bwj25AD7xUTHldF/DY9b4eDa2\nS4uM2gLwiD/w+3u1eiT719M2InXEVFGIag6ngZQXiT9Y1zuF5KOhIo/+7g22d3cC\nrHSIugwnRPHzOXUOXiUNFZRwDfFOKfSFyxGKXEc79+6FIeI0mk+Hp5e9VzU1ZwPo\nTJG6+TSk0Vem373fcqw1Vs1mt81DX+GN5JNsjcCvMSlWFisJL5/0v/k3oPQlUU9M\nV4Ll23INp6tCPl6o81vHaXu8roLmhrprGFj3vP/ETgMR/YszKNdoCpt6k1HXgqx4\nYwICBcXe28c2nLTbdQzY++5nBziBj3WR7/rsuOEfW90Hvz54WgaRHLz7jqLJA598\nXjqEzUsI05WxNT12iLrZ+4D+8TR3gA4cq5tJxjd1/tXa96wXGjQ94ft3vu3j9fGS\nKaFt4kVTgAYCYR7nDqLZKA8uYeC39ptRL+H9uW435BqxePqB+tD0RvxRXkg0hcyj\nmKxSA1g5+LdVrVYJrKjw\n=59n0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T06:38:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/ccbb40df9f4dc30028d2eae9a2bacadc8157e33e","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKGNjYmI0MGRmOWY0ZGMzMDAyOGQyZWFlOWEyYmFjYWRjODE1N2UzM2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/8bd9b55ba65b7ecef53829f3d1cf4a495fad075d","sha":"8bd9b55ba65b7ecef53829f3d1cf4a495fad075d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/8bd9b55ba65b7ecef53829f3d1cf4a495fad075d"}],"sha":"ccbb40df9f4dc30028d2eae9a2bacadc8157e33e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/ccbb40df9f4dc30028d2eae9a2bacadc8157e33e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/8bd9b55ba65b7ecef53829f3d1cf4a495fad075d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T20:53:08Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T20:53:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Trip planner: device-test fixes, ballot map pins and the article in the app (§25, stages B and C) (#1443)\n\n* Trip planner: leg strip, leg header and journey days after the first device test\n\nStage A of §25 on a device turned up four things:\n\n- The city list opened as a sheet had no way out: it used to be\n  pushed, and the sheet also refused the swipe. It gets a \"Fertig\"\n  button and allows the swipe again (a list, not a form).\n- The leg chips were too thin to hit and the \"Etappen\" pencil sat at\n  the end of the scrolling strip, off-screen on a trip with several\n  legs. The chips are 44 pt tall now, the pencil is icon-only and fixed\n  at the trailing edge of the strip.\n- The leg header, the way into everything of the leg, was two footnote\n  lines in secondary grey with a caption-sized chevron. It is a card\n  with a primary first line and the chevron a list row has.\n- A journey''s day that nothing is planned into (aboard, by train, over\n  several nights) was drawn as a buffer day with \"Diesen Tag jetzt\n  planen\" and the hours up to the arrival as a block to fill. It is a\n  journey card now that says the day''s window. The journey''s own\n  departure and arrival fixpoints lose the x that did nothing: the\n  re-plan wrote them back. The server refuses removing them\n  (isJourneyEnd) and refuses detailing a journey''s frame day, instead\n  of quietly undoing both.\n\nBuild 1690.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* Trip planner: ballot map pins and the article in the app (§25, stages B and C)\n\nStage B — the ballot on the map:\n- Pins carry the category''s symbol on a light dot with my answer as a\n  coloured ring (TripSpotMapPin.ringTint); the legend draws rings too.\n  A blue disc with a question mark said only \"not voted yet\".\n- The sheet behind a pin shows the place under the vote row: map\n  snippet, name on the sign, OpenStreetMap name, route facts, \"Warum\n  hier?\", the article, \"Alle Details\" — no second tap on an info icon.\n- The spot''s map snippet (TripSpotMapSnippet, detail view and sheet)\n  zooms in place and opens the maps app from the settings via a\n  corner button; it was a static picture.\n\nStage C — the Wikipedia article in the app:\n- GET /trip-planner/wikipedia/article?url= (wiki-article.ts,\n  wikipedia-client.ts): the German article where Wikipedia''s language\n  links name one, otherwise the local one with a translation by the\n  llm-service section by section. The first answer is the original\n  with translation \"pending\"; the work runs on and the app asks again\n  until \"done\" or \"failed\". Kept per article for a month\n  (trip_wiki_articles, migration 0227). Pictures from the article''s\n  files via Commons, main image first, no flags, maps or vector files.\n- TripArticleView reads it: photo strip, description, sections,\n  translation banner, attribution (Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 4.0, machine\n  translation named), \"Weiterlesen\" when clipped. Reached from the\n  spot detail, the pin sheet and the ballot sheet instead of Safari.\n- askForJson takes an optional max_tokens.\n\nBuild 1691. Docs: §25.3 and §25.4.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"814305be68b8b73b5bae06da2ef7ef2c5b124919","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/814305be68b8b73b5bae06da2ef7ef2c5b124919"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/8bd9b55ba65b7ecef53829f3d1cf4a495fad075d","verification":{"payload":"tree 814305be68b8b73b5bae06da2ef7ef2c5b124919\nparent c28bb166ba334018d9396def9c99d83e5f571add\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791147188 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791147188 +0200\n\nTrip planner: device-test fixes, ballot map pins and the article in the app (§25, stages B and C) (#1443)\n\n* Trip planner: leg strip, leg header and journey days after the first device test\n\nStage A of §25 on a device turned up four things:\n\n- The city list opened as a sheet had no way out: it used to be\n  pushed, and the sheet also refused the swipe. It gets a \"Fertig\"\n  button and allows the swipe again (a list, not a form).\n- The leg chips were too thin to hit and the \"Etappen\" pencil sat at\n  the end of the scrolling strip, off-screen on a trip with several\n  legs. The chips are 44 pt tall now, the pencil is icon-only and fixed\n  at the trailing edge of the strip.\n- The leg header, the way into everything of the leg, was two footnote\n  lines in secondary grey with a caption-sized chevron. It is a card\n  with a primary first line and the chevron a list row has.\n- A journey''s day that nothing is planned into (aboard, by train, over\n  several nights) was drawn as a buffer day with \"Diesen Tag jetzt\n  planen\" and the hours up to the arrival as a block to fill. It is a\n  journey card now that says the day''s window. The journey''s own\n  departure and arrival fixpoints lose the x that did nothing: the\n  re-plan wrote them back. The server refuses removing them\n  (isJourneyEnd) and refuses detailing a journey''s frame day, instead\n  of quietly undoing both.\n\nBuild 1690.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* Trip planner: ballot map pins and the article in the app (§25, stages B and C)\n\nStage B — the ballot on the map:\n- Pins carry the category''s symbol on a light dot with my answer as a\n  coloured ring (TripSpotMapPin.ringTint); the legend draws rings too.\n  A blue disc with a question mark said only \"not voted yet\".\n- The sheet behind a pin shows the place under the vote row: map\n  snippet, name on the sign, OpenStreetMap name, route facts, \"Warum\n  hier?\", the article, \"Alle Details\" — no second tap on an info icon.\n- The spot''s map snippet (TripSpotMapSnippet, detail view and sheet)\n  zooms in place and opens the maps app from the settings via a\n  corner button; it was a static picture.\n\nStage C — the Wikipedia article in the app:\n- GET /trip-planner/wikipedia/article?url= (wiki-article.ts,\n  wikipedia-client.ts): the German article where Wikipedia''s language\n  links name one, otherwise the local one with a translation by the\n  llm-service section by section. The first answer is the original\n  with translation \"pending\"; the work runs on and the app asks again\n  until \"done\" or \"failed\". Kept per article for a month\n  (trip_wiki_articles, migration 0227). Pictures from the article''s\n  files via Commons, main image first, no flags, maps or vector files.\n- TripArticleView reads it: photo strip, description, sections,\n  translation banner, attribution (Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 4.0, machine\n  translation named), \"Weiterlesen\" when clipped. Reached from the\n  spot detail, the pin sheet and the ballot sheet instead of Safari.\n- askForJson takes an optional max_tokens.\n\nBuild 1691. Docs: §25.3 and §25.4.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwry0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfPQQAHFql1FSUYIjyrrcgpcW1cGF\nmoAVqCLEXVm8o3Eeb+LKZApoFcpyH5TRx8KBWTU0GvvCIBgZKlOnz3MD04CXdJ/W\nxRYlXaxhgGNKc39I2AxPsUUwGnvxM65lbCCMTP0m/nxxjokYv9qtV5KAhC6o3Eav\nwj+tvgL1cz7qvjcDfaBuwcUdR4fvXGdRiT/YrXo1jDHstG21Aorcc9w8PW7JRkCR\nPv2QehKabHsEGlV3CRgp6JjfnrDTZB7HMr9yy2rK2nE0DidVWNduCxEpNWswArJ/\nnGYjz8mSqWA+Uhl1eYScj7SqbgxvFIMKKNqhZuI/Xqdo9TjHn7O0N/nZJB+nRThW\nFPhdiYZRpSDfpKy/R9+91ueNzk9LeO7l2EdwgGDLofY2anC5y7VuBV6Hm81oJr7D\nOC8DVoryF8T8s3Tl4HN3heTwn/KtpceFqmCT8iPqxsS+7W5KvEJDTEUHTCByFLYC\nXliEFGWGWoyAXh3DH/vzeuK+U1/ZJO6Y1bDWjEsUrhQ7Xx4ZIi5pIUSGq6ZyJraV\n8w/kvFXygc07o7yBBE1gNvlxJ+R7RKKq11wLXf6tR2wcaJZ8WaUnj65cSxAq17pE\npjACJSQlVB3d7D2YCpLx83MX3e6NwmJ6wW+W/Qarz029eE4rD3fZyL+bJqXLrxBm\n+oMMFz3pQ2oz4goRF83u\n=O5uN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T20:53:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/8bd9b55ba65b7ecef53829f3d1cf4a495fad075d","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDhiZDliNTViYTY1YjdlY2VmNTM4MjlmM2QxY2Y0YTQ5NWZhZDA3NWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/c28bb166ba334018d9396def9c99d83e5f571add","sha":"c28bb166ba334018d9396def9c99d83e5f571add","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/c28bb166ba334018d9396def9c99d83e5f571add"}],"sha":"8bd9b55ba65b7ecef53829f3d1cf4a495fad075d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/8bd9b55ba65b7ecef53829f3d1cf4a495fad075d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/c28bb166ba334018d9396def9c99d83e5f571add/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T20:47:34Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T20:47:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Depot documents: a tax statement only adds its tax to an existing transaction (#1444)\n\nA broker''s tax statement on its own (\"Steuerliche Behandlung: ...\") prints\nthe quantity and the amounts before and after taxes, but no price,\nKurswert or charges. It was read like a settlement: the amount before\ntaxes became the net, and the tax was summed from every tax word on the\npage, including the rates in its footnotes.\n\nParser:\n- looksLikeTaxStatement: \"Steuerliche Behandlung\" with no settlement\n  heading and no Kurswert elsewhere. A settlement with its tax statement\n  appended is still a settlement.\n- On a tax statement, gross is the amount before taxes, net the one\n  after, price and fees are not read, the date is the one its heading\n  names, and the tax is the printed total or else before minus after.\n- OCR tolerance: \"Steuem\" for \"Steuern\", and underline runs between a\n  label and its amount are dropped.\n- A number followed by \"%\" is never an amount; \"...steuersatz\" and\n  credited withholding tax no longer count as tax lines.\n\nEnrichment:\n- A tax statement never creates a transaction. It finds the one of the\n  same security, kind and quantity within the window, fills in the tax\n  when the row has none, and links itself. Without such a row the outcome\n  is the new \"no_transaction\".\n- The model calling it \"no settlement\" no longer rejects it.\n\nDialog: its own headline, \"Betrag vor/nach Steuern\" rows, and outcome\ntexts for tax statements.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7a4ebb79320aab0e1461ff187dbd7a63140da506","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/7a4ebb79320aab0e1461ff187dbd7a63140da506"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/c28bb166ba334018d9396def9c99d83e5f571add","verification":{"payload":"tree 7a4ebb79320aab0e1461ff187dbd7a63140da506\nparent 52b9d7c7fe10c3ca625ec4f9dcf33708604f80b0\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791146854 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791146854 +0200\n\nDepot documents: a tax statement only adds its tax to an existing transaction (#1444)\n\nA broker''s tax statement on its own (\"Steuerliche Behandlung: ...\") prints\nthe quantity and the amounts before and after taxes, but no price,\nKurswert or charges. It was read like a settlement: the amount before\ntaxes became the net, and the tax was summed from every tax word on the\npage, including the rates in its footnotes.\n\nParser:\n- looksLikeTaxStatement: \"Steuerliche Behandlung\" with no settlement\n  heading and no Kurswert elsewhere. A settlement with its tax statement\n  appended is still a settlement.\n- On a tax statement, gross is the amount before taxes, net the one\n  after, price and fees are not read, the date is the one its heading\n  names, and the tax is the printed total or else before minus after.\n- OCR tolerance: \"Steuem\" for \"Steuern\", and underline runs between a\n  label and its amount are dropped.\n- A number followed by \"%\" is never an amount; \"...steuersatz\" and\n  credited withholding tax no longer count as tax lines.\n\nEnrichment:\n- A tax statement never creates a transaction. It finds the one of the\n  same security, kind and quantity within the window, fills in the tax\n  when the row has none, and links itself. Without such a row the outcome\n  is the new \"no_transaction\".\n- The model calling it \"no settlement\" no longer rejects it.\n\nDialog: its own headline, \"Betrag vor/nach Steuern\" rows, and outcome\ntexts for tax statements.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwrtmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMi8QAGRI32PM+fhxTnwln