comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T19:23:35Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T19:23:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Trip planner: three levels, three places (§25, stage A) (#1441)\n\nThe day screen''s menu had grown to nineteen entries in four groups,\nand the groups did not follow what somebody is working on: \"Diese\nReise\" held the leg''s candidates and ballot next to the trip''s cities\nand settings, and the trip''s structure was one entry among many\nalthough the strip at the top already shows it. The planner has three\nlevels — trip, leg, day — and the middle one had no place of its own.\n\n- Trip: the leg strip is always shown and ends with \"Etappen\", the\n  structure editor (`TripLegsView`); the menu is now \"Reise\" and holds\n  only what belongs to the whole trip (settings, planners, travellers,\n  documents, journal, readiness, review, offline).\n- Leg: a tap on the leg header opens `TripLegSheet` — the leg itself\n  (edit), \"Hinzufügen\" (place search, route entry, nearby routes,\n  ideas) and \"Vorrat\" (candidates, ballot, day trip). A journey opens\n  the same sheet with its own editor.\n- Day: \"Abendlicht\" moves from the menu into the day''s frame, next to\n  the fixed times and the outing.\n- A new trip asks only for what it needs to exist: name, first place,\n  length and date, transport mode. Further legs, journeys, pace, group\n  and interests are done afterwards where they are changed later; the\n  sentence interpreter and the interest toggles leave the form.\n- Concept §25 records the rule, the table of where each former menu\n  entry went, and what stages B (ballot map) and C (Wikipedia) will do.\n\nBuild 1689.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3f1236b95a2405ea965252e164fbf67e7768916d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/3f1236b95a2405ea965252e164fbf67e7768916d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/2a2a2444e69a4fb87f1d936bdcaefd30acab1d9e","verification":{"payload":"tree 3f1236b95a2405ea965252e164fbf67e7768916d\nparent 1f0368cd4465f0eea2337f3368770065c8d63b16\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791141815 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791141815 +0200\n\nTrip planner: three levels, three places (§25, stage A) (#1441)\n\nThe day screen''s menu had grown to nineteen entries in four groups,\nand the groups did not follow what somebody is working on: \"Diese\nReise\" held the leg''s candidates and ballot next to the trip''s cities\nand settings, and the trip''s structure was one entry among many\nalthough the strip at the top already shows it. The planner has three\nlevels — trip, leg, day — and the middle one had no place of its own.\n\n- Trip: the leg strip is always shown and ends with \"Etappen\", the\n  structure editor (`TripLegsView`); the menu is now \"Reise\" and holds\n  only what belongs to the whole trip (settings, planners, travellers,\n  documents, journal, readiness, review, offline).\n- Leg: a tap on the leg header opens `TripLegSheet` — the leg itself\n  (edit), \"Hinzufügen\" (place search, route entry, nearby routes,\n  ideas) and \"Vorrat\" (candidates, ballot, day trip). A journey opens\n  the same sheet with its own editor.\n- Day: \"Abendlicht\" moves from the menu into the day''s frame, next to\n  the fixed times and the outing.\n- A new trip asks only for what it needs to exist: name, first place,\n  length and date, transport mode. Further legs, journeys, pace, group\n  and interests are done afterwards where they are changed later; the\n  sentence interpreter and the interest toggles leave the form.\n- Concept §25 records the rule, the table of where each former menu\n  entry went, and what stages B (ballot map) and C (Wikipedia) will do.\n\nBuild 1689.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwqe3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACrAQAKM3f2uC8kydkEi4uweJwvfd\n2S3oCZ7eMoszVfMyy0om0nOZLqGKn0jobmgzzVhgniHN1PA/jkAwArEKaxKdMb5g\nTkM4j0+MeZemqOFX33f5uLgqpGP2rxXjIMkRe8gQS7mqTsrDG3dra6rzEpeuVtpI\njOfWVzWVOkURnn5cbU945RN1VpN6gl9oQMnM24r6lrWEp6IMaIQ10BLwwMtjq64O\nli1gpyOZTLFEd7u+ZsImsifR/qo7Zi9NiaMsB/fIcWkLE1/DPOq39XmLQCqKsa7Y\nbUEqfgZqClr4OIVbznl8atFb4Rcoil9DwRVJG3ux+HLppvs/i+sPcBIdmHIjGjBa\n/1l3ly5kA/cMa1gHgVySJkbmtEqYVT4FslzhUAe82HfFg2oUe54GM/5A6zflsgGt\n4ig5Ctvu7oSCEsmBEupFu/Wc5RuCXhBg4SYzdP43pdxK/vijg6HV4oaQPNKdzbN6\njyXkuFZUJvMJ2Lq90T0wYjTn/5VqmUbODre5mgVSgZN4ZVUd9sJrnPqXJXKZFdnZ\n5xkvHZXosXdA2aUmtGKnGwDpgQbnsVlTb2bZGPRQ9vT9BSzWHTFqXmR4ZS1m3i8B\ncEJhXBWyhcTtKeVneYV7/Q/qlRRk6qpzfuq+RxIRQw2EUqAn1WtrJjjFu06cazS2\nX1jQ039mHR9L5w2HqrtC\n=lAyi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T19:23:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/2a2a2444e69a4fb87f1d936bdcaefd30acab1d9e","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDJhMmEyNDQ0ZTY5YTRmYjg3ZjFkOTM2YmRjYWVmZDMwYWNhYjFkOWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/1f0368cd4465f0eea2337f3368770065c8d63b16","sha":"1f0368cd4465f0eea2337f3368770065c8d63b16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/1f0368cd4465f0eea2337f3368770065c8d63b16"}],"sha":"2a2a2444e69a4fb87f1d936bdcaefd30acab1d9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/2a2a2444e69a4fb87f1d936bdcaefd30acab1d9e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/1f0368cd4465f0eea2337f3368770065c8d63b16/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T16:31:13Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T16:31:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"iOS city list: no swipe-away on any form page, add-city date prefilled, rows aligned (#1440)\n\n* iOS city list: no swipe-away on any form page, add-city date prefilled, rows aligned\n\nFrom the walk-through:\n\n- The add-city sheet could be swiped away, and from the \"Fortbewegung\"\n  page inside it a swipe closed the whole form. The lock sits on each\n  sheet''s NavigationStack now (city, journey, add-city, and the day\n  view''s edit sheet), and the mode page says it too, because the lock\n  on a sheet''s root does not reach a pushed page.\n- Adding a city asks for its first day, prefilled with the day after\n  the trip so far — the day after the last place''s last day, or the day\n  a closing journey arrives (`TripTransitSlots.nextDay`). Sent only when\n  dated; an undated trip leaves it to the trip. `TripDraftLegView` takes\n  an `extra` section for it.\n- Journeys sit on the same level as the places in the city list — a leg\n  of its own with its own icon, not a sub-item — and the row separators\n  run from the row''s leading edge instead of the first text.\n\nBuild 1688.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* Trip planner: list the planners owner-first, deterministically\n\n`syncPlanners` wrote the accounts'' traveller rows in one statement, so\nthey shared a `created_at` and the list fell back to ordering by id —\nwhich was whatever order `WHERE id IN (…)` happened to return. On some\nruns the invitee came back before the owner, and\n`travellers.test.ts` failed on an unrelated PR. The rows are now written\nowner first, then the invitations in the order they were made.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"87b411cb449edb229bcb88c585d29e82fafd9f8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/87b411cb449edb229bcb88c585d29e82fafd9f8a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/1f0368cd4465f0eea2337f3368770065c8d63b16","verification":{"payload":"tree 87b411cb449edb229bcb88c585d29e82fafd9f8a\nparent 6aeebb55a8c24d78959c12a31c47b049244af49c\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791131473 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791131473 +0200\n\niOS city list: no swipe-away on any form page, add-city date prefilled, rows aligned (#1440)\n\n* iOS city list: no swipe-away on any form page, add-city date prefilled, rows aligned\n\nFrom the walk-through:\n\n- The add-city sheet could be swiped away, and from the \"Fortbewegung\"\n  page inside it a swipe closed the whole form. The lock sits on each\n  sheet''s NavigationStack now (city, journey, add-city, and the day\n  view''s edit sheet), and the mode page says it too, because the lock\n  on a sheet''s root does not reach a pushed page.\n- Adding a city asks for its first day, prefilled with the day after\n  the trip so far — the day after the last place''s last day, or the day\n  a closing journey arrives (`TripTransitSlots.nextDay`). Sent only when\n  dated; an undated trip leaves it to the trip. `TripDraftLegView` takes\n  an `extra` section for it.\n- Journeys sit on the same level as the places in the city list — a leg\n  of its own with its own icon, not a sub-item — and the row separators\n  run from the row''s leading edge instead of the first text.\n\nBuild 1688.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* Trip planner: list the planners owner-first, deterministically\n\n`syncPlanners` wrote the accounts'' traveller rows in one statement, so\nthey shared a `created_at` and the list fell back to ordering by id —\nwhich was whatever order `WHERE id IN (…)` happened to return. On some\nruns the invitee came back before the owner, and\n`travellers.test.ts` failed on an unrelated PR. The rows are now written\nowner first, then the invitations in the order they were made.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwn9RCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWA4QAJbo9/WnUtVv5pM6HD8iTTo1\ngGqa882iNV7bYQgn47gxlyPL7WY+rNw0uak8BeGpJtcWXpBj0382DJhIPrTGqLEm\n9szWC4pWXfe7rAmkGKQho7UlCaBbFZJcLRrs52XNJw6GAl5ae/3kDVlrJRplMVOO\nZjpSxg3Z525WObVfsXsOSAoAxqknsdQ7zbn7Hqass/zdcJdjEsnLAIS/dj1dwgDV\nX8DnRlhNpN0sercn5DqTJsW4QFq/8bplpTmMlmac7HnQ4Ycy90AHvOSyTJfDLNpt\nLzBA7u2FlOWPBCQ3LJimI3xA552yIpA4WP9gv2SpEjbkefAytt45JkoamdX4/sOQ\nKbB2G8vWDuw5u2VPUey1ZSUY6p+52p3a2hRoVUjw/ftAeZC9V66X3elVTMTXg46O\nvVPregJYZ9RmYoEFbW/0JtQgAKXVOOHaD2H6C9bTyHdMeZF98U91kpM/PUCGPBwy\nYrGmiecFQvpJwq5KUZko89MP1XhMYjmp2J0Ci+aLWxo5RrxMYxoxsBaxd0bORQii\n5bfSBbM0FewA250F6lakRV9FVs+CuJ+UEd25XImBn+8iorGM6JNM2IZ9OnHWcyol\n8ACtQj5XGAfZmnDyyII4ZU8ZwKIwLY5ugWCjghulXRY5JTxeUIrE/f44E7yHJKGE\n/lLqEd51e4rhqYga2XXv\n=oH9/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T16:31:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/1f0368cd4465f0eea2337f3368770065c8d63b16","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDFmMDM2OGNkNDQ2NWYwZWVhMjMzN2YzMzY4NzcwMDY1YzhkNjNiMTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/6aeebb55a8c24d78959c12a31c47b049244af49c","sha":"6aeebb55a8c24d78959c12a31c47b049244af49c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/6aeebb55a8c24d78959c12a31c47b049244af49c"}],"sha":"1f0368cd4465f0eea2337f3368770065c8d63b16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/1f0368cd4465f0eea2337f3368770065c8d63b16"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/6aeebb55a8c24d78959c12a31c47b049244af49c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T09:35:11Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T09:35:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Trip planner: the corridor follows the roads; city forms ask only for the arrival (#1439)\n\n* Trip planner: the corridor follows the roads the router knows\n\nThe corridor was an ellipse with the two ends as foci: for a day''s drive\na band a few kilometres wide around the straight line, which is not\nwhere the motorway runs. The candidates for a journey sat on the line\nbetween the two cities and not on the way anybody drives (§24, stage 2).\n\n- Router: `routes()` asks Valhalla for the way and up to two\n  alternatives (`alternates`) and reads every road that comes back with\n  a shape; `polyline.ts` decodes them (six places, as Valhalla writes).\n- Geo: `POST /pois/search` takes `path` — a line and a width — and\n  answers with what lies within the width of the road, the detour as\n  twice the distance to the line. Envelope first for the GiST index.\n- Corridor: with a mode and a reachable router the search runs along\n  each road, half the detour budget wide, in every region the roads\n  cross; what comes back is measured at the router (origin → stop,\n  stop → destination, two matrices over at most 120 candidates), sorted\n  by that driven detour and dropped past the budget. Without a router\n  the ellipse serves as before; the endpoint says which with `source`.\n- The transit leg''s pool is built the same way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* iOS city forms: only the arrival; the way here is a journey\n\n\"Die Fahrt dorthin\" on the city form asked for a departure from the\ncity before and an arrival — the old transfer (§4.2) — next to the\njourney that has existed since §22.7, and nobody could tell which to\nuse for a longer drive. The form now asks only when the group arrives,\nand says that the drive itself — departure, duration, places on the\nway — is a journey added in the city list. The city edit footer says\nthe same. Build 1687.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* geo: the path test expects the museum past the destination\n\nWithin the width of the road''s end, as it was within the ellipse; the\nsearch was right and the expectation was not.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1c2fc83b2448547cfa2d24d7fadfff06c57d2565","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/1c2fc83b2448547cfa2d24d7fadfff06c57d2565"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/6aeebb55a8c24d78959c12a31c47b049244af49c","verification":{"payload":"tree 1c2fc83b2448547cfa2d24d7fadfff06c57d2565\nparent 3f7fc0f1c83608e65b0ff1344fc0783ed2f52b52\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791106511 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791106511 +0200\n\nTrip planner: the corridor follows the roads; city forms ask only for the arrival (#1439)\n\n* Trip planner: the corridor follows the roads the router knows\n\nThe corridor was an ellipse with the two ends as foci: for a day''s drive\na band a few kilometres wide around the straight line, which is not\nwhere the motorway runs. The candidates for a journey sat on the line\nbetween the two cities and not on the way anybody drives (§24, stage 2).\n\n- Router: `routes()` asks Valhalla for the way and up to two\n  alternatives (`alternates`) and reads every road that comes back with\n  a shape; `polyline.ts` decodes them (six places, as Valhalla writes).\n- Geo: `POST /pois/search` takes `path` — a line and a width — and\n  answers with what lies within the width of the road, the detour as\n  twice the distance to the line. Envelope first for the GiST index.\n- Corridor: with a mode and a reachable router the search runs along\n  each road, half the detour budget wide, in every region the roads\n  cross; what comes back is measured at the router (origin → stop,\n  stop → destination, two matrices over at most 120 candidates), sorted\n  by that driven detour and dropped past the budget. Without a router\n  the ellipse serves as before; the endpoint says which with `source`.\n- The transit leg''s pool is built the same way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* iOS city forms: only the arrival; the way here is a journey\n\n\"Die Fahrt dorthin\" on the city form asked for a departure from the\ncity before and an arrival — the old transfer (§4.2) — next to the\njourney that has existed since §22.7, and nobody could tell which to\nuse for a longer drive. The form now asks only when the group arrives,\nand says that the drive itself — departure, duration, places on the\nway — is a journey added in the city list. The city edit footer says\nthe same. Build 1687.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* geo: the path test expects the museum past the destination\n\nWithin the width of the road''s end, as it was within the ellipse; the\nsearch was right and the expectation was not.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwh3PCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbXUQAFNCR5UWBMrhOHCVk5AwoIfM\n9BC/cKL3Heud6LnbBMYi39D/WgugFQnMIYq5+Cq1ah9CdIrCVDpyysvjhrF5PN49\nDHKYcE2v0mAlxKUhNVASJ/lJyzTavpp7vpmM+TcUUaj9ocSV+3PaniW6/KyGOV7b\niK2tX2xVADQaCn97GWMkbw4bDDp1rcY/2haQ/fP1m8hie5HMDaSX7DyOsiwHzmjO\ngrCfNLGSRsAPWpj9g84rsYFzuLVZOttDMGyFlI0ONR4QHP5bpRGdBMr12OIxS2XT\nSsI48ORoRd2/V2C5WLjO9qxy4UkxW+FbKVBkv9dxRFW50XXEP7ifHcLQNa5T34fw\nm3gN3dNAnnsnVmA4rZXZ9QecudpfXno3T0qHJu7CE6Wg9RV1pwjjPAk52i7ouXUK\n3io8aMENAsSYcgn1ah3329isgh7F1AIdh0pC1mWxx1jg8KwTSQp85bg/2Sxvfdch\nr/ENe7e/fP4mCH9v2j0bMytKM9ol9LVlLciEiWnQ5XQaLLCMRvIUEPpblLh/TeuK\nb0fU0mVeCN6VGfaLa5MI9ZDrHGEesripK5EyqoDcLDV4jv7zcAjlPlhrpWtrYNmE\nEpRqTpxjfYb5A466ppO+A1GT5jGmKOCnOINlm1LwVALEuaUQ4/xBTopwwFRiLOuK\n3sQuTsbopNFWEo2OgLOm\n=pp0F\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T09:35:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/6aeebb55a8c24d78959c12a31c47b049244af49c","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDZhZWViYjU1YThjMjRkNzg5NTljMTJhMzFjNDdiMDQ5MjQ0YWY0OWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/3f7fc0f1c83608e65b0ff1344fc0783ed2f52b52","sha":"3f7fc0f1c83608e65b0ff1344fc0783ed2f52b52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/3f7fc0f1c83608e65b0ff1344fc0783ed2f52b52"}],"sha":"6aeebb55a8c24d78959c12a31c47b049244af49c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/6aeebb55a8c24d78959c12a31c47b049244af49c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/3f7fc0f1c83608e65b0ff1344fc0783ed2f52b52/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T09:16:36Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T09:16:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Trip planner: interest ticks become a filter with \"Alles andere\"; journey buttons say why they are blocked (#1438)\n\n* Trip planner: the interest ticks are a filter, with \"Alles andere\"\n\n\"Was zählt auf dieser Reise?\" read backwards: nothing ticked was the\nneutral state, a tick gave +2 and excluded nothing, and next to it the\nsentence interpreter''s category list narrowed the search with nothing\non screen to say so.\n\nNow ticked is searched and unticked is not. Every line is on to begin\nwith, and a sixteenth line \"Alles andere\" stands for what none of the\nfifteen names, so a filter over a short vocabulary does not silently\ndrop the bridge and the square. Nothing ticked and everything ticked\nboth mean everything (`selectionOf` → null); the bonus is gone and\n\"ihr wolltet: …\" is said only when the selection is narrowed; words\noutside the vocabulary are ignored rather than matched against nothing.\nThe interpreter''s categories become ticks (`interestsForCategories`)\nand are no longer applied in the search. Migration 0225 clears ticks\nand categories on existing trips so they keep searching everything,\nwhich is what their screen now says.\n\niOS: header \"Wonach gesucht wird\", footer explains the filter, all\nlines on by default on both screens. Build 1686.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* iOS city list: say why a journey cannot be made yet, before the screen opens\n\nFrom the walk-through: once some places of a trip are dated, a journey\nwhose neighbour has no date is refused on save (\"eine Weiterreise hat\nein Datum — erst der Reise Daten geben …\") — after the two moments were\ntyped. The three \"einfügen\" buttons now ask `TripTransitSlots.blocker`\nfirst and, when a place the journey touches has no date, stay disabled\nwith that reason under them, naming the place. An undated trip still\ntakes its dates from the journey, so nothing blocks there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b4a4b1cedb402ac5b96b10a45bfef2bb768d2b25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/b4a4b1cedb402ac5b96b10a45bfef2bb768d2b25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/3f7fc0f1c83608e65b0ff1344fc0783ed2f52b52","verification":{"payload":"tree b4a4b1cedb402ac5b96b10a45bfef2bb768d2b25\nparent ed3edb76d329501c50d6427f753ba7cf2adb7f3e\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791105396 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791105396 +0200\n\nTrip planner: interest ticks become a filter with \"Alles andere\"; journey buttons say why they are blocked (#1438)\n\n* Trip planner: the interest ticks are a filter, with \"Alles andere\"\n\n\"Was zählt auf dieser Reise?\" read backwards: nothing ticked was the\nneutral state, a tick gave +2 and excluded nothing, and next to it the\nsentence interpreter''s category list narrowed the search with nothing\non screen to say so.\n\nNow ticked is searched and unticked is not. Every line is on to begin\nwith, and a sixteenth line \"Alles andere\" stands for what none of the\nfifteen names, so a filter over a short vocabulary does not silently\ndrop the bridge and the square. Nothing ticked and everything ticked\nboth mean everything (`selectionOf` → null); the bonus is gone and\n\"ihr wolltet: …\" is said only when the selection is narrowed; words\noutside the vocabulary are ignored rather than matched against nothing.\nThe interpreter''s categories become ticks (`interestsForCategories`)\nand are no longer applied in the search. Migration 0225 clears ticks\nand categories on existing trips so they keep searching everything,\nwhich is what their screen now says.\n\niOS: header \"Wonach gesucht wird\", footer explains the filter, all\nlines on by default on both screens. Build 1686.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* iOS city list: say why a journey cannot be made yet, before the screen opens\n\nFrom the walk-through: once some places of a trip are dated, a journey\nwhose neighbour has no date is refused on save (\"eine Weiterreise hat\nein Datum — erst der Reise Daten geben …\") — after the two moments were\ntyped. The three \"einfügen\" buttons now ask `TripTransitSlots.blocker`\nfirst and, when a place the journey touches has no date, stay disabled\nwith that reason under them, naming the place. An undated trip still\ntakes its dates from the journey, so nothing blocks there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwhl0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7rQQAAQvka4IgBcF06xC6ZSdUw+i\njjbDdSkVZV3Y4y7rgFE1h9BAFH2pnHkYnNDU81mIbBDmQHnYWB0rT46nQ/zbfHah\nrDUgaqyI2MvXRXRJ7C+jC9nwVLEDjQbG4w3UiozVUZeBDYbnajaAgNABpWe8Ii1V\n1OPxyNgRjakuHvUOky10SWkKYmuApQ7wGFqgTwfFxznyRctr2hvjY7u6YwKPw2lU\nnd8G0AuCVugk6xtmHzbCLacoXZY24g7/1a8LJe/23PFZe9uoKRWt/rUxNbJmYu5i\nZywieLD4csJu3/goXKkitsM2WZIB3gueDsp2zmTa3wrfw9GJr6MyS/Q/QqSU/fsG\npeI62+vwptBIttMFUdMIJOp6PF7BXEKP1ej8tBvRy378GSel1hkpw9gfyJpuyMbi\nEdUNffmhMhbTjqJBNbv11AvcTubDTGka4wpc7HdEg4NrSpEspwm8bKdM6dphaQ6J\nHElJKbaT5sKSSbfzKIXi5wYSBM+HIEUlV72FB2QQhO0foNRGwpPC2SFfinAjV6u3\n4j2GKRoEVNldoMJ6eSgk9euqoJ/FTL3qbj6BHp4vrMVyd/e6MTOZogU89Piu3tsX\naKUQN/s7pSA+u9o2gFmZXC5sYQp9rvHep+Lp0HMGlH6W1Me9W5nx0u3A+dw3Brsm\nGoEKOtTdpET/8wLpoNwe\n=4ef7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T09:16:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/3f7fc0f1c8360