lost on the way back:\n  `onAppear` prefilled the journey again and overwrote it. Prefill once.\n- The picker row grew to two lines because `LabeledContent` wraps its\n  value under the title when the two do not fit; a plain HStack keeps it\n  to one line, the choice lives on its own page anyway.\n- On the choice page the hint now sits in the label''s title column,\n  flush with the mode name, and the separator runs from the icon.\n- The journey sheet and the city sheet can no longer be swiped away:\n  typed moments must not vanish without asking; \"Abbrechen\" is a tap.\n- Rows in the city list get a little more air between title, caption\n  and the small notes under them.\n\nBuild 1685.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4ce7f0ab09af404753b3f20306799e223c079578","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/4ce7f0ab09af404753b3f20306799e223c079578"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/ed3edb76d329501c50d6427f753ba7cf2adb7f3e","verification":{"payload":"tree 4ce7f0ab09af404753b3f20306799e223c079578\nparent 51447988fc006fdfbacee8b1b3365490ae51d02f\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791103565 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791103565 +0200\n\niOS journey screen: keep the chosen mode, one-line picker row, no swipe-away (#1437)\n\nFrom the cruise walk-through:\n\n- Choosing a mode on the \"Fortbewegung\" page was lost on the way back:\n  `onAppear` prefilled the journey again and overwrote it. Prefill once.\n- The picker row grew to two lines because `LabeledContent` wraps its\n  value under the title when the two do not fit; a plain HStack keeps it\n  to one line, the choice lives on its own page anyway.\n- On the choice page the hint now sits in the label''s title column,\n  flush with the mode name, and the separator runs from the icon.\n- The journey sheet and the city sheet can no longer be swiped away:\n  typed moments must not vanish without asking; \"Abbrechen\" is a tap.\n- Rows in the city list get a little more air between title, caption\n  and the small notes under them.\n\nBuild 1685.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwhJNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJBoQAHhwgSsoD3v75qKpFVElXiWr\nAOtLi03JIC4zYPnwDak1nwGP0hUW3E6GhCu/g5BnmGtZWuVvAj7RQ6RWvwkwY6P1\nJk4sv+ojUkbS2HIFxckH+3I7968mhadLCVEhPdbxsErVb+ZTqhIwSkY4SRwqjUzv\n2ITKd49W9fqQOYjfScTulTSwj/ov/V4OOI+zrO5+kPlGCg1XKbaKy0J9H6PbAwZ1\nAWwEIGbltUXDlN8di4aeYneZxbbzS9oDypoNP9eLcHqWcD6pyoKTScA8939QsK9/\nlrGhtZKrAWjI/mYxxfW7dIz+Ld3AG/XruTpDs8Scr9GOyJ9aUSAfe+6c3kXxZdMl\nvL5zriBcMoGiiMW2KxywAGegsDilIopXr3GIw2O2pBMJ+2r9b9+iop+hgZpgB04s\nEzY7LX8v4/8JD4HfFnzjz2Ykt4mMpOi91jZqciudQJQh145a/1PLnF7k029eIGw/\n3YHfTM4/we7qgBT/u25j3BV2lvswisrx3//2aCbR9qc+897nZgzmt7NMw2FYSRGP\naerALfcFK+yB7OdGCBVFEL9bQmrkOHXQWicAKZs3Vkkkw8qUkmyyos4h4pSIGNz4\n5I+8gIr0fhZu2L9S9HR4mV4DtwAuGtwAGuWSkVbcV8FMT7obYFMT6D4gSyWDINHE\nZCbHpM0E8Soyw6C+S4mw\n=70FB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T08:46:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/ed3edb76d329501c50d6427f753ba7cf2adb7f3e","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKGVkM2VkYjc2ZDMyOTUwMWM1MGQ2NDI3Zjc1M2JhN2NmMmFkYjdmM2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/51447988fc006fdfbacee8b1b3365490ae51d02f","sha":"51447988fc006fdfbacee8b1b3365490ae51d02f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/51447988fc006fdfbacee8b1b3365490ae51d02f"}],"sha":"ed3edb76d329501c50d6427f753ba7cf2adb7f3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/ed3edb76d329501c50d6427f753ba7cf2adb7f3e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/51447988fc006fdfbacee8b1b3365490ae51d02f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T08:18:15Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T08:18:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Scope the remaining photo-id endpoints to the viewer (#1436)\n\nIssue #1435 lists endpoints beyond /photos/file/* that only checked the\nmodule permission and then looked a photo, face or person up by id. A\nviewer could read another account''s OCR text, POI matches, edit recipes\nand the names of the people who made them, attach a transform row to a\nphoto they cannot see, copy someone''s recipe, assign a face to another\nuser''s person (leaking that person''s name through the faces listing),\nand have PATCH /persons/:id echo back anybody''s person record.\n\nAll of them now go through the one rule from photo-file-access.ts:\n\n- assertPhotoAccess(userId, photoId) throws not_found unless the photo\n  is the caller''s own, in an album they own or that is shared with\n  them, or the cover of such an album. It gates GET /photos/:id/ocr,\n  /poi-matches, /faces, and every transform read and write, including\n  auto-levels. A foreign photo is indistinguishable from an unused id.\n- getPhotoFacesLogic resolves a person name only when the person is the\n  caller''s; assignFaceToPersonLogic requires the target person to be the\n  caller''s; updatePersonLogic re-reads the record with the user filter\n  and answers 404 instead of returning another user''s person or\n  crashing on an unknown id.\n- GET /photos/uploaders lists only users who own a photo the caller can\n  see, rather than every account with photos.\n- The share-link coverage check is generalised to (link, photo) and\n  reused by assertPhotoInPublicLink, so a guest cannot read or write\n  comments on a photo the public listing withholds (hidden by a\n  participant, opted out of the link, or carrying a known face).\n\nTests cover each gate from the owner''s, a shared-album member''s and a\nstranger''s point of view. The existing transform tests share Alice''s\nphoto with Bob through an album, as the real app would.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ULXQb123aAKDosiRWXkofa\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"42b7ef1b7335bc80f19e7fe2d8e81c1c84fd35ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/42b7ef1b7335bc80f19e7fe2d8e81c1c84fd35ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/51447988fc006fdfbacee8b1b3365490ae51d02f","verification":{"payload":"tree 42b7ef1b7335bc80f19e7fe2d8e81c1c84fd35ca\nparent 23faa2807e9e3c8f255b07635e4a40650455eca9\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791101895 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791101895 +0200\n\nScope the remaining photo-id endpoints to the viewer (#1436)\n\nIssue #1435 lists endpoints beyond /photos/file/* that only checked the\nmodule permission and then looked a photo, face or person up by id. A\nviewer could read another account''s OCR text, POI matches, edit recipes\nand the names of the people who made them, attach a transform row to a\nphoto they cannot see, copy someone''s recipe, assign a face to another\nuser''s person (leaking that person''s name through the faces listing),\nand have PATCH /persons/:id echo back anybody''s person record.\n\nAll of them now go through the one rule from photo-file-access.ts:\n\n- assertPhotoAccess(userId, photoId) throws not_found unless the photo\n  is the caller''s own, in an album they own or that is shared with\n  them, or the cover of such an album. It gates GET /photos/:id/ocr,\n  /poi-matches, /faces, and every transform read and write, including\n  auto-levels. A foreign photo is indistinguishable from an unused id.\n- getPhotoFacesLogic resolves a person name only when the person is the\n  caller''s; assignFaceToPersonLogic requires the target person to be the\n  caller''s; updatePersonLogic re-reads the record with the user filter\n  and answers 404 instead of returning another user''s person or\n  crashing on an unknown id.\n- GET /photos/uploaders lists only users who own a photo the caller can\n  see, rather than every account with photos.\n- The share-link coverage check is generalised to (link, photo) and\n  reused by assertPhotoInPublicLink, so a guest cannot read or write\n  comments on a photo the public listing withholds (hidden by a\n  participant, opted out of the link, or carrying a known face).\n\nTests cover each gate from the owner''s, a shared-album member''s and a\nstranger''s point of view. The existing transform tests share Alice''s\nphoto with Bob through an album, as the real app would.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ULXQb123aAKDosiRWXkofa\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwgvHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUrsQAJj11WmNoDOS6HHGQb35a8Sv\nVMsndUR+getdqH8f6Bzcw8g2kZcsVX4rWELinzCO4X3kpSGEo2Yc5mQK/gh1dzSM\n0W97YG2gCtxiEhBsQncG1MxJxf8lpKJymAmyDcnSq54U+7vIT4K+6yu8vy0QnVIB\ngwVT9NU6ScHKkC0tMtw6He0XjD5iLiu75y63mUbuad3rFxSZoGIiCXkHqwLLlgrH\nFtHSdKKIok+3EdSA1cR5bfbFuTP7EbyfXnOLgZE+PgaSr44AiiwAYy5C3TRJObnh\nli1YAHhULoXlplpx9qc7C5geknxtGlEWeqMXZEiZ+ZEz+7oIRP+KMYjqHVAxiJE1\n8eZyUAkn/E7hsvZ8YwwPtxdhCFK5B79Wl9HHRXU/MFgvZQgH1OqGMohE5xBpoQcf\njz/22izFl3fyEnAizzyPsL/6MA/eca7p2uIyj8vV7UHs1sIm5x6JfAn9RQEGJqpa\nZDTYKuw9SmPiVAgTwokmN4vcnvqUSuduaz6nX1RPKAeWu90hn/kCJysG/+GhbLxf\nODui+dUF/eDeMBfgp6cnn0QqT9kuJv6k4jzF3EUUtzFuH3XeuRehc6LWtABpXJk4\ngZFbcfRnbAUTSVOfsynHXCfEkg55C0N3z0HjFFo4a0aMY/hXEDt8H96euOOobO+Q\nG7aV1597V141Ze31E5BY\n=SiEU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T08:18:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"