users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/16175dc6795154034bb0f98abcd463a431c7e857/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:49:05Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:49:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Restrict photo file access to the viewer''s own scope (#1433)\n\nA signed-in user holding module.photos and photos.view could fetch any\nphoto on the server: /photos/file/* only checked those two permissions\nbefore streaming whatever filename was asked for, and /photos/:id/render\nand /photos/:id/export looked the photo up by its sequential id without\na user condition. v=original even answered with the filename, so walking\nid=1,2,3,... handed out another account''s whole library.\n\nThe metadata endpoints already scope a photo to its owner plus the\nmembers of albums the user owns or has shared with them. The image\nbytes now follow the same rule:\n\n- photo-file-access.ts gains accessiblePhotoCondition(), the one SQL\n  predicate for \"a photo this user may see\" (own upload, member of an\n  accessible album, or cover of one), with viewerMayReadFile() and\n  viewerMayReadPhotoId() on top of it.\n- denyPhotoFileRequest() applies it to signed-in viewers. A photo\n  outside their scope is refused like any other unauthorized request\n  (403), and a share token still works for a viewer who was sent a\n  link to an album nobody shared with them.\n- renderPhotoTransformed and exportPhotoTransformed check the id\n  against the caller''s scope right after the permission gate and answer\n  a foreign photo with 404, indistinguishable from an unused id.\n\nTests replace \"a viewer reads any file\" with owner, stranger, shared\nalbum, shared cover and contributor cases, and add scope tests for the\nrender and export endpoints.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ULXQb123aAKDosiRWXkofa\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0123dd9319f0f747033317f16e29405d11a785e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/0123dd9319f0f747033317f16e29405d11a785e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/16175dc6795154034bb0f98abcd463a431c7e857","verification":{"payload":"tree 0123dd9319f0f747033317f16e29405d11a785e3\nparent d1899692bed15f70e97e0dd16e5d43b7acf4cdd0\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1791024545 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791024545 +0200\n\nRestrict photo file access to the viewer''s own scope (#1433)\n\nA signed-in user holding module.photos and photos.view could fetch any\nphoto on the server: /photos/file/* only checked those two permissions\nbefore streaming whatever filename was asked for, and /photos/:id/render\nand /photos/:id/export looked the photo up by its sequential id without\na user condition. v=original even answered with the filename, so walking\nid=1,2,3,... handed out another account''s whole library.\n\nThe metadata endpoints already scope a photo to its owner plus the\nmembers of albums the user owns or has shared with them. The image\nbytes now follow the same rule:\n\n- photo-file-access.ts gains accessiblePhotoCondition(), the one SQL\n  predicate for \"a photo this user may see\" (own upload, member of an\n  accessible album, or cover of one), with viewerMayReadFile() and\n  viewerMayReadPhotoId() on top of it.\n- denyPhotoFileRequest() applies it to signed-in viewers. A photo\n  outside their scope is refused like any other unauthorized request\n  (403), and a share token still works for a viewer who was sent a\n  link to an album nobody shared with them.\n- renderPhotoTransformed and exportPhotoTransformed check the id\n  against the caller''s scope right after the permission gate and answer\n  a foreign photo with 404, indistinguishable from an unused id.\n\nTests replace \"a viewer reads any file\" with owner, stranger, shared\nalbum, shared cover and contributor cases, and add scope tests for the\nrender and export endpoints.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ULXQb123aAKDosiRWXkofa\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwN2hCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMtYQAKeEbUaM50jx859EZIrKyZ69\nwCY9nI3uDSYae6RExYhsxuijMHkO13K8AnVoEA/ELFMGtiKp1UWMop+asXlivZcU\nP0ed1DVEuBv4Pn3mRVAefZlCYDleJ6BoP1iDt+FmADtJyfQ7zngk3ELXcQDP2TD3\nrmwJH/nWILY5BK+Bm2oMGt8TXGh8gAyuOs+tdr8+P0BDE7Ry0T9kDQSIIlkqdBwd\n4Vssd2nRBxEsrzgbhmySvUES4IQwOQyhxlT1LTC9oURG0Fvml/OZudKNbk4gl0ur\n2nYkMZXQ88JP7t+K4NMGh3Wzm4NiPIisB+sZClC35OlYx17MvSkGau8YPph+qTUG\nmWtKbW1j1q0T7b/NJ9aLeKuD4xctkph8ODIESN7Ehe7yvsout5bICBh3WimO3VE8\nli3gz2PE0ZO0LpTl1lY1ikn/GcExCudPpLB6jrfmHX0pJNQbxTGG7QtUk5boUVpI\n7moiopQ4fL6aVDgaD+2K8RJKtxS6JWHRqgOin8BgIgR0bk1ch1viTkBikldfMIkz\nhUGXp1/yNrYwCKWWS53EZYU9yO7hbuUQnmO1l4vyQ4AX9HXiewcAKl2bRzBKzCxi\n4QV6l/oY0ZSxyUC4wxi9cdgSQrFXC4gT0aEl1OnudAkwIynvgyadvfKBhBMuXatT\nJeSSdiEM5rXQSeJml/AB\n=oNyh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T10:49:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events