/api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/d1899692bed15f70e97e0dd16e5d43b7acf4cdd0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T22:38:39Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T22:38:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Orientation variants: recaps and stream (#1427)\n\nThe recap player and the stream card show one photo large; now they\nshow the side of a format pair that fits the screen, using the one\nrule the slideshow already follows (.claude/plans/orientierungs-\nvarianten.md, stage 6).\n\n- Backend: counterpartsByPhotoId(userId, photoIds) names the\n  best-ranked other side per photo. GET /recaps/:id ships them as\n  counterparts[], FeedPhotoItem carries counterpart. Only the viewer''s\n  own groups count, so other people''s photos never carry one.\n- Web: pickSideForScreen is the shared rule. RecapPlayer takes\n  counterparts and builds its slides over the fitting side (same\n  length, same indices); RecapsView loads the other sides in the same\n  details batch. PhotoFeedCard shows the fitting side with its aspect\n  ratio; likes, comments and the fullscreen stay with the item.\n- iOS: SlideshowVariants.pickSide, RecapPlayerView substitutes per\n  orientation before pairing, FeedCardView loads the file of the\n  fitting side.\n- Plan and CLAUDE.md record the feature as implemented.\n\nTests: counterpartsByPhotoId (backend), pickSideForScreen (web), recap\nand feed decoding plus side picking (iOS); a RecapPlayer format-pair\nstory in both orientations.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FU1mZY23NYn79RjaRTtZPQ\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b931d007574ec7941b1a480555ad288793c24764","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/b931d007574ec7941b1a480555ad288793c24764"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/d1899692bed15f70e97e0dd16e5d43b7acf4cdd0","verification":{"payload":"tree b931d007574ec7941b1a480555ad288793c24764\nparent 07c5113cab811d9aa2f6b4dc3f9bb7d8124c2ebb\nauthor as19git67 <anton@schegg.de> 1790980719 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790980719 +0200\n\nOrientation variants: recaps and stream (#1427)\n\nThe recap player and the stream card show one photo large; now they\nshow the side of a format pair that fits the screen, using the one\nrule the slideshow already follows (.claude/plans/orientierungs-\nvarianten.md, stage 6).\n\n- Backend: counterpartsByPhotoId(userId, photoIds) names the\n  best-ranked other side per photo. GET /recaps/:id ships them as\n  counterparts[], FeedPhotoItem carries counterpart. Only the viewer''s\n  own groups count, so other people''s photos never carry one.\n- Web: pickSideForScreen is the shared rule. RecapPlayer takes\n  counterparts and builds its slides over the fitting side (same\n  length, same indices); RecapsView loads the other sides in the same\n  details batch. PhotoFeedCard shows the fitting side with its aspect\n  ratio; likes, comments and the fullscreen stay with the item.\n- iOS: SlideshowVariants.pickSide, RecapPlayerView substitutes per\n  orientation before pairing, FeedCardView loads the file of the\n  fitting side.\n- Plan and CLAUDE.md record the feature as implemented.\n\nTests: counterpartsByPhotoId (backend), pickSideForScreen (web), recap\nand feed decoding plus side picking (iOS); a RecapPlayer format-pair\nstory in both orientations.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FU1mZY23NYn79RjaRTtZPQ\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",