tps://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/08250a00eb4e19b1b30877c2b1ca1ef899a3b78f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T19:24:22Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T19:24:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Finance: scroll the PDF in the settlement dialog, not the page behind it (#1336) (#1408)\n\nThe PDF pane had a fixed height but was no flex container, so PdfViewer\ngrew with its pages and the overflow was clipped: the wheel over the PDF\ndid nothing and fell through to the page underneath. Make the pane a flex\ncontainer (the same contract as the document detail''s PDF panel) and let\nthe dialog block background scrolling.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fb8bd7fabb2c5ef0fe2eb33e8a78538b7dd254ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/fb8bd7fabb2c5ef0fe2eb33e8a78538b7dd254ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/08250a00eb4e19b1b30877c2b1ca1ef899a3b78f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/08250a00eb4e19b1b30877c2b1ca1ef899a3b78f","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDA4MjUwYTAwZWI0ZTE5YjFiMzA4NzdjMmIxY2ExZWY4OTlhM2I3OGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/264ee524d025287a524663af4522298c9f677087","sha":"264ee524d025287a524663af4522298c9f677087","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/264ee524d025287a524663af4522298c9f677087"}],"sha":"08250a00eb4e19b1b30877c2b1ca1ef899a3b78f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/08250a00eb4e19b1b30877c2b1ca1ef899a3b78f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/264ee524d025287a524663af4522298c9f677087/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T19:16:48Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T19:16:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Routing status: read tiles from the plain status answer (#1407)\n\n`/status?verbose=true` is not how Valhalla takes options on a GET, so\n`has_tiles` never arrived and a router with a built tile set showed as\n\"reachable, but without tiles\" next to its own build date. Ask the plain\nstatus and treat a tile set age as proof of tiles; it also spares the\nrouter the bbox walk of the verbose answer.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f01149c855562666b846618f6925155961436429","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/f01149c855562666b846618f6925155961436429"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/264ee524d025287a524663af4522298c9f677087","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/264ee524d025287a524663af4522298c9f677087","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDI2NGVlNTI0ZDAyNTI4N2E1MjQ2NjNhZjQ1MjIyOThjOWY2NzcwODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/8a5862cbfd9658ce498e7ab3d24b010b954a4ea1","sha":"8a5862cbfd9658ce498e7ab3d24b010b954a4ea1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/8a5862cbfd9658ce498e7ab3d24b010b954a4ea1"}],"sha":"264ee524d025287a524663af4522298c9f677087","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/264ee524d025287a524663af4522298c9f677087"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/8a5862cbfd9658ce498e7ab3d24b010b954a4ea1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T16:44:56Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T16:44:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Finance: read settlements with rules and the language model, checked by arithmetic (#1336) (#1406)\n\nFixed rules break silently when a bank renames a label; a language model\nreads any layout but can misplace a digit without a trace. Settlements\nare now read by both, and arithmetic decides which value to trust.\n\n- llm-client: extractSettlementValues() asks the local model (/json-prompt)\n  for the 13 settlement fields as JSON, absolute amounts, nothing computed.\n- depot-settlement-merge.ts (pure): validates the model''s answer\n  (ISIN shape, numbers, dates), checks a reading (gross ± fees ± taxes =\n  net, quantity × price ≈ gross, ISIN check digit, plausible date) and\n  merges: agreement → \"both\"; gaps filled from the other source;\n  disagreement → the reading whose figures add up (ties go to the rules).\n  If they disagree on something that is booked and nothing adds up, the\n  verdict is \"unverified\".\n- depot-settlement-reader.ts: rules on every read; the model asked once\n  per document and its answer stored (finance_document_settlement_llm,\n  migration 0222) — dry runs and the review page use the stored answer\n  only. Only text with a security identifier and securities wording is\n  sent to the model. llm-service down → rules only, reported as such.\n- Enrichment: \"unverified\" readings book nothing and appear under\n  \"Erkennung unsicher\" in the review; the read-in notice counts them.\n- Inspection: per field the rules'' value, the model''s value and which was\n  used; the checks with their figures; the model''s status (used / cached\n  / unavailable / skipped); the verdict.\n- Dialog: \"Verwendet · Quelle · Regel / KI\" with disagreements marked,\n  the checks below, and a line saying how the document was read.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"762de866d398af56a25953c5dd74ce439aa45391","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/762de866d398af56a25953c5dd74ce439aa45391"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/8a5862cbfd9658ce498e7ab3d24b010b954a4ea1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/8a5862cbfd9658ce498e7ab3d24b010b954a4ea1","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDhhNTg2MmNiZmQ5NjU4Y2U0OThlN2FiM2QyNGIwMTBiOTU0YTRlYTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/8068561dd282ee92ebe64b51f3a243738d5570c8","sha":"8068561dd282ee92ebe64b51f3a243738d5570c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/8068561dd282ee92ebe64b51f3a243738d5570c8"}],"sha":"8a5862cbfd9658ce498e7ab3d24b010b954a4ea1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/8a5862cbfd9658ce498e7ab3d24b010b954a4ea1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/8068561dd282ee92ebe64b51f3a243738d5570c8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T16:00:37Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T16:00:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Finance: settlement preview dialog with what the parser recognised (#1336) (#1405)\n\nTwo things users ran into after reading in their settlements:\n\n1. Following a document link from the portfolio left the page, and back\n   did not return to the same place. Documents now open in a dialog\n   (SettlementDocumentDialog) over the portfolio: the PDF beside what was\n   read from it. Closing returns exactly where the user was; \"Im\n   Dokumentmodul öffnen\" stays available. Used from the transaction\n   source cell and from every document in \"Zu prüfen\", where a conflict\n   can also be applied from inside the dialog.\n\n2. It was unclear what the parser looks for, what it found, and whether\n   an LLM was involved. GET /finance/portfolio/documents/:id/inspection\n   returns every field the parser knows (kind, ISIN, WKN, name, depot\n   number, execution date, quantity, price, gross, fees, taxes, net,\n   currency) with the value found or null and the printed label it was\n   read after, why the text does or does not count as a settlement, the\n   depot a dry run would pick with how it was found (holding, depot\n   number, existing transactions) and whether the date came from the\n   statement or the document date, plus the transactions already linked.\n   It states that reading is rule-based and no LLM fallback exists.\n\nParser: inspectSettlement() returns partial results and per-field labels;\nparseSettlement() is built on it and unchanged for its callers.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"612d703bdac2529e7b469fc67deaed9180b5ee3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/612d703bdac2529e7b469fc67deaed9180b5ee3a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/8068561dd282ee92ebe64b51f3a243738d5570c8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/8068561dd282ee92ebe64b51f3a243738d5570c8","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDgwNjg1NjFkZDI4MmVlOTJlYmU2NGI1MWYzYTI0MzczOGQ1NTcwYzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/02ea89b97cbd223e4ec440c9ab41f63130bf57f6","sha":"02ea89b97cbd223e4ec440c9ab41f63130bf57f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/02ea89b97cbd223e4ec440c9ab41f63130bf57f6"}],"sha":"8068561dd282ee92ebe64b51f3a243738d5570c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/8068561dd282ee92ebe64b51f3a243738d5570c8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/02ea89b97cbd223e4ec440c9ab41f63130bf57f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T15:11:33Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T15:11:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Admin build number, statements-cron test order, routing tiles follow the extracts (#1404)\n\n* Admin: read the build number from /api/build-info again\n\nThe admin page showed \"Build unbekannt\". The build-info endpoint''s own\npath starts with /api (web/static.ts), unlike the service endpoints at\nthe root, but getBuildInfo() asked for ${API_BASE_URL}/build-info —\n/build-info in production (empty base) and, after the dev proxy strips\nits prefix, also /build-info in development. Nothing answers there, so\nthe page fell back to \"unbekannt\" and the new-build check in\nappUpdate.ts never saw a new build either. It asks for\n${API_BASE_URL}/api/build-info now, with a test for the URL and the\nfallback, and the stories answer the development path too.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* statements-cron test: delete transactions before accounts in the cleanup\n\nThe test cleaned up finance_account without finance_transaction, whose\nforeign key restricts the delete. When an earlier test file left\ntransactions in the shared test database, every test in the file failed\nin beforeEach (\"violates foreign key constraint\nfinance_transaction_account_id_fkey\"); alone it passed. Everything that\nreferences a transaction cascades or nulls, so one more delete suffices.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* Routing tiles follow the extracts: prune orphans, rebuild on change, merge overlaps\n\nThe routing container built tiles from every PBF the geo service had\never downloaded: deleting a region dropped its database but kept its\nextract, so a removed whole-Europe region still drove a continent-sized\ntile build, and overlapping extracts (Great Britain and England) went in\nside by side.\n\ngeo: deleting a region also deletes its cached extract; every six hours\n(and a minute after start) extracts whose region database does not exist\nare removed, unless an import of it is running or the file is younger\nthan a day (pbf-cache.ts, mapping file name to database the way the app\nnames it). Downloads go to a .part file and are renamed when complete,\nso an aborted download is never taken for a finished extract.\n\nrouting: while serving, the entrypoint compares the set of extracts every\nten minutes; a change that holds for one more check stops the service and\nthe container exits, compose restarts it, and it rebuilds from scratch —\ntiles and admin database — so nothing of a deleted extract survives. With\nno extracts left the old tiles are removed. Several extracts are merged\nwith osmium first (osmium-tool added to the image).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a6218983118d10c0e5ea73a089e7236e1205170c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/a6218983118d10c0e5ea73a089e7236e1205170c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/02ea89b97cbd223e4ec440c9ab41f63130bf57f6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/02ea89b97cbd223e4ec440c9ab41f63130bf57f6","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDAyZWE4OWI5N2NiZDIyM2U0ZWM0NDBjOWFiNDFmNjMxMzBiZjU3ZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/a610e616c3c16c7680e140e4899375c759967784","sha":"a610e616c3c16c7680e140e4899375c759967784","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/a610e616c3c16c7680e140e4899375c759967784"}],"sha":"02ea89b97cbd223e4ec440c9ab41f63130bf57f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/02ea89b97cbd223e4ec440c9ab41f63130bf57f6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/a610e616c3c16c7680e140e4899375c759967784/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:33:20Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:33:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Finance: portfolio review, holdings reconciliation, and settlement depot matching (#1336) (#1403)\n\n* Finance: portfolio review — settlement conflicts and holdings reconciliation (#1336)\n\nFollow-up to stage 4: the loose ends the document enrichment and the\ndepot snapshots can surface, in one place.\n\nHoldings reconciliation (depot-holding-reconciliation.ts):\n- Between two snapshots of a depot the change in shares must equal what\n  the transactions in between moved. Transactions are pooled and handed\n  to the next snapshot pair whose amount actually changes, so settlement\n  lag (trade Monday, shares Wednesday) does not read as a gap.\n- A change involving a transaction without a quantity, a split or a\n  corporate action is counted as unverifiable, not reported.\n- Unit tests for the pure walk; the position endpoint returns\n  holding_gaps and unverifiable_changes.\n\nReview (GET /finance/portfolio/review):\n- conflicts and settlements without a holding depot, found by a dry run\n  of the document enrichment (enrichDocument/enrichPendingDocuments take\n  a dryRun option), so the list is current and empties once resolved;\n- holding gaps across the depots in scope;\n- documents are only listed to their owner or a finance admin.\n\nResolve (POST /finance/portfolio/documents/:documentId/apply): write the\nstatement''s values onto the conflicting transaction (the booking date\nstays) and link the document; requires write access.\n\nFrontend: a \"Zu prüfen\" section on the portfolio page (PortfolioReview)\nwith conflicts (confirm, then apply), holding gaps and unmatched\ndocuments; a reconciliation section on the position page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n* Finance: find a settlement''s depot without a current holding (#1336)\n\nSettlements of securities sold before the first FinTS sync never matched\na depot, because only holdings snapshots were consulted. A statement now\nfinds its depot by, in order:\n\n1. a snapshot of a depot holding the ISIN/WKN (as before),\n2. the depot number it prints (\"Depotnummer\", \"Depot-Nr.\", \"Depotkonto\"),\n   matched against the account number with tolerance for padding and\n   sub-depot suffixes — only when exactly one depot matches,\n3. the one depot that already has transactions of the security.\n\nParser: reads the depot number (same line only), a WKN printed beside the\nISIN without its own prefix (\"ISIN/WKN DE…/123456\", \"WKN/ISIN …/DE…\"),\nand no longer takes the next line (\"Schlusstag …\") as the security name;\nthe line above the identifier is used when it looks like a name.\n\nReview: unmatched settlements carry the ISIN, WKN and depot number they\nwere read with, and the UI says why each found no depot.\n\nPortfolio: depots with neither a holdings snapshot nor a transaction are\nleft out of the depot list and the \"n of m depots\" count.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n* Finance: leave closed depots out of the portfolio by default (#1336)\n\nA household''s closed depots (moved to another broker, sold out) still\ncarry history, so they counted as depots and their old positions mixed\ninto the current figures (\"5 of 5 depots\" with only two in use).\n\n- Portfolio, transactions, position and review endpoints cover the open\n  depots unless `closed=true` is passed; a closed depot picked by id is\n  always covered. The portfolio reports how many closed depots it hid and\n  flags closed ones in the depot list.\n- Frontend: \"Geschlossene Depots einbeziehen\" in the filter panel\n  (?closedDepots=1, with its own filter chip), \"(geschlossen)\" in the\n  depot selector, \"n geschlossene ausgeblendet\" in the page hint, and the\n  flag travels to the position page and the review section.\n- Document enrichment still reaches closed depots: their settlements\n  belong to their history.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DoEgs1Tx8wZyzVtNGNjhZm\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b403098dc0211ac4fee0fc6a7e57b8ecd4feb360","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/b403098dc0211ac4fee0fc6a7e57b8ecd4feb360"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/a610e616c3c16c7680e140e4899375c759967784","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/a610e616c3c16c7680e140e4899375c759967784","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKGE2MTBlNjE2YzNjMTZjNzY4MGUxNDBlNDg5OTM3NWM3NTk5Njc3ODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/75273e7db3bd2926b7c2613147a05ced0016929f","sha":"75273e7db3bd2926b7c2613147a05ced0016929f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/75273e7db3bd2926b7c2613147a05ced0016929f"}],"sha":"a610e616c3c16c7680e140e4899375c759967784","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/a610e616c3c16c7680e140e4899375c759967784"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/75273e7db3bd2926b7c2613147a05ced0016929f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T13:19:51Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T13:19:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Watchtower: update the routing container, and containers in a restart loop (#1402)\n\nWatchtower only updates the containers named in its command list, and\nfk-encore-routing was never added when the service was introduced, so\nthe fixed routing image was not pulled. It also skips containers stuck\nin a restart loop by default, which is exactly when a fixed image\nmatters. Add routing to the list, set WATCHTOWER_INCLUDE_RESTARTING,\nand say in docker-compose.yml and DEPLOYMENT.md that a new service has\nto be added to the list.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7e18f0b46687c02c38e9c12b26114b01345414d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/7e18f0b46687c02c38e9c12b26114b01345414d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/75273e7db3bd2926b7c2613147a05ced0016929f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/75273e7db3bd2926b7c2613147a05ced0016929f","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDc1MjczZTdkYjNiZDI5MjZiN2MyNjEzMTQ3YTA1Y2VkMDAxNjkyOWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/ad1551ea8638a92ce5cf6ce8c6fefbfca536f88e","sha":"ad1551ea8638a92ce5cf6ce8c6fefbfca536f88e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/ad1551ea8638a92ce5cf6ce8c6fefbfca536f88e"}],"sha":"75273e7db3bd2926b7c2613147a05ced0016929f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/75273e7db3bd2926b7c2613147a05ced0016929f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/ad1551ea8638a92ce5cf6ce8c6fefbfca536f88e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T12:51:05Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T12:51:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Clear the widgets'' snapshots and photos on sign-out (#1399)\n\nThe widget extension never checks a session — it only reads the\nsnapshots and JPEGs the app left in the App Group container. Sign-out\ncleared the tokens but not those, so the home screen kept showing the\nprevious account''s photo, owner and album names, including to the\nnext account signed in on the same phone.\n\nWidgetSnapshotStore.clearAll() removes all three snapshots and their\nimages and reloads the timelines; AuthManager.clearSession() calls it\nnext to the Spotlight wipe, which exists for the same reason.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016LiwkGCxsp2BNzCigrvHiH","tree":{"sha":"fc220dc20c76c9d372eeed49cbbf1ad276fbc364","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/fc220dc20c76c9d372eeed49cbbf1ad276fbc364"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/ad1551ea8638a92ce5cf6ce8c6fefbfca536f88e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/ad1551ea8638a92ce5cf6ce8c6fefbfca536f88e","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKGFkMTU1MWVhODYzOGE5MmNlNWNmNmNlOGM2ZmVmYmZjYTUzNmY4OGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/b1cb21eece9f65f542fb1008e4dada76789fb949","sha":"b1cb21eece9f65f542fb1008e4dada76789fb949","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/b1cb21eece9f65f542fb1008e4dada76789fb949"}],"sha":"ad1551ea8638a92ce5cf6ce8c6fefbfca536f88e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/ad1551ea8638a92ce5cf6ce8c6fefbfca536f88e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/b1cb21eece9f65f542fb1008e4dada76789fb949/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T12:49:00Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T12:49:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Documents: run the tax-review recompute at midday (#1400)\n\nThe job moves from 02:15 UTC to 11:00 UTC (13:00 in summer, 12:00 in\nwinter, Berlin), inside the 10–15 o''clock window and after the batch\njobs that end at 10:30 UTC. The docs say the same.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TzUSmLtnpEakztrMexTZWZ\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a18e181d8105f8d021a3c2a3a8b387c8268b3718","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/a18e181d8105f8d021a3c2a3a8b387c8268b3718"},"url":"https://ap