ps://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/d73d9fa4b4ae8771b936d0b44af6f1ca709ded5f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:17:20Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:17:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix natural photo search: pin transformers to 4.x, report embedding errors distinctly (#1388)\n\n* Distinguish embedding-service failures in natural photo search\n\nThe search endpoint now maps embedding-service timeouts, unreachable\nhosts and gateway errors to deadline_exceeded / unavailable / internal,\nand the gallery shows a matching message instead of one generic error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015XnT4bofDJmhYRCBMwaT9n\n\n* Pin transformers to 4.x so CLIP text search works again\n\nopen-clip-torch 2.26.1 calls batch_encode_plus, which transformers 5\nremoved, so every /search/text request returned HTTP 500.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015XnT4bofDJmhYRCBMwaT9n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"47960ee023779cad1ee0b7446dcb64b6de8ae315","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/47960ee023779cad1ee0b7446dcb64b6de8ae315"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/d73d9fa4b4ae8771b936d0b44af6f1ca709ded5f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/d73d9fa4b4ae8771b936d0b44af6f1ca709ded5f","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKGQ3M2Q5ZmE0YjRhZTg3NzFiOTM2ZDBiNDRhZjZmMWNhNzA5ZGVkNWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/56422ef67fe34e9f3ef8ff4563fb375ef59e1da1","sha":"56422ef67fe34e9f3ef8ff4563fb375ef59e1da1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/56422ef67fe34e9f3ef8ff4563fb375ef59e1da1"}],"sha":"d73d9fa4b4ae8771b936d0b44af6f1ca709ded5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/d73d9fa4b4ae8771b936d0b44af6f1ca709ded5f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/56422ef67fe34e9f3ef8ff4563fb375ef59e1da1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:42:08Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:42:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Routing service (Valhalla), stage 1: container, client, travel table, status and compare (#1387)\n\nReal travel times come in stages (docs §24). This is the first: a\nrouting container built from the geo service''s PBF extracts (tiles in\nrouting_data, rebuilt on restart when an extract is newer), a router\nclient (status, matrix, route; transit not asked without GTFS), a\ntravel table that asks the router once per day for every pair and\nfalls back to the estimate everywhere else, a solver hook that reads\nfrom such a table, GET /trip-planner/routing/status (tiles behind the\nnewest region, honestly) and POST /trip-planner/routing/compare for\nthe measurement §14 asks for before the router shapes a plan.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"18b973c99c7417c584780da728e59e6919b06cd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/18b973c99c7417c584780da728e59e6919b06cd0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/56422ef67fe34e9f3ef8ff4563fb375ef59e1da1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/56422ef67fe34e9f3ef8ff4563fb375ef59e1da1","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDU2NDIyZWY2N2ZlMzRlOWYzZWY4ZmY0NTYzZmIzNzVlZjU5ZTFkYTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/a47b035c71a1ef1cd7a55a8ed888bc57b5185295","sha":"a47b035c71a1ef1cd7a55a8ed888bc57b5185295","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/a47b035c71a1ef1cd7a55a8ed888bc57b5185295"}],"sha":"56422ef67fe34e9f3ef8ff4563fb375ef59e1da1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/56422ef67fe34e9f3ef8ff4563fb375ef59e1da1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/a47b035c71a1ef1cd7a55a8ed888bc57b5185295/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:24:04Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:24:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Suggest a journey without dates; mobility as a choice page (#1386)\n\nThe journey suggestion no longer needs dated cities: on a trip without\ndates it names the two clock times and no day, the form opens on today\nwith them, and saving the journey dates the trip. How a traveller gets\nabout (foot, wheelchair, pram) is a \"Mobilität\" row leading to a page of\nchoices, like the trip''s \"Fortbewegung\". Build number 1682.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"73ac718a9a75b0b2d465ce4d3cad7e63fdcf139d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/73ac718a9a75b0b2d465ce4d3cad7e63fdcf139d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/a47b035c71a1ef1cd7a55a8ed888bc57b5185295","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/a47b035c71a1ef1cd7a55a8ed888bc57b5185295","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKGE0N2IwMzVjNzFhMWVmMWNkN2E1NWE4ZWQ4ODhiYzU3YjUxODUyOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/1c7e4df27cb5a0407e1f14e0906a0c4deae95d9d","sha":"1c7e4df27cb5a0407e1f14e0906a0c4deae95d9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/1c7e4df27cb5a0407e1f14e0906a0c4deae95d9d"}],"sha":"a47b035c71a1ef1cd7a55a8ed888bc57b5185295","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/a47b035c71a1ef1cd7a55a8ed888bc57b5185295"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/1c7e4df27cb5a0407e1f14e0906a0c4deae95d9d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:54:04Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:54:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Journeys date an undated trip; a home set once; end the Live Activity of a deleted trip (#1385)\n\n* Journeys date an undated trip; a home set once for every new trip\n\nA journey to or from home, or between two places, no longer needs the\nneighbouring city to carry a date: when the trip has none, the journey\ndates it — the arrival day is the first place''s first day, the\ndeparture day the last place''s last day, counted back over the places\nbefore. The legs screen offers Anreise and Heimreise as soon as home is\nknown, and the journey form says that the trip gets its dates from it.\n\nWhere a person lives is said once, in the trip settings, kept in\ntrip_user_homes (migration 0219) and copied into every trip they\ncreate; the first home given to a trip becomes theirs while none is\nset. A trip made before offers the person''s home with one tap.\n\nBuild number 1680.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* End the Live Activity when its trip is deleted or left\n\nDeleting a running trip left its day in the Dynamic Island: the\nrunning plan and the offline snapshot outlived the trip, and a wake\nkept the Activity current from the snapshot. TripPlanGone.forget()\nends the Activity, stops the fences, drops the snapshot and the\nscreen state and re-reads the running plan; the list calls it after\ndeleting or leaving. TripRunningDay.load() no longer falls back on the\nsnapshot when the server said no (deleted, no longer shared), only\nwhen it could not be reached. Build number 1681.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ef81cd355a89dc733f5ee6267b1be935d675eea7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/ef81cd355a89dc733f5ee6267b1be935d675eea7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/1c7e4df27cb5a0407e1f14e0906a0c4deae95d9d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/1c7e4df27cb5a0407e1f14e0906a0c4deae95d9d","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDFjN2U0ZGYyN2NiNWEwNDA3ZTFmMTRlMDkwNmEwYzRkZWFlOTVkOWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/1c7cee40ebe0219e0844403be2662593cd1fa0df","sha":"1c7cee40ebe0219e0844403be2662593cd1fa0df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/1c7cee40ebe0219e0844403be2662593cd1fa0df"}],"sha":"1c7e4df27cb5a0407e1f14e0906a0c4deae95d9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/1c7e4df27cb5a0407e1f14e0906a0c4deae95d9d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/1c7cee40ebe0219e0844403be2662593cd1fa0df/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:33:41Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:33:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"iOS widgets: show the recap cover and the feed photo, not only text (#1384)\n\nThe three home-screen widgets (#764) had been text-only on purpose:\nthe app''s thumbnail cache lives in its private Caches directory, which\nthe widget extension''s sandbox cannot read, so a widget had nothing to\ndraw but a caption and two lines.\n\nGive them a shared place for a photo. `WidgetImageStore` keeps one\nJPEG per widget in `widget-images/` inside the App Group container.\nAfter the recap list or the feed has written its text snapshot (as\nbefore), the app downloads the recap cover or the feed photo once at\nwidget size (`/photos/file/…?w=800&convert=true`), downscales it, and\nstores it there; the snapshot records the file name and the widget\nshows the photo as its background under a gradient. Text is written\nfirst and the image follows, so a widget is never behind the app, and a\nsnapshot whose cover is unchanged keeps its file rather than fetching\nit again. A new recap in the same slot does not inherit the old photo,\nand a failed download leaves the text card as it was.\n\nSnapshots written before this still decode: the new fields are\noptional.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WS4MTT15DtqRaz4Q35mNHJ\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f5aa778813f6dc2787d60af0096c5e9f6e0c0c09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/f5aa778813f6dc2787d60af0096c5e9f6e0c0c09"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/1c7cee40ebe0219e0844403be2662593cd1fa0df","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/1c7cee40ebe0219e0844403be2662593cd1fa0df","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDFjN2NlZTQwZWJlMDIxOWUwODQ0NDAzYmUyNjYyNTkzY2QxZmEwZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/9567dbf9548baa1ac90899c2c3e787b01e2a8d10","sha":"9567dbf9548baa1ac90899c2c3e787b01e2a8d10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/9567dbf9548baa1ac90899c2c3e787b01e2a8d10"}],"sha":"1c7cee40ebe0219e0844403be2662593cd1fa0df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/1c7cee40ebe0219e0844403be2662593cd1fa0df"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/9567dbf9548baa1ac90899c2c3e787b01e2a8d10/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T06:32:48Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T06:32:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Forecast: plan vs. actual — snapshots, today''s wealth, and the bookings (#1383)\n\n* Forecast: plan vs. actual — snapshots, today''s wealth, and the bookings\n\nCloses #1342.\n\nSnapshots\n- New table finance_forecast_snapshot (migration 0219): per scenario the\n  yearly series of wealth and liquid wealth, the liquid and total wealth\n  the household had when it was taken, and the scenario config.\n- Taken by hand (POST /finance/forecast/snapshots) or by the new daily\n  cron, which writes one snapshot per saved scenario and one for the\n  defaults for every household whose last cron snapshot is older than\n  27 days.\n- GET /finance/forecast/plan-actual lists the snapshots with what each\n  expected for today (linear between its start value and its year\n  ends), today''s liquid and total wealth as the forecast starts from\n  them, and the actuals below. DELETE removes a snapshot.\n\nActuals from the bookings\n- Inflows, outflows and the savings rate per month over the last twelve\n  full months across the household''s accounts, leaving out moves\n  between its own accounts (counterparty IBAN of the household, or a\n  mirror booking of the same amount on another account within three\n  days).\n- Against the plan: the spending the items add up to, and the savings\n  the simulation expects in its first full year. POST\n  /finance/forecast/actuals/adopt writes the actual spending into the\n  household''s living-expense item.\n\nFrontend\n- Card \"Plan und Wirklichkeit\": today''s wealth, a button to keep the\n  current scenario''s stand, the snapshot table with the deviation of\n  today''s wealth from what each expected, and the bookings against the\n  plan with the adopt button.\n\nTests: interpolation, transfer detection and averaging, the twelve-month\nwindow, planned spending; snapshots end to end with a linked account and\na year of bookings; the cron''s once-a-month guard. Fixtures invented.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TzUSmLtnpEakztrMexTZWZ\n\n* Forecast: snapshot table scrolls inside its card on narrow screens\n\nThe table sat directly in a flex column and kept its intrinsic width; a\nwrapper with min-width 0 lets ScrollX do the scrolling.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TzUSmLtnpEakztrMexTZWZ\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a6b6ebe3642939effb9419bcddfe961f32f7fae8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/a6b6ebe3642939effb9419bcddfe961f32f7fae8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/9567dbf9548baa1ac90899c2c3e787b01e2a8d10","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/9567dbf9548baa1ac90899c2c3e787b01e2a8d10","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDk1NjdkYmY5NTQ4YmFhMWFjOTA4OTljMmMzZTc4N2IwMWUyYThkMTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/b37962b59dfb60cdc41d734f8443042e69d4af7c","sha":"b37962b59dfb60cdc41d734f8443042e69d4af7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/b37962b59dfb60cdc41d734f8443042e69d4af7c"}],"sha":"9567dbf9548baa1ac90899c2c3e787b01e2a8d10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/9567dbf9548baa1ac90899c2c3e787b01e2a8d10"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/b37962b59dfb60cdc41d734f8443042e69d4af7c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T20:24:01Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T20:24:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Forecast: survivor scenario — what happens when one person dies (#1382)\n\nCloses #1341.\n\nEngine\n- The scenario gains `survivor` (person, age, expense factor, income\n  offset rate and allowance). From the birthday month of that age the\n  person''s salary, income, expenses, health insurance, care costs and own\n  pensions end, as do their running contributions.\n- Pension items gain `survivorShare`: the surviving partner receives that\n  share of the pension (default 55 % statutory, 60 % company, 0 private),\n  from the death on, whether or not the pension had started. For the\n  statutory share the survivor''s own income of the previous month above\n  the allowance is offset at the given rate; the survivor''s pension\n  itself does not count as own income.\n- Life insurance items gain `deathBenefit`: paid tax-free at death before\n  maturity (default the guaranteed payout), the contract ends; a running\n  annuity dies with the person.\n- Living expenses are scaled by the expense factor; the spending curve\n  follows the survivor when the reference person has died.\n- The result carries `death` and a \"death\" marker among the milestones.\n  A death in the past or beyond the horizon is ignored.\n- Analysis: `survivorCheck` simulates the death at every age ahead and\n  names the worst one (earliest failure, else smallest remainder).\n\nAPI\n- `runSimulation` adds an \"Ohne Todesfall\" comparison whenever the\n  scenario names a death, and takes `survivorFor` for the age check.\n- Scenario and item normalisation for the new fields; older configs get\n  the defaults.\n\nFrontend\n- \"Hinterbliebene\" under the assumptions: who dies at which age, expense\n  factor, offset rate and allowance; a quick check strip per age with the\n  worst age marked, a click puts that death into the scenario.\n- Item dialog: survivor share on pensions, death benefit on life\n  insurances. Charts show the death marker and the comparison.\n\nAlso fixes two type gaps left by earlier rounds (`currentMonthlyPension`\nin the shared statement-values type, a test fixture).\n\nTests: death before and after leaving work and before and after the\npension start, income offset, death benefit and contract end, private\npension leaving nothing, ignored deaths; survivor check; API comparison\nand age check; scenario defaults. Fixtures invented.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TzUSmLtnpEakztrMexTZWZ\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d53e1ff3606739ba2b3d23c92f83e8b7d1e2d28f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/d53e1ff3606739ba2b3d23c92f83e8b7d1e2d28f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/b37962b59dfb60cdc41d734f8443042e69d4af7c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/b37962b59dfb60cdc41d734f8443042e69d4af7c","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKGIzNzk2MmI1OWRmYjYwY2RjNDFkNzM0Zjg0NDMwNDJlNjlkNGFmN2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/17e8cab1035d1254602541a4158f70f5623314ba","sha":"17e8cab1035d1254602541a4158f70f5623314ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/17e8cab1035d1254602541a4158f70f5623314ba"}],"sha":"b37962b59dfb60cdc41d734f8443042e69d4af7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/b37962b59dfb60cdc41d734f8443042e69d4af7c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/17e8cab1035d1254602541a4158f70f5623314ba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T18:51:50Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T18:51:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Forecast: health insurance after work — capital income, ceiling, pensioners'' split (#1381)\n\nThe salary is net, so the employee''s share of health insurance is already\ngone; what matters is what the household pays once work ends, and that\ndepends on whether the person qualifies for the pensioners'' insurance.\n\nEngine\n- Voluntarily insured: the contribution is assessed on every income of\n  the person (earned, pensions of any kind, rent, annuities), an equal\n  share of the household''s income, and last month''s capital income\n  (returns of the cash, depot and other pots, owned assets in full,\n  household assets in equal shares; a home''s appreciation is not\n  income). Capped at the contribution ceiling, never below the minimum\n  contribution. Before: own income only, no capital income, no ceiling.\n- Pensioners'' insurance (KVdR): the statutory pension carries half the\n  health rate plus the full care rate, a company pension the full rate;\n  private pensions and capital income are free. Before: the full rate on\n  every pension.\n- One-off payouts count for neither.\n- Scenario gains `healthInsurance.careRate` (0.036) and\n  `healthInsurance.maxMonthlyIncome` (5 512.50, indexed with inflation);\n  older configs get the defaults.\n\nFrontend\n- New health-insurance items start with no extra premium while employed;\n  the field is described as an extra premium on top of the net salary.\n- Scenario fields for the care share and the ceiling; dialog and item\n  summary explain the modes.\n- The statement reader proposes premiums only where one is paid as such\n  (extra premium, private tariffs).\n\nTests: voluntary base with capital income, household share and ceiling;\npensioners'' split across statutory, company and private pensions;\nscenario defaults. Fixtures invented.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TzUSmLtnpEakztrMexTZWZ\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a8d55fcf083c8859c26db693f5e248a45cc953e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/a8d55fcf083c8859c26db693f5e248a45cc953e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/17e8cab1035d1254602541a4158f70f5623314ba","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/17e8cab1035d1254602541a4158f70f5623314ba","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDE3ZThjYWIxMDM1ZDEyNTQ2MDI1NDFhNDE1OGY3MGY1NjIzMzE0YmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/839f966adf1f2194e910550d1f947674645a4605","sha":"839f966adf1f2194e910550d1f947674645a4605","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/839f966adf1f2194e910550d1f947674645a4605"}],"sha":"17e8cab1035d1254602541a4158f70f5623314ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/17e8cab1035d1254602541a4158f70f5623314ba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/839f966adf1f2194e910550d1f947674645a4605/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T12:43:02Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T12:43:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Search a long journey''s corridor in stretches geo will take (#1380)\n\nGeo searches one ellipse of at most 400 km, and a day''s drive can be\nlonger: adding a 424 km journey failed with geo''s HTTP 400 as an\ninternal error. corridorCandidates() now cuts the journey into\nstretches of at most 350 km, searches each in every region and keeps\na place found twice at its smaller detour. The in-memory geo client\nrefuses over-long corridors like the service does, so the split is\nunder test.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c031294eb184bb81b3447991edbbbf9d76de3403","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/c031294eb184bb81b3447991edbbbf9d76de3403"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/839f966adf1f2194e910550d1f947674645a4605","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/839f966adf1f2194e910550d1f947674645a4605","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDgzOWY5NjZhZGYxZjIxOTRlOTEwNTUwZDFmOTQ3Njc0NjQ1YTQ2MDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/d9d5c927071ded89df0baae3fcbba20650ed1be9","sha":"d9d5c927071ded89df0baae3fcbba20650ed1be9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/d9d5c927071ded89df0baae3fcbba20650ed1be9"}],"sha":"839f966adf1f2194e910550d1f947674645a4605","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/839f966adf1f2194e910550d1f947674645a4605"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/d9d5c927071ded89df0baae3fcbba20650ed1be9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T09:37:47Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T09:37:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Toolbar glass behind the list/map switch; say why the journeys are not offered (#1379)\n\n* Hide the toolbar''s shared glass behind the list/map switch\n\nOn iOS 26 the toolbar draws a glass capsule around each item and the\nsegmented picker draws its own, so the switch sat a few points inside\nits background on either side. TripPresentationToolbarItem hides the\nshared background where the modifier exists and is used by the pool\nand the ballot. Build number 1678.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* Say why the way there and home are not offered\n\nWith home set but the first or last city undated, the legs screen\nhid \"Anreise einfügen\" and \"Heimreise einfügen\" without a word. The\nsection footer now names the city that has no date and what to switch\non. Build number 1679.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* Close the German quotes in the undated-city hint\n\nAn ASCII quote ended the string literal early. Use the typographic\nclosing quote, as the rest of the copy does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d1b149e7228bca305857b69be57214241282844b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/d1b149e7228bca305857b69be57214241282844b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/d9d5c927071ded89df0baae3fcbba20650ed1be9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/d9d5c927071ded89df0baae3fcbba20650ed1be9","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKGQ5ZDVjOTI3MDcxZGVkODlkZjBiYWFlM2ZjYmJhMjA2NTBlZDFiZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/ded707fb509da527f5c69da70a1dcb5266273372","sha":"ded707fb509da527f5c69da70a1dcb5266273372","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/ded707fb509da527f5c69da70a1dcb5266273372"}],"sha":"d9d5c927071ded89df0baae3fcbba20650ed1be9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/d9d5c927071ded89df0baae3fcbba20650ed1be9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/ded707fb509da527f5c69da70a1dcb5266273372/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T08:24:29Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T08:24:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Corridor search across every crossed region; transport mode as a choice page (#1378)\n\n* Search the corridor in every region it crosses, not only the ends\n\nA journey from home to the coast passes through imported regions that\ncontain neither end; the corridor search only ran in the regions of the\ntwo ends, so the stretch between stayed empty. regionsIntersecting()\nin the region router returns every ready region whose bbox touches a\nbox, and corridor.ts pads the box of the ends by half the ellipse''s\nminor axis. Ends still come from the exact lookup; the middle is\nsearched wherever a rectangle overlaps.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n* Transport mode as a settings-style choice page\n\nThe \"Unterwegs\" row in every \"Wie?\" section is now a \"Fortbewegung\"\nrow that pushes a page of choices: one row per mode with its symbol\nand hint, a tick on the chosen one. The per-site hint rows under the\nold picker are gone; the page carries them. Build number 1677.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"70d165a3506989e12d485910d5441ab3cb53eeeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/70d165a3506989e12d485910d5441ab3cb53eeeb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/ded707fb509da527f5c69da70a1dcb5266273372","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/ded707fb509da527f5c69da70a1dcb5266273372","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKGRlZDcwN2ZiNTA5ZGE1MjdmNWM2OWRhNzBhMWRjYjUyNjYyNzMzNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/cc214abe5b094379b8bd79e5a211ccd49472a92d","sha":"cc214abe5b094379b8bd79e5a211ccd49472a92d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/cc214abe5b094379b8bd79e5a211ccd49472a92d"}],"sha":"ded707fb509da527f5c69da70a1dcb5266273372","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/ded707fb509da527f5c69da70a1dcb5266273372"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/cc214abe5b094379b8bd79e5a211ccd49472a92d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T07:48:51Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T07:48:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Tighter frame around the transaction cards on a phone (#1377)\n\nThe cards on the transaction list sat inside 16px of page and carried\n16px of their own padding on top: on a 390px screen a third of the row\nwas frame. Two things give a little.\n\nThe phone gutter goes from 16px to 12px, for every page: enough for a\nfocus ring (4px reach) and a thumb''s margin, and the search field, the\nheadings and the cards stay on one edge, which a list-only tweak would\nhave broken. Above `md` the gutter is 24px as before.\n\nThe card''s own padding goes from 0.85rem/1rem to 0.65rem/0.75rem and the\ngap between cards from 0.6rem to 0.5rem.\n\nAlso in this change: the Excel import dialog''s file button lost the top\nof its focus ring — the dialog content scrolls and has no padding above\nits first child. The `.pick` row now keeps the ring''s reach at the top\nand takes it back on the other sides. It came in with the forecast work\nand had the two dialog stories red in the Storybook runner.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FyPMNxK4aSArGgayVvpqsc\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2a996b397845dfd7086f5b0eb0c79d4b517dd353","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/2a996b397845dfd7086f5b0eb0c79d4b517dd353"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/cc214abe5b094379b8bd79e5a211ccd49472a92d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/cc214abe5b094379b8bd79e5a211ccd49472a92d","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKGNjMjE0YWJlNWIwOTQzNzliOGJkNzllNWEyMTFjY2Q0OTQ3MmE5MmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/3615af8f8c4ef76581943bd39e3d6fe6564bab33","sha":"3615af8f8c4ef76581943bd39e3d6fe6564bab33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/3615af8f8c4ef76581943bd39e3d6fe6564bab33"}],"sha":"cc214abe5b094379b8bd79e5a211ccd49472a92d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/cc214abe5b094379b8bd79e5a211ccd49472a92d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/3615af8f8c4ef76581943bd39e3d6fe6564bab33/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T05:51:42Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T05:51:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Forecast: robustness, reverse calculation, and corrections from a calculation audit (#1376)\n\n* Forecast: sensitivity table, levers, stress test and reverse calculation\n\nTwo what-if questions on top of the simulation (#1339, #1340), all pure\nfunctions in finance/forecast-analysis.ts that only call simulate with a\nchanged input.\n\nRobustness (#1339):\n- Sensitivity table: earliest leave-work age of the chosen person over\n  return × inflation around the scenario''s rates (five by three cells).\n- Levers: how many years the earliest age moves when the return drops by\n  one point, inflation rises by one point, living expenses grow by 10 %,\n  or the depot loses 30 % in the year of leaving; the biggest is named.\n- Stress test: the scenario gains `stress.crashYear` / `crashSize`; the\n  depot loses that share at the start of the crash year, saved with the\n  scenario like every other assumption.\n\nReverse calculation (#1340): a target age per person; when it does not\nwork, bisection over each lever on its own gives the additional monthly\nsavings until leaving, the spending cut after leaving (share and monthly\namount), the required return on depot and other investments, and the\none-off amount today; \"not reachable\" when the bound does not suffice.\nWhen it works, the monthly buffer the household could spend on top.\n\nAPI: `runSimulation` takes `robustness` and `targetAge` for `earliestFor`\nand answers `sensitivity`, `levers` and `reverse`; the earliest age is\nnow searched up to 75 like the slider allows.\n\nFrontend: \"Wie robust ist das?\" panel and a target-age input in \"Wann\naufhören?\", crash controls under the assumptions, two new components\nwith stories; a click on a table cell adopts its rates.\n\nTests use invented households and amounts only.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TzUSmLtnpEakztrMexTZWZ\n\n* Forecast: corrections from the calculation audit\n\nA review of every calculation behind Finanzen › Prognose, written up in\n.claude/plans/prognose-rechenpruefung.md. What changes the numbers:\n\nEngine\n- Cash earns nothing unless an asset names a rate; the scenario''s return\n  is the return on investments. Interest on cash is taxed like other\n  capital income. (A Tagesgeld without a rate compounded at 4 % tax-free.)\n- Statutory pension: adjusted from today on, since the statement quotes\n  today''s pension value; company and private pensions stay nominal at\n  their start. New field `currentEntitlement` (the pension earned so\n  far): leaving work before the regular age lands proportionally between\n  it and the projection, then the deduction applies.\n- A statutory pension starts the month after the birthday month (§ 99\n  SGB VI), in the birthday month for those born on the first; the same\n  month counts for the deduction.\n- A lump sum is paid only when its amount is above zero; otherwise the\n  annuity runs.\n- Sensitivity and levers move every investment''s own return by the same\n  step, not only the scenario default.\n- Result carries `startMonth` so a partial first year can be labelled.\n\nMapping, import, statements\n- One-off amounts of the current year start in the current month\n  (January lay before the simulation start and was never booked).\n- A life insurance whose maturity year has passed is no longer imported\n  (it paid out again at the start); the current year is flagged.\n- Imported statutory pensions are bound to the person''s pension\n  milestone with regular age and the usual deduction, so the sliders\n  and the deduction reach them.\n- A rate cell of \"1\" means 1 %; regular retirement age of new persons by\n  birth year; giro and cash accounts offered as asset items; a negative\n  balance is read as 0.\n- Statement reader: proposals for health insurance premiums, a premium\n  of zero is a value, an expense without rhythm counts as monthly,\n  \"neuer Beitrag … jährlich\" is not a monthly premium, and the earned\n  entitlement of a statutory statement is read and proposed.\n\nFrontend\n- The health-insurance line in the cash-flow chart was stacked on top\n  of total expenses; both lines now have their own stack.\n- Leave age from a date milestone comes from the engine''s resolved age;\n  current age from the full birth date.\n- Minimum-wealth line deflated per year and pots stacked liquid-first;\n  bridge deflation never before the start year; percent fields keep\n  three decimals; texts and labels corrected; first chart year marked\n  as partial; item dialog gains the entitlement field and hints on when\n  growth and adjustment apply.\n\nTests: engine (cash default, statutory timing, adjustment from today,\nentitlement interpolation, zero lump sum), analysis (explicit returns),\nimport (current-year one-off), API (account suggestions). All fixtures\ninvented.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TzUSmLtnpEakztrMexTZWZ\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1b60006a60a06435aee805a6a49b019a5c95262e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/1b60006a60a06435aee805a6a49b019a5c95262e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/3615af8f8c4ef76581943bd39e3d6fe6564bab33","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/3615af8f8c4ef76581943bd39e3d6fe6564bab33","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDM2MTVhZjhmOGM0ZWY3NjU4MTk0M2JkMzllM2Q2ZmU2NTY0YmFiMzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/b71d72b8cd2bad0d264db7068e7ee76fd868d6ae","sha":"b71d72b8cd2bad0d264db7068e7ee76fd868d6ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/b71d72b8cd2bad0d264db7068e7ee76fd868d6ae"}],"sha":"3615af8f8c4ef76581943bd39e3d6fe6564bab33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/3615af8f8c4ef76581943bd39e3d6fe6564bab33"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/b71d72b8cd2bad0d264db7068e7ee76fd868d6ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T20:14:20Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T20:14:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Inline transport-mode picker and one action block on the spot detail (#1375)\n\nThe \"Unterwegs\" picker (foot, bike, transit, car) was a Form menu picker\nwhose Label rows left only the symbol tappable on iOS 17/18. It is now\none shared TripTransportModePicker drawn inline, used on all five\nscreens that ask.\n\nTripSpotActionSections draws a spot''s actions as one section instead of\none per action; each action''s explanatory sentence moves from the\nsection footer into its row as a caption.\n\nBuild number 1676.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSkPd5rVvryfTqbafCwo2n\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"359291f68108fcfd5ddcf60d1414da086c06dbf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/359291f68108fcfd5ddcf60d1414da086c06dbf4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/b71d72b8cd2bad0d264db7068e7ee76fd868d6ae","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/b71d72b8cd2bad0d264db7068e7ee76fd868d6ae","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKGI3MWQ3MmI4Y2QyYmFkMGQyNjRkYjcwNjhlN2VlNzZmZDg2OGQ2YWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/22e946d6b4acd6708964b7db4c612fade36f2ecb","sha":"22e946d6b4acd6708964b7db4c612fade36f2ecb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/22e946d6b4acd6708964b7db4c612fade36f2ecb"}],"sha":"b71d72b8cd2bad0d264db7068e7ee76fd868d6ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/b71d72b8cd2bad0d264db7068e7ee76fd868d6ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/22e946d6b4acd6708964b7db4c612fade36f2ecb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T19:35:39Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T19:35:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Forecast: premium invoices and policies as document kinds; chart tooltip beside the pointer (#1374)\n\n* Forecast: premium invoices and policies as kinds of linked documents\n\nProperty and supplementary insurances send no statements; their figures\ncome from the premium invoice (Beitrags-/Prämienrechnung) and the policy\n(Versicherungsschein or a Nachtrag).\n\n- Two new document kinds, premium_invoice and policy (migration 0218\n  widens the check). Recognised by the documents module''s type\n  (rechnung / vertrag), by wording, or by the language model; a declined\n  increase and a Standmitteilung keep precedence. The user can set them\n  in the dialog like any other kind.\n- Both count as documents with values, like a statement, so their premium\n  becomes a proposal for the item.\n- Premiums written as \"Jahresprämie\", \"Prämie jährlich\" or \"Monatsprämie\"\n  are read as well.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TzUSmLtnpEakztrMexTZWZ\n\n* Forecast charts: tooltip lists only non-zero values and opens beside the pointer\n\n- The tooltip of the forecast charts leaves out series that are zero in\n  the hovered year (below half a euro), so a year shows only the sources\n  it actually has.\n- A custom \"aside\" positioner hangs the tooltip from the top of the plot,\n  opening to the right of the pointer on the left half and to the left on\n  the right half, so the column pointed at stays visible.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TzUSmLtnpEakztrMexTZWZ\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"26bf1f75b3fa130f879d0b7fbdb56d0e176302bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/26bf1f75b3fa130f879d0b7fbdb56d0e176302bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/22e946d6b4acd6708964b7db4c612fade36f2ecb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/22e946d6b4acd6708964b7db4c612fade36f2ecb","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDIyZTk0NmQ2YjRhY2Q2NzA4OTY0YjdkYjRjNjEyZmFkZTM2ZjJlY2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/0a308bf4ba14cbc76b985ee6669012defaa60b96","sha":"0a308bf4ba14cbc76b985ee6669012defaa60b96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/0a308bf4ba14cbc76b985ee6669012defaa60b96"}],"sha":"22e946d6b4acd6708964b7db4c612fade36f2ecb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/22e946d6b4acd6708964b7db4c612fade36f2ecb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2434239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67","id":2434239,"login":"as19git67","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzQyMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/as19git67","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/0a308bf4ba14cbc76b985ee6669012defaa60b96/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T15:37:34Z","email":"anton@schegg.de","name":"as19git67"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T15:37:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Finish stage 6: every focus ring shows, every dialog has a size (#1372)\n\nThe last two gaps against #1281''s definition of done.\n\nTen `:focus-visible` rules turned the outline off and put a background\ntint in its place. A tint is what hover looks like; a keyboard user\ntabbing onto one of these tiles, menu items or badges had nothing that\nsaid \"you are here\". The declaration goes and the global ring shows; the\ntint stays as the hover it always was. The five `outline: none` left all\ndraw the ring themselves in the same rule.\n\nFive dialogs had no size class: the album creation form and the four\nbatch dialogs behind the document basket, which PrimeVue sized to their\ncontent. Confirmation-shaped ones take `dialog-sm`, forms `dialog-md`.\nThe photo editor stays the one deliberate full-screen exception.\n\nCLAUDE.md now lists the unification as implemented and points at the\nrule sections it left behind rather than at an active plan.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FyPMNxK4aSArGgayVvpqsc\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0936892a544eca55c62c55fa194ac7ca9d1d0ea3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/trees/0936892a544eca55c62c55fa194ac7ca9d1d0ea3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/git/commits/0a308bf4ba14cbc76b985ee6669012defaa60b96","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/0a308bf4ba14cbc76b985ee6669012defaa60b96","node_id":"C_kwDORl_MVtoAKDBhMzA4YmY0YmExNGNiYzc2Yjk4NWVlNjY2OTAxMmRlZmFhNjBiOTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/as19git67/fk-encore/commit/ed9e15f4a6647751c1040ab999cee545a3fdf368","sha":"ed9e15f4a6647751c1040ab999cee545a3fdf368","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/ed9e15f4a6647751c1040ab999cee545a3fdf368"}],"sha":"0a308bf4ba14cbc76b985ee6669012defaa60b96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits/0a308bf4ba14cbc76b985ee6669012defaa60b96"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/as19git67/fk-encore/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=be24ae58584723bada8441450932a9e7f0daea74&since=2025-03-3