s://api.github.com/users/Avien/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Avien","id":4569044,"login":"Avien","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NjkwNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Avien/users-portal/commits/a3c8ffa0b2089dea29e35065b3c502c5f71db0de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T11:34:52Z","email":"avi.engelstein@gmail.com","name":"Avi Engelshtein"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T11:34:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(roadmap): mark live-order feedback done, add AI-scan readiness tracking (#26)\n\nLive WebSocket order visual feedback shipped across several PRs this cycle\n(row highlight, unseen-order badges, smart live-follow, stable viewport\nheight, plus an Angular production-only CSS animation-scoping fix) but the\nroadmap still listed it as open — marks it Done with what actually landed.\n\nRenames \"Portfolio / reviewer README polish\" to \"Portfolio / reviewer /\nAI-scan readiness\" and expands it: the goal is making the repo legible to\nboth human reviewers and automated/LLM-based GitHub scanners, never keyword\nstuffing or claims that don''t trace to real code/tests/docs. Adds tracking\nfor terminology appearing as real prose (not only diagrams), consistent\nterminology across README and deep dives, self-contained deep-dive\nsummaries for search retrieval, repo topics for architecture concepts, and\nevaluating whether a small AGENTS.md adds anything beyond CLAUDE.md.\n\nRoadmap-only - no README/docs implementation in this commit.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a459760862ae7c51e8dbd246ee910e7a61e65d94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Avien/users-portal/git/trees/a459760862ae7c51e8dbd246ee910e7a61e65d94"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Avien/users-portal/git/commits/a3c8ffa0b2089dea29e35065b3c502c5f71db0de","verification":{"payload":"tree a459760862ae7c51e8dbd246ee910e7a61e65d94\nparent 0744e5add2126016023f2c93b6e286347a476180\nauthor Avi Engelshtein <avi.engelstein@gmail.com> 1788003292 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788003292 +0300\n\ndocs(roadmap): mark live-order feedback done, add AI-scan readiness tracking (#26)\n\nLive WebSocket order visual feedback shipped across several PRs this cycle\n(row highlight, unseen-order badges, smart live-follow, stable viewport\nheight, plus an Angular production-only CSS animation-scoping fix) but the\nroadmap still listed it as open — marks it Done with what actually landed.\n\nRenames \"Portfolio / reviewer README polish\" to \"Portfolio / reviewer /\nAI-scan readiness\" and expands it: the goal is making the repo legible to\nboth human reviewers and automated/LLM-based GitHub scanners, never keyword\nstuffing or claims that don''t trace to real code/tests/docs. Adds tracking\nfor terminology appearing as real prose (not only diagrams), consistent\nterminology across README and deep dives, self-contained deep-dive\nsummaries for search retrieval, repo topics for architecture concepts, and\nevaluating whether a small AGENTS.md adds anything beyond CLAUDE.md.\n\nRoadmap-only - no README/docs implementation in this commit.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqksPcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZOsQABS7EwzzVNWx67FN9L5RWJ5f\nQK0QRGesYOX4dhHdBsm5vE5PdlXRDtpf+3e/MKElctWc2d