 architecture, design, and review were \"led\nby me throughout,\" implying continuous personal ownership of every design\ndecision and code review. That''s no longer an accurate description of how\nthis repository is developed.\n\nRewrites it to reflect the actual split: the core architecture, domain\nboundaries, shared cross-framework contracts, and framework-isolation\nrules were established up front and are encoded durably in CLAUDE.md, Nx\nmodule-boundary tags, generators, and automated review tooling - not\ncarried only as an ongoing personal review claim. Implementation itself is\nincreasingly delegated to AI agents, primarily Claude Code, with day-to-day\nwork happening more at the level of feature intent, system behavior,\nconstraints, and review direction.\n\nAlso adds a CLAUDE.md row to the tooling table, corrects the slash-command\ndescription (they''re explicitly invoked, not inferred from freeform\nchat), replaces the closing quote with the project''s actual open question\n(\"how far can implementation be delegated to autonomous agents while\nstill preserving architectural consistency, maintainability, and\ntechnical quality?\"), and adds one sentence distinguishing this\ndevelopment-workflow section from the separately-described LLM Business\nAgent product feature.\n\nVerified every referenced artifact before writing: .claude/commands/*.md,\nthe feature-domain generator''s file count, tools/agent.mjs, and\ntools/pr-review-agent.mjs (confirmed it loads CLAUDE.md verbatim as its\nsystem prompt).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: tighten agentic AI development narrative\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a8cf4bb5b7398d5fcd6124d2f1fcfa3baee2da45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Avien/users-portal/git/trees/a8cf4bb5b7398d5fcd6124d2f1fcfa3baee2da45"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Avien/users-portal/git/commits/555ecc798f9160e9b9d27c71fa5a7a73e4a9c6f6","verifica