Avien/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Avien/users-portal/commits/ab4df520bc13a69434d9c0a3dd7d06f5522b05f3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T10:06:26Z","email":"avi.engelstein@gmail.com","name":"Avi Engelshtein"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T10:06:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(railway): pause synthetic order generation when no clients connected (#21)\n\nThe recurring process-level generator (tools/mock-orders-ws-server.mjs)\npreviously emitted a synthetic order every 5-15s regardless of connected\nclient count, creating meaningless background activity, advancing order\nIDs with nobody watching, and filling Railway logs even with zero\nvisitors. It now checks wss.clients.size on each tick: with zero clients\nit still reschedules (generation self-resumes on reconnect) but does not\ncreate an order, allocate an id, mutate the canonical store, or log —\npreserving the single process-level scheduler property (10 connected\nclients still see exactly one event stream, not 10x the rate).\n\nThe one-time startup burst is now scoped to viewing sessions instead of\nthe whole process lifetime: a 0->1 connected-clients transition schedules\na fresh 3-order demo burst, a second client joining an already-active\nsession does not, and the guard (isBurstInFlight) resets only once the\nburst''s own final timer fires - never merely because clients disconnected.\nThat distinction matters: an earlier version reset the guard on disconnect\ninstead, which let a client that dropped before its burst finished, and\nwas replaced by a new one before the burst completed, schedule a second,\noverlapping burst (6 interleaved orders instead of a clean 3). An\nalready-started burst is still allowed to finish even if its triggering\nclient disconnects; only new *recurring* orders are held back while the\nservice has zero connected clients.\n\nAlso replaces the plain connect/disconnect console logs with structured\nJSON (message, activeClients, isExcludedClient) suitable for Railway log\nfiltering. The connecting client''s IP (read from Railway''s X-Real-IP\nforwarded header, with a local-dev fallback to the raw socket address) is\nused only to compute isExcludedClient and is deliberately never written\nto the log line itself - the one declared purpose (telling the deploy\nowner''s own traffic apart from real visitors) is fully served by that\nboolean, with no operational need to persist raw IPs as PII in Railway''s\nlogs. An optional DEMO_LOG_EXCLUDED_IPS env var (comma-separated IPs, set\nmanually in Railway - never committed here) drives that classification\nonly; it never gates access or changes order-generation behavior for any\nIP.\n\nVerified live against a real local process: zero clients for 20s produces\nno emit logs at all; connect-A/disconnect/connect-B before 2.5s produces\nexactly 3 orders (not 6, confirming the overlap fix); DEMO_LOG_EXCLUDED_IPS\ncorrectly tags a matching connection without altering its order\ngeneration, and clientIp never appears in a logged line.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"874985198834b11ac330a2f1b274d724429e1e03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Avien/users-portal/git/trees/874985198834b11ac330a2f1b274d724429e1e03"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Avien/users-portal/git/commits/ab4df520bc13a69434d9c0a3dd7d06f5522b05f3","verification":{"payload":"tree 874985198834b11ac330a2f1b274d724429e1e03\nparent 31efb07b3dcf022c65dfd7018d106aa2094edf1c\nauthor Avi Engelshtein <avi.engelstein@gmail.com> 1787738786 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787738786 +0300\n\nfeat(railway): pause synthetic order generation when no clients connected (#21)\n\nThe recurring process-level generator (tools/mock-orders-ws-server.mjs)\npreviously emitted a synthetic order every 5-15s regardless of connected\nclient count, creating meaningless background activity, advancing order\nIDs with nobody watching, and filling Railway logs even with zero\nvisitors. It now checks wss.clients.size on each tick: with zero clients\nit still reschedules (generation self-resumes on reconnect) but does not\ncreate an order, allocate an id, mutate the canonical store, or log —\npreserving the single process-level scheduler property (10 connected\nclients still see exactly one event stream, not 10x the rate).\n\nThe one-time startup burst is now scoped to viewing sessions instead of\nthe whole process lifetime: a 0->1 connected-clients transition schedules\na fresh 3-order demo burst, a second client joining an already-active\nsession does not, and the guard (isBurstInFlight) resets only once the\nburst''s own final timer fires - never merely because clients disconnected.\nThat distinction matters: an earlier version reset the guard on disconnect\ninstead, which let a client that dropped before its burst finished, and\nwas replaced by a new one before the burst completed, schedule a second,\noverlapping burst (6 interleaved orders instead of a clean 3). An\nalready-started burst is still allowed to finish even if its triggering\nclient disconnects; only new *recurring* orders are held back while the\nservice has zero connected clients.\n\nAlso replaces the plain connect/disconnect console logs with structured\nJSON (message, activeClients, isExcludedClient) suitable for Railway log\nfiltering. The connecting client''s IP (read from Railway''s X-Real-IP\nforwarded header, with a local-dev fallback to the raw socket address) is\nused only to compute isExcludedClient and is deliberately never written\nto the log line itself - the one declared purpose (telling the deploy\nowner''s own traffic apart from real visitors) is fully served by that\nboolean, with no operational need to persist raw IPs as PII in Railway''s\nlogs. An optional DEMO_LOG_EXCLUDED_IPS env var (comma-separated IPs, set\nmanually in Railway - never committed here) drives that classification\nonly; it never gates access or changes order-generation behavior for any\nIP.\n\nVerified live against a real local process: zero clients for 20s produces\nno emit logs at all; connect-A/disconnect/connect-B before 2.5s produces\nexactly 3 orders (not 6, confirming the overlap fix); DEMO_LOG_EXCLUDED_IPS\ncorrectly tags a matching connection without altering its order\ngeneration, and clientIp never appears in a logged line.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjrqiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAESsQAD/UYiJ9XYD8LMODLWuhUGTR\nZhLVVGUbbt+I/NoV0VATjj+8wO6XxLGL5O9pTNUQXAK+7ujOOu7Zef4vsG23G/de\nmr8DxJJP4HdUI5QaDjnp9WBZh53sKf5jvj+FTWOUws26Vr57HQfdf/L/hT46JAga\n4O6PJ37/ZQIiuzhF8oa7loZRe1cqUnN6mNcsatyM5JJNpZ98eKwTi5tW948nAUnA\nfMyf/iVeFB7TNHmEhANsJbPWRYlyFhXALsHqiiQqZC1rN6pZeSw0T7dx+CtfizKI\nHL4S/a0iwEwqYZmuT0muILVYBlKd8238AMgHgniUjSkR4RgOSWiZL6SuJ96dNt99\n1M7sQAoh0UAMfdalI8nPmbsqyozwzqpd49rlTmVgCfuPr+1TUmsYFMq66Ojuzbu8\nVA0hS/o2WaoL4nXu72sKKap0BxlpOEdas4Buhpuq63VjuIsOEUSnEcOP7fK5P+bC\nI/KuYJyOhGRdoUtmQLv6ZmkALhwJ07vahhkoAPCaTrIY3AoKlEpmWYxfXJpRSSu+\nTuZVzvROEkgpFTa/sPP6VQisZhEceJEfhOAH/cf2GrV4aGU5DrZQcY7UMh+F7LPO\nLQesYKTGWwYpC1aBtefjsJKBQy5MeLl/s+6Gtm3d31fA9OfV2Jlx6CtfnleYLTBw\n0KM76/YFcimQI2ZfQ0hD\n=HIFu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T10:06:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Avien/users-portal/commit/ab4df520bc13a69434d9c0a3dd7d06f5522b05f3","node_id":"C_kwDORmGsMdoAKGFiNGRmNTIwYmMxM2E2OTQzNGQ5YzBhM2RkN2QwNmY1NTIyYjA1ZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Avien/users-portal/commit/31efb07b3dcf022c65dfd7018d106aa2094edf1c","sha":"31efb07b3dcf022c65dfd7018d106aa2094edf1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Avien/users-portal/commits/31efb07b3dcf022c65dfd7018d106aa2094edf1c"}],"sha":"ab4df520bc13a69434d9c0a3dd7d06f5522b05f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Avien/users-portal/commits/ab4df520bc13a69434d9c0a3dd7d06f5522b05f3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4569044?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Avien","id":4569044,"login":"Avien","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NjkwNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Avien/users-portal/commits/31efb07b3dcf022c65dfd7018d106aa2094edf1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:31:05Z","email":"avi.engelstein@gmail.com","name":"Avi Engelshtein"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:31:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(angular): scope orders-row-pulse animation reference outside @media (#20)\n\nAngular''s production CSS optimizer scopes @keyframes names per component\n(orders-row-pulse -> _ngcontent-xxx_orders-row-pulse) but only rewrites\n`animation` references to that scoped name in top-level rules. The rule\nwas nested inside @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference), so the\nrewrite was skipped and the animation silently referenced a keyframes\nname that no longer existed in production — the row never highlighted.\n`ng serve` doesn''t run this optimization pass, so it looked correct in\ndev. Vue and React use different, non-AST-based scoping mechanisms and\nwere never affected.\n\nMoves the animation declaration to the top level (unconditional) and\nturns prefers-reduced-motion into an override (animation: none + static\nbackground) instead, matching the already-correct .spinner animation\nelsewhere in the app. Verified against a real local production build\nserved against the live Railway backend.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1fcf053e22f294498eae9f475f820f8e920fc93f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Avien/users-portal/git/trees/1fcf053e22f294498eae9f475f820f8e920fc93f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Avien/users-portal/git/commits/31efb07b3dcf022c65dfd7018d106aa2094edf1c","verification":{"payload":"tree 1fcf053e22f294498eae9f475f820f8e920fc93f\nparent 3e5370c34e2f1605d9ddbe3aaaa997a6159dd8f1\nauthor Avi Engelshtein <avi.engelstein@gmail.com> 1787671865 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787671865 +0300\n\nfix(angular): scope orders-row-pulse animation reference outside @media (#20)\n\nAngular''s production CSS optimizer scopes @keyframes names per component\n(orders-row-pulse -> _ngcontent-xxx_orders-row-pulse) but only rewrites\n`animation` references to that scoped name in top-level rules. The rule\nwas nested inside @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference), so the\nrewrite was skipped and the animation silently referenced a keyframes\nname that no longer existed in production — the row never highlighted.\n`ng serve` doesn''t run this optimization pass, so it looked correct in\ndev. Vue and React use different, non-AST-based scoping mechanisms and\nwere never affected.\n\nMoves the animation declaration to the top level (unconditional) and\nturns prefers-reduced-motion into an override (animation: none + static\nbackground) instead, matching the already-correct .spinner animation\nelsewhere in the app. Verified against a real local production build\nserved against the live Railway backend.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbU5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADN0QAG4g5fZFNwU8VLzU1gqyfaSM\nHfxTNkvz/PDjxPzSSJpkrT+Is/OsWx50rYjClUN3MRF8lE+KxIxuEVbq3DwiEpc6\naPOwr0A52U6f/ZF5lSgG5L0NOw2bkh/6udeEHwhQlct+dhEtxDUuJQYvh2xUtyk0\nd8d3qcew2F+GGzvo3SSLpborHSV2H1TuAPcs8eR7Kc4qVusPQqx5h1y0HdGCQto6\nR9JKU0WjQmIURJYbQLyIfH8YaETVqMDRe2FO7rwHXcUJlK+9haGsDNv6hL7Za5PM\n6DhcO9ef0+QNP08gFEyrwadbSpZAK/5kH86lWnOw7RT8tgvs1Emrs/Snt7rIqsgl\nAeJV7uIVhCFfkt1rKLv73k4qBOrrHMniQVnmJFPjzLzuIZmRG32ZNadmq1Or8XGU\nr4rRCLoUSUUoT6vUqenCGlZkhshj3iVYhS+sFAgxaLa8W58XAP2cc4+bjVD03/8L\nybI4BieaKi6AvL+INyY/8qsmQlh8FbkgH7cpF1N7DRcOhenUsVByhvgeTTYEld4I\nbgYf6zHBZ8nOaYsGumutOlkJ8ndcpCFMxfO7DgLmrQPVNQdUGQD70NQxSOm6TGMP\nlQSnZTArnCEEwpRskxapY9Gjb8ER/+5RwFIcq5gMnd1Qtu9qlDrKdYvI