:"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Avien/users-portal/commit/e029ee00ab6169347136a62c7eb05256c57772c2","node_id":"C_kwDORmGsMdoAKGUwMjllZTAwYWI2MTY5MzQ3MTM2YTYyYzdlYjA1MjU2YzU3NzcyYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Avien/users-portal/commit/8f5521db9b0c5f50efc1772cb313881fe27029dc","sha":"8f5521db9b0c5f50efc1772cb313881fe27029dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Avien/users-portal/commits/8f5521db9b0c5f50efc1772cb313881fe27029dc"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Avien/users-portal/commit/79896df803e473e6d3154cbfa58b61b34c7458dd","sha":"79896df803e473e6d3154cbfa58b61b34c7458dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Avien/users-portal/commits/79896df803e473e6d3154cbfa58b61b34c7458dd"}],"sha":"e029ee00ab6169347136a62c7eb05256c57772c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Avien/users-portal/commits/e029ee00ab6169347136a62c7eb05256c57772c2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4569044?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Avien","id":4569044,"login":"Avien","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NjkwNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Avien/users-portal/commits/79896df803e473e6d3154cbfa58b61b34c7458dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T12:23:22Z","email":"avi.engelstein@gmail.com","name":"mymac"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T12:23:22Z","email":"avi.engelstein@gmail.com","name":"mymac"},"message":"feat(business-agent-widget): Phase 2 — <business-agent-widget> Web Component\n\nAdds libs/business-agent-widget: a hand-rolled, framework-free Web\nComponent (Shadow DOM, attribute-driven \"endpoint\" config defaulting to\n/api/business-agent, CustomEvent output) that drops into any of the three\napps or the no-build portal-shell via a plain <script type=\"module\">.\nOwns only the prompt input, loading/error/result presentation, and the\nfetch call — no business logic, no tool definitions, no agent-loop code\n(that stays server-side in tools/business-agent-server.ts).\n\nPublic contract (business-agent-widget.events.ts, exported via index.ts\nfor Angular/React/Vue to consume in Phase 3):\n- BUSINESS_AGENT_ANSWER_EVENT / BUSINESS_AGENT_ERROR_EVENT constants\n  (DOM event names unchanged: ''agent:answer'' / ''agent:error'')\n- AgentAnswerEventDetail / AgentErrorEventDetail typed detail shapes\n- AgentAnswerEvent / AgentErrorEvent CustomEvent<T> aliases\n\nHardening applied before merge:\n- Full response-contract validation (answer: string, trace: array,\n  turns: number) via an isAgentResponse type guard, not just an\n  answer-only check — routes any violation through the existing\n  malformed-response/error path. No runtime schema dependency added.\n- Accessible name on the prompt input (aria-label)\n- Removed observedAttributes (dead — no attributeChangedCallback ever\n  used it; endpoint is read live via a getter)\n- Safe handling of non-Error values thrown/rejected during fetch, via a\n  toErrorMessage helper, instead of an unsafe `as Error` cast\n\ntools/business-agent-server.ts: added minimal CORS (wildcard origin,\nOPTIONS preflight) — required for the widget''s configurable endpoint to\nactually work cross-origin against the port-8787 dev server from any of\nthe app ports (4000/4200/4201/4202).\n\nReal Vite lib-mode build (nx build business-agent-widget) produces a\nsingle dependency-free ~3.7 kB ES module. Verified live in a real\nbrowser via a throwaway demo page: Shadow DOM renders, cross-origin\nfetch succeeds under the new CORS headers, real multi-tool agent answers\nrender as text, and agent:answer/agent:error fire with the documented\npayload shape.\n\n15 focused tests (vitest + jsdom, wired through the standard\n`nx test business-agent-widget`): endpoint default/override, loading\nstate, exact fetch call shape, success event + text-only rendering (XSS\nregression), 4 parameterized malformed-response contract violations,\nnon-OK server response, and both Error and non-Error rejection paths.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ef77f7cc83e98e8b033d56b8c3121b65f1828db2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Avien/users-portal/git/trees/ef77f7cc83e98e8b033d56b8c3121b65f1828db2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Avien/users-portal/git/commits/79896df803e473e6d3154cbfa58b61b34c7458dd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4569044?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Avien","id":4569044,"login":"Avien","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NjkwNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avien/starred{/owner}{/repo}","sub